PVD("cambodia_ndp_2024-2028",{"docs":["","CMB NDP 2024 2028 unofficial translation"],"s":{"1":[[1,"30","3","Disaster Management Coordination and Rapid Response Mechanism","With the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDM) as its secretariat, the Royal Government has implemented various activities to manage disasters through several legal instruments.",""],[1,"30","3","Water Conservation and Flood Preparedness Measures","The government has also issued four guiding circulars related to water conservation to prepare for and mitigate the risks caused by climate change, measures to cope with floods as the Mekong River rises, continued flood response measures, actions to conserve water to prevent damage to crops and for general use, the National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2019-2023, a national emergency preparedness plan, and emergency preparedness plans for all 25 capital cities and provinces.",""],[1,"30","3","Gender Mainstreaming in Disaster Risk Reduction","Furthermore, the government has adopted a strategic plan to mainstream gender into disaster management at the national and sub-national levels, enhance women's capacity in community-based disaster risk reduction programs, and integrate gender into climate change adaptation.",""],[1,"58","4","Armed Forces Civil Support and Disaster Response","Continue to strengthen the longstanding tradition of engagement between the armed forces and the people, particularly through interventions during natural disasters, the conduction of humanitarian operations, support agricultural productivity, contribute to construct physical infrastructure development, and participate in environmental and natural resource protection efforts",""],[1,"116","2","Disaster Risk Awareness and Information Systems Strengthening","Increase awareness of disaster risk management and reduction by expanding public and stakeholder knowledge of disaster risks, improving the quality and coverage of disaster information management systems, and advancing multi-hazard risk assessment",""],[1,"116","3","Disaster Risk Management Governance Strengthening","Strengthen governance for disaster risk management by enhancing legal frameworks, policies, normative legal documents, institutional arrangements, and budgeting for disaster risk management and reduction, integrating and aligning disaster risk reduction with sustainable development goals and climate change adaptation, mainstreaming disaster risk reduction across sectors, implementing disaster risk management programs, providing technical support and appropriate financing, and improving mechanisms for financial preparedness",""],[1,"116","4","Disaster Risk Reduction Investment Scale-Up","Scale up investment in disaster risk reduction for resilience by increasing the resilience of construction practices and infrastructure standards, strengthening the service delivery capacity of social service agencies including social protection and safety nets, and promoting participation by the private sector and businesses in climate and disaster resilience",""],[1,"116","5","Disaster Preparedness and Risk Management Strengthening","Enhance preparedness for disasters to ensure effective response, recovery, stabilization, and reconstruction by improving multi-hazard early warning systems, strengthening disaster response and recovery capacity, increasing readiness for public health emergencies and social protection responses, building officials' capacity in disaster risk management and reduction, and improving the overall effectiveness of disaster risk management.",""]],"2":[[1,"81","3","National Food System Strengthening for Food Security and Nutrition","and to strengthen food system that can support food security and nutrition for all people.",""],[1,"81","4","Resilient and Inclusive Food System Strengthening","including strengthening food system that is robust, smart, resilient, and inclusive",""],[1,"82","11","National Food Fortification Strategy Development and Expansion","Continue developing the First National Strategy on Food Fortification in Cambodia, 2025- 2028, to guide the strengthening and expansion of food fortification and the prevention and management of micronutrient deficiencies, through comprehensive technical guidelines on fortification, promotion and enforcement of relevant laws and normative legal documents to ensure the quality and safety of fortified foods, and nationwide public awareness on the importance of consuming fortified foods.",""],[1,"83","6","Strategic Food Reserve Management and Agricultural Commercialization Support","Continue contributing to the management and maintenance of the Royal Government's strategic food reserve, and strengthen commercialization of rice and other high-potential agricultural products for export by increasing paddy and rice production, upgrading quality across the paddy-rice value chain, and diversifying markets for rice and other agricultural products in line with existing competitiveness and priority market demand.",""],[1,"83","7","Strategic Staples Price Stability Support","Continue supporting price stability for strategic staples in the domestic market by retailing to the public at affordable prices with assured quality and quantity to meet domestic consumption needs, and by contributing to the management of food imports and exports based on a nationwide food-balance approach.",""],[1,"84","1","Third National Food Security and Nutrition Strategy Implementation","Develop, disseminate, and implement the Third National Strategy on food security and nutrition, 2024-2028, and continue to implement and update the food systems roadmap for Cambodia's sustainable development 2030",""],[1,"84","1","Food Systems Roadmap Implementation and Update","continue to implement and update the food systems roadmap for Cambodia's sustainable development 2030",""],[1,"84","2","Food Security and Nutrition Coordination Capacity Building","Strengthen institutional development and build the capacity of capital and provincial coordination leadership teams for food security and nutrition to drive sector improvements, including piloting nutrition-sensitive WASH core working groups at the subnational level",""],[1,"84","3","Food Security and Nutrition Policy Research and Data Dissemination Initiative","Promote research to generate evidence for implementation and for updating food security and nutrition policies and strategies, share findings through media channels, and enhance innovative, digital public-private engagement to support data collection, storage, and dissemination",""],[1,"84","4","National Nutrition Advocacy and Food Systems Coordination Initiative","Lead the nutrition movement and represent Cambodia as a founding member of the Champions Network for Food Systems Transformation by advancing action across priority intervention areas, and by routinely organizing National Nutrition Day, essential Food Safety Day events, and multi-sectoral technical working group meetings to further strengthen the sector",""],[1,"84","5","Child Wasting Prevention and Reduction Action Plan","Update and implement the global action plan to prevent and reduce child wasting, and update and implement Cambodia's decision on nutrition for growth",""],[1,"84","6","Food Security and Nutrition Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop and apply key indicators to monitor and evaluate multi-sectoral technical work on food security and nutrition and prepare regular reports to the Royal Government.",""],[1,"84","7","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""]],"3":[[1,"32","1","Social Environmental Fund for Low-Carbon and Climate-Resilient Development","effective use of the Social Environmental Fund, aim to ensure economic development with low carbon emissions and resilience to climate change.",""],[1,"32","1","Green Technology Research and Data Compilation in Target Provinces","researching and compiling data on the use of green technology in agriculture, industry, and other sectors in target provinces.",""],[1,"32","1","Green Technology Assessment and Research Collaboration","The government is also analyzing and evaluating green technologies and collaborating with institutions on research that focuses on: 1) green transportation; 2) the use of nuclear energy for peaceful purposes, renewable energy, and clean energy; 3) the application of eco-friendly technology in special economic zones; 4) accelerating clean technology innovation and entrepreneurship in new businesses and small and medium-sized enterprises in Cambodia; and 5) assessing the potential of nature-based solutions and green infrastructure to enhance water security and increase resilience to floods and droughts in highland areas.",""],[1,"32","2","Sustainable Urban Development Strategic Plan","the government has launched the Sustainable Urban Development Strategic Plan 2020-2030 for seven target cities (Kep, Sihanoukville, Battambang, Siem Reap, Kampong Cham, Suong, and Bavet)",""],[1,"32","2","Sustainable Consumption and Production Roadmap","the Cambodia Sustainable Consumption and Production Roadmap 2022-2035",""],[1,"32","2","Green Buildings Research Dissemination","It has also disseminated research reports on the status of green buildings in Cambodia",""],[1,"32","2","Circular Economy Strategic and Action Plan","a strategic plan and action plan for the circular economy from 2021 to 2030",""],[1,"32","2","Climate Change and Carbon Neutrality Policy Instruments","It has also developed policies, agreements, conventions, UN frameworks, roadmaps, and development strategic plans related to climate change and carbon neutrality in Cambodia",""],[1,"32","2","Updated NDC and LTS4CN Implementation and Tracking System","as well as an implementation plan and tracking system for the Updated NDC and LTS4CN (NDC Tracking System)",""],[1,"123","2","Clean and Efficient Energy Policy Incentives","continuing to incentivize and encourage investment in affordable clean energy",""],[1,"123","2","Smart and Green Agricultural Policy","introducing a smart and green agricultural policy",""],[1,"123","2","Innovation Policy for Industrial Processes and Consumption","an innovation policy for industrial processes and consumption",""],[1,"123","2","Smart Cities and Green Transport Policy","a policy for smart cities and green transport",""],[1,"123","2","Integrated Waste Management Policy","a policy for management of solid, liquid, gas and dangerous wastes",""],[1,"123","2","Strengthened Environmental Impact Assessment for Domestic and Cross-Border Projects","effectively strengthening environmental impact assessment (EIA) for domestic and cross- border projects",""],[1,"123","6","Skills, Technology, and Environmental Research Development","Continuing to develop skills and technology knowledge, as well as carrying out scientific research on environment, green development, water security, reduction of greenhouse gas emissions, adaptation to climate change, and sustainable use of natural resources;",""],[1,"123","6","Public Awareness Booklets for Environment-Friendly Village and School Policies","and producing instruction booklets to promote public, school and monastery participations in the implementation of the policy for schools, monasteries, environment friendly, and the policy for \"safe village-commune-Sangkat,\" with good sanitation, beauty and good environment.",""],[1,"123","9","Delegation of Functions and Resources to Subnational Administrations","Delegate functions and resources to subnational administrations to strengthen accountability and ownership, ensuring the sustainability of natural resources and the environment",""],[1,"123","10","Public and Stakeholder Participation for National Cleanliness and Sustainability","Enhance public and stakeholder participation to advance cleanliness, greenness, and sustainability nationwide",""],[1,"124","1","Climate-Smart Investment Policy Dissemination","Disseminate policies and normative legal instruments to the private sector to promote climate-smart investment",""],[1,"124","3","Multi-Stakeholder Environment and Climate Cooperation","Strengthen cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions, development partners, civil society organizations, academic institutions, and the private sector on environment and climate change.","relevant ministries and institutions"]],"4":[[1,"3","2","National Strategic Development Plan Implementation","The Royal Government of Cambodia shall continue the implementation of the National Strategic Development Plan of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly.",""],[1,"4","3","Pentagonal Strategy for Growth, Employment, Equity, Efficiency, and Sustainability","the Royal Government of Cambodia under the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly has launched the Pentagonal Strategy for Growth, Employment, Equity, Efficiency, and Sustainability.",""],[1,"4","5","National Development Plan Coordination and Implementation Framework","It provides a shared reference and coordination tool to implement the Five Key Measures and the Pentagonal Strategy - phase I",""],[1,"4","5","Plan Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","it ensures that all stakeholders implement the plan with accountability and effectiveness through the integration of monitoring and evaluation mechanisms",""],[1,"5","1","Dynamic Stakeholder System for NSDP Implementation","I call on all ministries, government institutions, and stakeholders to join forces in a spirit of unity, proactivity, and innovation to implement this NSDP successfully.",""],[1,"9","2","National Strategic Development Plan","The NSDP serves as the primary policy instrument for operationalizing the Royal Government's comprehensive strategic framework for socio-economic development as articulated in the Pentagonal Strategy Phase I.",""],[1,"9","3","National Strategic Development Plan Resource Mobilization and Monitoring Framework","the National Strategic Development Plan (NSDP) of the Royal Government for the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly provides a comprehensive framework for prioritizing and mobilizing both domestic and international resources to support the implementation of measures, activities, programs, and projects.",""],[1,"9","3","National Strategic Development Plan Monitoring and Adaptive Prioritization System","It ensures that resource utilization is aligned with national priorities, establishes mechanisms for monitoring progress against defined indicators and targets, and serves as a basis for adjusting priorities and resource allocations based on evidence and emerging needs.",""],[1,"9","3","National Strategic Development Plan Accountability and Global Commitments Integration","The NSDP also strengthens accountability and integrates Cambodia's commitments to global development agendas.",""],[1,"10","1","Plan Implementation, Monitoring, and Evaluation Mechanism","It also establishes mechanisms for implementation, monitoring, evaluation, and the refinement of key performance indicators to ensure the effective execution of the Plan during the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly.",""],[1,"10","7","NSDP Implementation, Monitoring, Evaluation, and Risk Management Mechanism","Chapter 5 sets out the mechanisms for implementation, monitoring, evaluation, and risk management to ensure the effective execution of the NSDP under the Royal Government during the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly.",""],[1,"32","4","Implementation of the Pentagonal Strategy, Six Priority Policy Programs, and Five Key Measures","The Royal Government has promoted the implementation of the Pentagonal Strategy, the Six Priority Policy Programs, and the Five Key Measures, achieving significant progress and major milestones in 2024.",""],[1,"56","1","Pentagonal Strategy Phase 1","The Royal Government has launched the Pentagonal Strategy - phase 1 for growth, employment, equity, efficiency, and sustainability.",""],[1,"56","2","National Strategic Development Plan Alignment and Coordination Framework","This National Strategic Development Plan serves as a comprehensive economic and social development framework, carefully formulated in alignment with the directives of the Pentagonal Strategy.",""],[1,"56","2","Harmonization of Policy Programs, Priority Objectives, and Ministry Action Plans","Its purpose is to harmonize key policy programs and priority objectives of this strategy with the action plans, programs, and priority projects of relevant ministries-institutions responsible for implementation.",""],[1,"56","2","Implementation of Phase 1 National Development Goals","The Plan is designed to realize the national development goals set out in Phase 1 of the Pentagonal Strategy under the 7th Legislative term of the Royal Government.",""],[1,"56","3","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning for Priority Program Implementation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"60","13","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning for Priority Program Implementation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"117","3","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"120","5","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:","Ministries-institutions"],[1,"124","9","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning for Priority Programs","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"126","17","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning for Priority Digital Programs","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified",""],[1,"128","9","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning for Priority Programs","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"129","7","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"130","8","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation for NSDP Priority Actions","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"136","1","NSDP Implementation Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","This involves formulating and implementing detailed measures, specific action plans, and establishing institutional mechanisms to coordinate, monitor, and evaluate the NSDP's targeted objectives with clarity, thoroughness, and precision.",""],[1,"136","1","Ministry of Planning NSDP Lead Coordination Mandate","To this end, the Royal Government delegates responsibility to the Ministry of Planning to serve as the lead institution to guide and coordinate, monitor, and evaluate the execution of key priority policies, activities, and programs across ministries-institutions.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"136","1","Execution Leadership and Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanisms","To enhance the effectiveness of this implementation, the Royal Government has established mechanisms for promoting execution, leadership coordination, and monitoring and evaluation, as outlined below:",""],[1,"136","2","NSDP Coordination, Consolidation, Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","the Royal Government designates the Ministry of Planning as the lead agency to coordinate and consolidate progress, as well as to monitor, and evaluate the implementation of the NSDP, with full cooperation from all relevant ministries- institutions under the concept of \"Dynamics of Stakeholder System\".","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"136","2","Pentagonal Strategy Phase 1 Monitoring and Evaluation Committee","For the monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of the Pentagonal Strategy Phase 1, the Committee on Monitoring and Evaluation of the implementation of the Pentagonal Strategy Phase 1 (CME-PS1) measures results at the impact and outcome levels.",""],[1,"136","4","Dedicated Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanisms for NSDP Implementation","To ensure the effective and efficient implementation of the NSDP for the 7th Legislature, the Royal Government has put in place dedicated monitoring and evaluation mechanisms.",""],[1,"136","5","Annual NSDP Progress Reporting and M&E Coordination Framework","Within this monitoring and evaluation framework, ministries-institutions shall prepare annual progress reports on the implementation of the NSDP within their respective mandates and submit them to the Ministry of Planning.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","1","Progress Reporting and Evaluation Mechanism","and preparing comprehensive progress reports for submission to the Royal Government.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","1","Mid-Term and End-of-Term Evaluation System","the Ministry of Planning carries out mid-term and end-of-term evaluations assessing impacts, outcomes, and outputs, providing an in-depth analysis of achievements against the action plans and priority programs set out in the NSDP for the 7th Legislature.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","1","Evidence Use for Pentagonal Strategy Phase 2 Formulation","The findings from these evaluations will serve as key inputs for the formulation of the Pentagonal Strategy Phase 2, enabling the Royal Government to address challenges and strengthen implementation effectiveness to advance Cambodia's socioeconomic development.",""],[1,"137","2","National Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination and Capacity-Building","The Ministry of Planning is responsible for coordinating data collection, surveys, administrative records, and other essential statistics to support the monitoring and evaluation activities of all ministries-institutions.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","2","Pentagonal Strategy Phase 1 Monitoring and Evaluation Framework Implementation","It also facilitates the implementation of the monitoring and evaluation framework for the Pentagonal Strategy Phase 1, promotes the timely and accurate submission of progress reports by ministries-institutions, leads monitoring and evaluation for the NSDP, and builds the capacity of relevant ministries-institutions to improve the quality and effectiveness of monitoring, evaluation, and progress reporting.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","3","NSDP Performance Monitoring and Coordination Framework","Guide and coordinate with all relevant ministries-institutions to measure progress in implementing the NSDP for the 7th Legislature against established targets of performance indicators.",""],[1,"137","3","Performance Indicator Definitions and Data Methodology Standardization","Within the performance management framework, lead and coordinate with all relevant ministries-institutions to define the definitions, calculation methodologies, and data sources for each performance indicator, with the aim of establishing adequate tools for reviewing the accuracy of performance measurements in past implementation efforts.",""],[1,"137","4","Progress Monitoring and Implementation Coordination Mechanism","Monitor and evaluate the progress of planned work achievements, and coordinate with responsible institutions to expedite the implementation of measures and priority programs that are delayed or have not yet commenced.",""],[1,"137","5","Annual Monitoring and Evaluation Reporting","Prepare annual monitoring and evaluation reports, a mid-term evaluation in 2026, and an end-of-term evaluation in 2028, providing comprehensive assessments based on actual achievements, for submission to the Royal Government.",""],[1,"137","6","NSDP Coordination and Alignment Mechanism","Ministries-institutions are responsible for leading coordination and ensuring alignment in the development of policies, strategies, sectoral plans, annual action plans, and budgets to support the successful implementation of the NSDP.",""],[1,"137","6","NSDP Action Plan Implementation and Reporting","They shall implement action plans to achieve performance indicator targets, comply with relevant legal and regulatory guidelines for monitoring and evaluation, and provide timely progress reports and feedback to the Ministry of Planning.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","8","NSDP Implementation Action Plans and Budgeting","Develop detailed action plans and corresponding budgets to ensure the effective implementation of measures outlined in the NSDP.",""],[1,"137","9","Monitoring and Evaluation Framework and Progress Reporting Support","Collaborate with the Ministry of Planning in preparing the monitoring and evaluation framework and progress reports and support the implementation of measures and priority programs that are experiencing delays or have not yet progressed.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","10","Coordination Leadership and Focal Point Designation","Designate clear leadership and focal point officers to ensure effective coordination with the Ministry of Planning.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"137","11","NSDP Monitoring and Evaluation Reporting Guidelines","the Ministry of Planning shall develop guidelines for preparing annual monitoring reports, mid-term evaluations, and end-of-term evaluations, using a standardized reporting format for the NSDP monitoring and evaluation framework.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"138","1","Annual Monitoring Reports for NSDP Implementation","Annual Monitoring Reports focus on tracking the progress of NSDP implementation by ministries-institutions, with the objective of identifying achievements and/or emerging challenges, thereby facilitating the identification of timely and appropriate solutions to expedite implementation toward set targets.",""],[1,"138","9","Annual Monitoring Report Finalization Mechanism","Annual Monitoring Reports shall be finalized no later than two months after receiving progress monitoring reports from all ministries-institutions.",""],[1,"138","10","Mid-Term Evaluation Report Finalization Process","Mid-Term Evaluation Reports shall be finalized no later than three months after receiving mid-term evaluation reports from all ministries-institutions.",""],[1,"138","11","End-of-Term Evaluation Report Finalization Mechanism","End-of-Term Evaluation Reports shall be finalized no later than three months after receiving end-of-term evaluation reports from all ministries-institutions.",""],[1,"138","18","Monitoring and Evaluation Prioritization and Budget Support","Leaders of all ministries-institutions should prioritize monitoring and evaluation activities.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"139","2","NSDP Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity-Building for Focal Point Officers","The Ministry of Planning shall provide training and capacity-building initiatives for focal point officers in ministries-institutions on the NSDP framework and key indicators for monitoring, inspection, and evaluation","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"139","3","Sectoral Development Planning and Monitoring Framework","Ministries and institutions shall develop sectoral development plans, action plans, and strategic budgets aligned with the NSDP, as well as clear monitoring and evaluation plans to ensure successful sectoral implementation.","Ministries and institutions"],[1,"140","1","Comprehensive Cross-Sector Reform Programme","the Royal Government of Cambodia remains committed to undertaking comprehensive reforms across all sectors.",""],[1,"140","1","National Policy and Development Strategy Alignment Initiative","the Government seeks to align national policies and development strategies to form a unified driving force that builds a strong foundation and enhances resilience.",""],[1,"140","3","National Strategic Development Plan Implementation","the Royal Government remains determined, with unwavering commitment and readiness across all ministries and institutions, to effectively implement this National Strategic Development Plan.",""]],"5":[[1,"11","4","Sub-National Democratic Development Program","The National Program for Sub-National Democratic Development provides a strategic framework to transform sub-national administrations into a unified administration that ensures a timely and effective response to local development needs.",""],[1,"11","4","Sub-National Administration Reform and Fiscal Decentralization","The Royal Government has improved the structure, management systems, and work procedures, and transferred authority and functions, while also implementing financial decentralization by increasing spending for sub-national administrations.",""],[1,"11","4","Capacity Building for Sub-National Administrations","This is linked to capacity building to ensure clear transparency, accountability, and flexibility based on actual circumstances.",""],[1,"13","3","Decentralization and De-concentration Reform Program","In implementing the decentralization and de-concentration reform program to enhance work efficiency, the Royal Government has achieved commendable progress through the preparation and implementation of legal frameworks, national programs, action plans, and various technical guidance documents.",""],[1,"13","4","Sub-National Democratic Development Program Review and Administrative Reform","Specifically, the Royal Government has implemented two phases of the National Program for Sub-National Democratic Development.",""],[1,"13","4","Sub-National Administration Structure and Function Allocation Reform","This involves the continuous review and improvement of the structure, management system, and function allocation of sub-national administrations.",""],[1,"13","4","Capital and Provincial Administration Integration Reform","The government has also adjusted the structure and management system of capital and provincial administrations by integrating health departments, hospitals, operational district health offices, health centers, health posts, and state-run children's care centers into the management structure of",""],[1,"58","8","Provincial Administration Reform","Review and revise the structure, management system, and functions of provincial administration to align with the principles of unified administration and the characteristics of regional administration, aiming to establish a robust, intelligent, effective, and transparent provincial administration",""],[1,"58","9","Municipal and District Administration Institutional Strengthening and Evaluation","Strengthen and evaluate the organizational structure, and functions of municipal and district administrations to ensure alignment with the characteristics of urban and rural governance, as well as compatibility with local geographical, demographic, and economic potential",""],[1,"58","11","Collaborative Partnership Mobilization for Decentralization Reforms","Strengthen collaborative partnerships with development partners, civil society organizations, and the private sector to mobilize resources and foster participation in advancing deconcentration and decentralization reforms",""],[1,"58","13","Sub-national Social Accountability Strengthening","Continue to strengthen and expand social accountability efforts within sub-national administrations to enhance the effectiveness and transparency of public services delivery and local development.",""],[1,"59","4","Sub-national Human Resource Management Decentralization","Strengthening the effectiveness of human resource development and management at the sub-national level through the delegation of powers in decision making and responsibilities in terms of staff recruitments, management and deployment.",""],[1,"59","6","Decentralization of Sub-national Finance and Planning","Decentralizing sub-national administration's finance and planning to ensure adequate budget to perform its functions and policy priorities, as stipulated in the development plans, investment programs, and the budget strategic plans.",""],[1,"59","12","Sub-national Human Resource Management and Development Improvement","Enhance the effectiveness of human resource management and development at sub- national administrations",""],[1,"60","7","Sub-national Human Resources Management and Capacity-Building Support","Strengthen and enhance human resources management at sub-national administration level by appropriate allocating public officials on actual needs, ensuring competency, professional skills, ethical standards, and clearly defined working conditions, while providing capacity- building support to council members and public officials in sub-national administrations",""],[1,"60","9","Performance-Based Management System for Sub-National Administrations","Establish and implement performance-based management system within sub-national administrations",""],[1,"60","10","Incentive Policy for Sub-National Public Officials","Lead and coordinate study and formulation of policies to incentivize public officials serving in sub-national administration, aiming to attract and retain competent, experienced, and professionally skilled public officials to fulfill roles in sub-national administration, particularly in rural and remote areas",""],[1,"60","12","Sub-national Administration Performance Support, Monitoring, and Evaluation","Enhance the effectiveness of sub-national administration operations through continuous support, monitoring, and evaluation of their performance.",""]],"6":[[1,"16","3","Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy","To strengthen ownership and partnership in development, the Royal Government has prepared and implemented the 2019-2023 Strategy on Development Cooperation and Partnership.",""],[1,"16","3","Development Cooperation Alignment and Partnership Mechanisms","It also applies principles, mechanisms, and tools to align development cooperation with national development priorities, strengthen inclusive partnership in cooperation, and enhance the effectiveness of development cooperation.",""],[1,"16","3","Development Cooperation Financing Data Management System","By reinforcing Cambodia's data management system on cooperation financing, the government has improved the transparency, accountability, and efficiency of resource utilization.",""],[1,"16","3","Partnership Consultation Forums","Necessary mechanisms and partnership consultation forums at all levels have been implemented, achieving remarkable progress.",""],[1,"17","3","Economic Diplomacy Strategy","the Royal Government has implemented an economic diplomacy strategy and a proactive foreign policy.",""],[1,"32","4","Strengthening Bilateral and Multilateral Foreign Relations","In the foreign affairs sector, the Royal Government continues to strengthen and expand good relations and cooperation with all friendly countries, both bilaterally and multilaterally.",""],[1,"47","10","Smart Diplomacy and Strategic Partnership Expansion","Continue to strengthen the peaceful coexistence through building and expanding good relations with key partners, along with the pursuit of smart diplomacy",""],[1,"72","3","Strengthening Development Cooperation Coordination and Financing Management","The Cambodia Development Cooperation Board (CDCB) of the Council for the Development of Cambodia shall continue enhance effectiveness and foster coordinated, mutually beneficial partnerships with all development actors, grounded in the principles of equality and mutual respect, while strengthening the Royal Government's ownership of the national development agenda and further improving the effective management and use of development cooperation financing.",""],[1,"72","8","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"72","9","Development Cooperation Partnership Strategy 2024-2028","Formulating and implementing the \"Development Cooperation Partnership Strategy 2024-2028\" to strengthen inclusive partnerships.",""],[1,"72","10","Development Cooperation Financing Mobilization and Coordination","Mobilizing, coordinating, and managing development cooperation financing from all sources, and aligning resources with national priorities to improve efficiency of the resource utilization.",""],[1,"72","11","Strengthening Partnership Mechanisms and Tools","Enhancing the effectiveness of the implementation of existing partnership mechanisms and tools, which can be additionally created, when needed, to enhance bi-directional accountability and to strengthen inclusive partnerships.",""],[1,"72","12","Regional and Global Integration and Communications Initiative","Continuing to undertake regional and global integration and communications through mechanisms, measures, programs, and initiatives, to enhance Cambodia's prestige and interests, as well as to increase opportunities for development and confidence towards the climate for investment, business, and trade in Cambodia, based on the principles of \"equal rights and equal footing\".",""],[1,"73","1","Strengthening Partnerships with Non-Governmental Organizations","Continuing to strengthen partnerships with non-governmental organizations through the implementation of the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations to increase collaboration in a harmonious, effective, transparent, and accountable partnership.",""],[1,"73","4","Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy 2024-2028","Prepare and implement the Development Cooperation and Partnership Strategy 2024-2028 to further strengthen the Royal Government's ownership and leadership in advancing national development effectiveness, and to deepen constructive partnerships with all development actors",""],[1,"73","5","Development Cooperation Financing Mobilization and Coordination","Continue to mobilize, coordinate, and manage development cooperation financing from all sources, and align these resources prudently with national development priorities",""],[1,"73","6","Partnership Coordination Mechanism Strengthening","Enhance the effectiveness of existing partnership coordination mechanisms and instruments, and establish additional ones where necessary, to promote mutual accountability and strengthen constructive partnerships",""],[1,"73","7","NGO Partnership Strengthening through Legal Implementation","Further strengthen partnerships with non-governmental organizations through implementation of the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations and related normative legal documents, in order to foster collaborative partnerships that are harmonious, effective, transparent, and accountable",""],[1,"73","8","Development Cooperation Financing Review","Review the role of development cooperation financing to respond to rapid changes in the global and domestic development context and architecture, as well as the evolving structure of development finance flows for Cambodia",""],[1,"73","9","International Development Effectiveness Engagement and Coordination","Continue to engage in international forums on development effectiveness, and work jointly with development actors to implement relevant commitments consistent with Cambodia's context and the Royal Government's existing consultation mechanisms.",""],[1,"73","11","Foreign NGO Cooperation and Registration Facilitation","Continue robust cooperation with foreign non-governmental organizations in the national interest by fostering a favorable enabling environment for new registrations and renewals, ensuring transparent mission delivery, and supporting contributions to Cambodia's socio-economic development",""],[1,"73","14","Civil Society Cooperation and Resource Mobilization Expansion","Strengthen and expand cooperation with civil society organization (CSO) networks across the capital and provinces, by sector and partner membership, as well as with CSOs more broadly; further expand cooperation with CSOs from friendly countries to mobilize assistance and financial resources for domestic partner CSOs, and to deepen people-to- people solidarity between the Cambodian people and the peoples of friendly countries",""],[1,"73","15","Domestic CSO Classification and Capacity Development","Conduct research to classify and develop categories of domestic CSOs, and continue to strengthen the institutional capacity of the Civil Society Alliance Forum through staff",""],[1,"74","2","Continuation of Existing Projects and New Project Mobilization","Continue implementing existing projects and identify development partners to support the implementation of additional new projects",""],[1,"74","3","Funding Support for Cooperating Partner CSO Small-Scale Projects","Mobilize funding sources to support cooperating partner CSOs in implementing small-scale projects, in order to ensure continuity of activities.",""]],"7":[[1,"120","6","Land Registration and Land Dispute Settlement Reform","Continuing to deepen land reform by promoting land registration and out-of-court land dispute settlements, developing plans for land management and urbanization at both national and sub-national levels, aimed at streamlining the management and development of land.",""],[1,"121","3","Accelerated Land Administration and Registration Reform","Accelerate land administration processes through the implementation of the second-phase land registration plan, the registration of indigenous minority community lands as collective property, expedited registration of state lands, the formulation of legal and technical standards to incorporate construction information into immovable property ownership certificates, the acceleration of land dispute resolutions via all available mechanisms, the expansion of permanent satellite-based measurement station networks to facilitate nationwide mapping and land registration, the establishment of data management and information centers, and the ongoing update of the Kingdom of Cambodia's geographical name registry for newly established villages, communes, and districts",""],[1,"141","4","Single-Entry Identification Service Mechanism","Number of commune and sangkat administrations implement single-entry mechanisms for identification services",""]],"8":[[1,"133","3","Public Financial Management Reform Programs","the continued implementation of public financial management reform programs, accompanied by systematic monitoring and evaluation to ensure cost effectiveness",""],[1,"133","3","Planning and Budget Alignment Framework","strengthening the alignment between planning (under the frameworks of the NSDP and the three-year rolling Public Investment Program), budget formulation (within the strategic budget planning framework), and the management and execution of the budget",""]],"10":[[1,"109","10","Demographic Policy Measures for Workforce Sufficiency","Promoting the introduction of appropriate and timely policy measures, focusing on demographic changes manifested by changes in population age structure, to ensure that the rates of birth, mortality and migration remain in good condition that can translate into sufficiency of manpower to support the resilient, sustainable, and inclusive socio- economic development.",""],[1,"112","1","National Population Policy Implementation and Monitoring","Continue to promote and coordinate implementation of the National Population Policy 2016-2030 through phased monitoring and evaluation of action plans, a midterm progress review of the mandate, dissemination on population and demography, and awareness raising on community development",""],[1,"112","3","Capacity Building for Population and Development Officials","Strengthen the capacity of officials of the General Secretariat for Population and Development through training in analytical skills and calculation of key demographic indicators, demographic dividend indicators, and the five pillars of the demographic dividend (education, health, employment, economy, and governance) to inform relevant policies and strategies, maximize the demographic dividend, and enhance research competencies.",""],[1,"112","4","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries- institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""]],"11":[[1,"129","8","Legislative Drafting and Enactment Acceleration","Continuing to draft, accelerate, and enact draft laws and related regulations.",""]],"12":[[1,"94","5","Telecommunications and Radio Frequency Legal Reform","Draft and amend the law on telecommunications, the law on radio frequency, and related legal instruments",""],[1,"94","6","Policy and Regulatory Frameworks for Submarine Cables, Airspace, and Space Activities","Establish policy, legal, and regulatory frameworks for submarine cables, airspace and space activities, and satellites",""],[1,"94","7","National Radio Frequency Spectrum Planning and Regulation","Prepare the national radio frequency spectrum Plan and related regulations on planning, management, and allocation, to manage this scarce national resource efficiently in line with national and international standards",""],[1,"94","8","Mobile Base Station Rollout Monitoring","Continue monitoring the rollout of mobile base stations to expand coverage and improve service quality nationwide, especially at priority and remote tourism sites",""],[1,"94","9","Submarine and Cross-Border Fiber Optic Network Expansion","Increase the operational capacity of existing submarine and cross-border terrestrial fiber- optic cables and expand new builds to deliver high-speed, reliable internet services",""],[1,"94","10","Fiber-Optic Network Expansion for High-Speed Connectivity","Expand backbone and distribution fiber-optic networks to narrow the digital divide between national and subnational levels, extending high-speed connectivity to capitals, provinces, communes, and sangkats.",""]],"13":[[1,"125","9","High-Speed Internet and Fiber-Optic Connectivity Expansion","Continue building high-speed internet infrastructure and networks, deploy fiber-optic connectivity, and establish internal networks for ministries, government institutions, and subnational administrations",""],[1,"125","16","Cambodia Digital Community Platform","Establish a Cambodia digital community platform to convene digital experts and collaborate with relevant ministries and institutions to promote digital technologies to communities and the public, and establish a Digital Professionals Association to pool human resources and build professional capacity in the digital sector.",""],[1,"126","15","Digital Economy Satellite Account Framework Development","Digital Economy and Business Committee, in coordination with the Ministry of Planning, shall develop the Digital Economy Satellite Account framework to measure the size of the digital economy.","Ministry of Planning"],[1,"128","9","Digital Infrastructure Expansion Programme","The strategic objectives are to build and expand digital infrastructures, including digital connectivity, telecommunications infrastructures and cloud or data centers, aimed at strengthening the quality and efficiency of digital connectivity, information sharing and provision of telecommunications services.",""],[1,"128","10","Telecommunications Infrastructure Investment and Service Coverage Expansion","Encouraging telecommunications operators and Internet service providers to improve the quality and coverage of services through more investments in infrastructures, especially in areas with high potentials.",""],[1,"128","11","Telecommunications Backbone and Digital Connectivity Expansion","Continuing to build and develop telecommunications backbone infrastructures and distribution networks; and enhancing digital infrastructure connectivity at national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"128","12","Universal Service Obligation Fund for Telecommunications Network Expansion","Promoting investments and the use of the Universal Service Obligation Fund in an efficient, transparent, and accountable manner, to build and expand telecommunications networks and supporting infrastructures for high-speed Internet connections to reduce digital gaps.",""],[1,"128","13","Submarine and Cross-Border Optical Cable Capacity Expansion Assessment","Assessing the feasibility of increasing the capacity of existing submarine and cross-border optical cables, when needed.",""],[1,"128","14","Telecommunications Infrastructure and Spectrum Regulatory Update","Continuing to update laws and regulations related to the management of telecommunications infrastructures and radio frequency spectrum resources.",""],[1,"128","15","Telecom Infrastructure Sharing Promotion","Continuing to promote the sharing of telecom infrastructures, in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.",""],[1,"128","16","Cloud Infrastructure Regulatory Framework Development","Developing regulatory frameworks for cloud infrastructures, by sectors and classifications of data.",""],[1,"129","1","National Data Center Utilization and Private Data Center Investment Initiative","Promoting the utilization of national data centers to support digital systems of ministries- institutions that do not have a data center; and encouraging private operators to invest in building data centers, with attention given to high standards and security of data.",""],[1,"129","3","Digital Government Network Infrastructure Upgrade","Develop and optimize the digital government network infrastructure to connect all ministries, institutions, and Cambodian missions abroad over a secure, dedicated government network, by upgrading existing infrastructure and investing in additional networks",""],[1,"129","4","Subnational Digital Infrastructure Connectivity Expansion","Accelerate digital infrastructure connectivity at subnational levels, from capital and provinces to communes and sangkats, including commune and sangkat administrations, administrative police posts, schools, health centers, and community hubs, to support digital public service delivery, online education and training, and access to market and agricultural information",""],[1,"129","5","National Data Center Establishment","Establish a National Data Center, including an operations center and a disaster recovery site, leveraging cloud technologies to provide infrastructure, platform, software, and data services for government and the private sector",""],[1,"129","6","National Infrastructure Data Registry","Develop a national infrastructure data registry to manage, monitor, and evaluate the performance and needs of national infrastructure.",""],[1,"148","7","Digital Platform Development and Utilization for Industry, SMEs, and Handicrafts","Promotion of the development and utilization of digital platforms in industrial, SMEs, and handicraft sector",""]],"14":[[1,"94","11","Digital Policy and Regulatory Framework Development","Develop policies that promote key digital technologies, including the Digital Government Roadmap, data governance policy, open data policy, priority cloud policy, a national artificial intelligence strategy, the cybersecurity law, the personal data protection law, the digital government law, the information and communications technology law, the online safety law, a sub-decree establishing digital transformation units, and standards and guidelines on digital signatures, data centers, interoperability, and internal cybersecurity management",""],[1,"94","12","Digital Infrastructure Interconnection Initiative","Promote interconnection of digital infrastructure across ministries and state and private institutions at national and subnational levels",""],[1,"94","13","Digital Identity Infrastructure and Telephone Number Management System","Develop and strengthen digital identity infrastructure and the telephone-number management system to support the management, use, and verification of natural and legal persons in digital form for online transactions, while reinforcing national and personal security",""],[1,"94","14","Single-Window Public Service Delivery Platform","Establish a single-window service platform to deliver public services across ministries and institutions at national and subnational levels",""],[1,"95","6","Public Service Delivery Automation and Technology Platform Upgrade","Enhancing quality, transparency, efficiency, and reliability, and bringing public services closer to consumers/users through the use of automation systems and technology platforms for public service delivery to facilitate procedures, reduce time and other related expenses; as well as performing inspections and ensuring other compliances",""]],"15":[[1,"76","12","Digital Education and School Digital Infrastructure Development","Continuing to promote digital education, developing digital infrastructures in schools, and promoting studies of science, technology, engineering, arts and mathematics (STEAM).",""],[1,"77","7","Digital Education and STEM Support Programme","Advance digital education, develop digital infrastructure in schools, and enhance teaching and learning in science and technology, with targeted support for STEM-related research projects",""],[1,"94","15","National E-Learning and Training Platform","Promote a national e-learning and training platform to provide educational content that reduces the digital divide, especially in remote rural areas, via online delivery",""],[1,"94","16","Digital Inclusion Support for Vulnerable Groups","Advance digital inclusion by supporting the development and provision of devices, systems, and digital content for persons with disabilities, young children, the elderly, and people with low literacy",""],[1,"94","17","Digital Talent Development Programme","Develop digital talent in line with Cambodia's 2024-2035 Digital Skills Development Roadmap.",""]],"16":[[1,"91","10","Digital Technology Adoption in Business and Economic Activities","Encouraging the optimum use of digital technologies, especially in the business and economic activities through interconnected and systematic measures.",""],[1,"95","1","Research, Development, and Digital Innovation Promotion","Promote research and development and digital innovation in public and private institutions, consistent with the digital economy and society policy and the Cambodia digital government policy",""],[1,"95","2","Digital Parks and Startup Market Expansion Initiative","Establish digital parks and expand market opportunities for digital start-ups by fostering partnerships between start-ups and enterprises of all sizes and sectors.",""],[1,"102","12","Shared Digital Infrastructure and Digital Innovation Platform Development","Continue to build and develop shared digital infrastructure and digital innovation platforms, and establish mechanisms to implement enterprise digital transformation programs",""],[1,"102","13","Science, Technology and Innovation Hub Development","Promote the application of science and technology, and develop the national institute of science, technology and innovation into a hub for creativity, invention, and innovation to serve the industrial and handicraft sectors, especially micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs).",""],[1,"103","2","National Start-up Development Strategy","Formulate and implement a national strategy for start-up development",""],[1,"103","3","National Start-up Program and Start-up Support Services","Continue implementing the Cambodia national start-up program, contribute to building the start-up ecosystem, and continue to design and deliver support programs for start-ups, including business incubation and acceleration",""],[1,"103","4","Enterprise Digital Transformation Program","Continue implementing the enterprise digital transformation program to accelerate digital adoption among micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSMEs)",""],[1,"126","17","Digital Transformation and E-Commerce Promotion Programme","promote digital transformation in the economic sectors; develop digital startups; and promote the Enterprises Go Digital, the development of digital value chains and e-commerce, and building and development of digital innovation system, to facilitate business and trade, aimed at accelerating economic growth.",""],[1,"127","3","Development of Common Digital Enabling and Innovation Platforms","Continuing to develop common digital enabling platforms and digital innovation platforms.",""],[1,"127","4","Digital Startups, Digital Businesses, and E-Commerce Ecosystem Support Programme","Promoting digital startups, digital businesses, and e-commerce ecosystem to be more vibrant and complementary to one another through market linkages and expansions, expansion of investment, financing, and other supportive programs.",""],[1,"127","5","Enterprises Go Digital Program","Developing and launching the Enterprises Go Digital program.",""],[1,"127","9","Digital Economy Legal and Regulatory Framework","Introducing laws on digital economy and supportive regulations, and incorporating digital economy into the national account.",""],[1,"127","12","Last-Mile Delivery Sector Strategic Plan","Develop and establish a strategic plan to promote and advance the last-mile delivery sector, to create an ecosystem and concrete implementation mechanisms in this field, grounded in the principles of efficiency, innovation, sustainability, crisis resilience, and interoperability",""],[1,"127","14","MSME Cluster Pilot and Development Programme","Foster an entrepreneurial culture, digital market literacy, and innovative mindsets, and advance digital business practices for micro, small and medium enterprises, through piloting and developing MSME clusters in priority sectors.",""],[1,"127","16","Digital Accreditation Framework for Conformity Assessment Bodies","Establish a procedural framework for assessing, recognizing, and accrediting competence and capability for conformity assessment bodies and related registration services via digital platforms, to facilitate domestic and international trade",""],[1,"127","17","Competitive Innovation Challenge Mechanisms","Create competitive mechanisms and challenges for technologists, entrepreneurs, and engineers to identify and nurture talented industry actors and catalyze innovation, especially among young engineers and entrepreneurs",""],[1,"127","18","Digital Technology Application Workshops for SMEs","Organize workshops on the application of digital technologies for business operations for small and medium enterprises",""],[1,"127","19","Industrial Technology Transfer and Matchmaking Support","Promote and incentivize the transfer of new technologies in the industrial sector, including handicrafts, to strengthen SME capabilities for technology transfer and technology matchmaking",""],[1,"128","1","Technical Officials Capacity-Building for Service Delivery and Inspection","Build the capacity of technical officials to keep pace with technological advances, enabling proactive service delivery and high-quality, efficient inspection and verification",""],[1,"128","2","Metrology Law Implementation and Sector Development Plan Activities","Strengthen implementation of the Law on Metrology and carry out activities under the Metrology Sector Development Strategic Plan 2023-2027.",""],[1,"128","3","Digital Business and E-Commerce Promotion","Ministry of Commerce shall promote digital business, enterprise digital transformation, digital value chains, and e-commerce by effectively implementing the Law on Electronic Commerce","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"128","5","Cambodia Startup Platform Development and Adoption Support","Continue to develop and drive adoption of the Cambodia Startup Platform to support startups and help build a vibrant national entrepreneurship ecosystem",""],[1,"128","6","Enterprise Digital Transformation Programs","Promote wide-scale and effective implementation of enterprise digital transformation programs",""],[1,"128","7","Entrepreneurship and Innovation Support Programs","Continue to design and implement programs that support and promote entrepreneurship and innovation, contributing to a dynamic startup ecosystem",""],[1,"128","8","Digital Economy Law Drafting Feasibility Assessment","Assess the feasibility of drafting a Digital Economy Law and related normative legal documents.",""]],"17":[[1,"69","2","National Cybersecurity and Digital Security Capacity Strengthening","The National Center for Information Technology prioritizes actions to, combat terrorism and crime in Cambodia through information and digital systems, prevent and suppress radicalization, extremism, the dissemination of false information, and incitement that could provoke social unrest aimed at undermining the lawful Royal Government, manage and safeguard technology security, build and strengthen the human resource capacity and infrastructure of security forces in the technology field, domestically and abroad, and strengthen and expand security cooperation in the technology sector with partners at home and overseas.",""],[1,"69","4","Journalism Ethics Code Enforcement","Organize and regulate the conduct of journalists by fully applying the professional code of ethics for journalism, so that journalists perform their duties professionally, responsibly, and effectively",""],[1,"69","5","Amend Normative Legal Documents for Inclusive Dissemination","Amend existing normative legal documents to promote effective inclusive dissemination",""],[1,"69","6","Joint False Information Response Campaigns","Develop joint campaigns to combat false information, setting out specific mechanisms for response",""],[1,"69","7","Digital Technology Training for Civil Servants and Journalists","Provide digital-technology training for civil servants and journalists to improve the quality and effectiveness of information and public communication, aligned with social context and global digital transformation",""],[1,"69","8","Strategic Information and Public Opinion Management","Coordinate with Ministries-institutions and municipal and provincial administrations to manage information and public opinion, disseminating through all formats, especially digital television and digital radio, expanding coverage, and responding promptly to negative information in a proactive, coordinated manner, to safeguard the Royal Government's achievements and reputation",""],[1,"69","9","Information Sector Capacity-Building and Partnership Cooperation","Promote cooperation with national and international institutions and partners to strengthen capacity, exchange experience, and train human resources in the information sector",""],[1,"69","10","Government Communication and Dissemination Campaign","Produce and disseminate articles, interviews, videos, audio, images, and newsletters on the Royal Government's policies, strategies, actions, and achievements, to ensure rapid and effective communication.",""],[1,"69","11","Cybersecurity Law Implementation and National Cybersecurity Management System","the Ministry of Post and Telecommunications shall prioritize advancing the adoption of the Cybersecurity Law, preparing related normative legal documents, establishing a national cybersecurity management system, and promoting training and public awareness on cybersecurity.","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications"],[1,"69","12","Digital Security Governance Coordination Committee","Digital Security Committee shall lead, coordinate, and drive digital security governance to protect the interests of all stakeholders against attacks of every kind, ensuring responses through technical measures and operational forces responsible for guaranteeing and safeguarding digital security.",""],[1,"129","7","Digital Security Infrastructure and Institutional Framework Development","The strategic objectives are to build trustworthiness in digital system through the development of infrastructures and institutional frameworks for digital security and raising awareness on digital security to promote the widespread use of digital technologies.",""],[1,"129","9","Digital Security Committee and National Center for Digital Security","Establishing Digital Security Committee and National Center for Digital Security; and encouraging more investments in digital security infrastructures and systems.",""],[1,"129","9","Digital Security Infrastructure Investment","Establishing Digital Security Committee and National Center for Digital Security; and encouraging more investments in digital security infrastructures and systems.",""],[1,"129","10","Digital Security Governance Framework Development","Developing rules and procedures, standards, technical frameworks, guiding principles, codes of conduct, and response mechanisms, as the foundation for developing digital security infrastructures and systems.",""],[1,"129","11","Critical Infrastructure Digital Security Framework","Developing a framework for re-evaluating loopholes and strengthening digital security systems for critical infrastructures.",""],[1,"129","12","Digital Security Skills Training and Awareness Programme","Continuing to provide training on and develop digital security skills; and raising awareness on digital security to publicly mainstream digital security, self-protection, and anti- cybercrime.",""],[1,"129","13","Cybercrime Collaboration and Cooperation Mechanism","Establishing collaboration and cooperation mechanisms among institutions concerned, including the state, private sector, and the public, to timely report, prevent, institute security measures and move towards cybercrime crackdown.",""],[1,"129","14","Global and Regional Digital Security Cooperation Frameworks","Establishing global and regional cooperation frameworks for information sharing and risk management, related to digital security in both global and regional contexts.",""],[1,"130","3","Cybersecurity Safeguards and Information Security Governance Framework","Develop and implement cybersecurity safeguards, including policies and normative legal documents for governance, standards for information security management systems, and audit trail and data integrity verification systems for data use and data flows",""],[1,"130","4","Digital Security Operations Center","Establish a Digital Security Operations Center to monitor technology systems against attacks and unlawful intrusions, including a cybersecurity operations center and a digital forensics laboratory to support research, monitoring, data analysis, and the protection of technology systems",""],[1,"130","5","Digital Public Order and Cybersecurity Mechanism","Develop and implement mechanisms to maintain public order and security in the digital domain, in cooperation with relevant partners, to enhance quality, strengthen cybersecurity, and combat cybercrime.",""],[1,"130","6","National Information Infrastructure Cybersecurity Strengthening","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications shall continue to strengthen digital security management and protection for the national information infrastructure by establishing security procedures and deploying technical systems and equipment for monitoring, supervision, protection, and prevention of cyberattacks.","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications"],[1,"130","7","Digital Security Committee Coordination and Leadership Mechanism","Digital Security Committee shall ensure the effective and authoritative delivery of leadership, coordination, and promotion of digital security management to protect the interests of all stakeholders, withstand attacks of all forms, and mount comprehensive responses across technical and operational dimensions to ensure and safeguard digital security.",""],[1,"148","14","National Computer Emergency Response Team Coordination Mechanism","Computer Emergency Response Team (CERT) mechanism cooperates nationally with the public and private sectors",""],[1,"148","15","International Cooperation for the Computer Emergency Response Team Mechanism","Computer Emergency Response Team (CERT) mechanism cooperates internationally",""]],"18":[[1,"17","1","E-Commerce Strategy and Go4eCAM Project","The e-Commerce Strategy / Go4eCAM Project ... have also been implemented.",""],[1,"24","4","E-commerce Legal and Digital Trade Services System","The government has also implemented a system for depositing notification letters for guaranteed transactions linked to an electronic payment system and is providing public services for commercial registration, trademark registration, and Certificate of Origin applications through an automated system.",""],[1,"25","1","Digital Commerce Platforms and Market Access Support","Other efforts include creating digital platforms for management, application, and product recognition, and helping to find markets for \"One Village One Product\" goods.",""]],"19":[[1,"25","2","National Digital Television Platform","the Royal Government, with the Ministry of Information as its facilitator, has established a national digital television platform.","Ministry of Information"],[1,"25","2","ASEAN Digital Media Harmonization Cooperation","Cooperation within the ASEAN framework is being pursued to harmonize the development of digital media in the region.",""],[1,"25","2","Digital Television Transition and Analog Switch-Off","The transition from analog to digital television is underway to launch the Cambodian digital television platform by the end of 2023 and shut down analog broadcasts by 2025.",""]],"20":[[1,"90","11","Postal Sector Development Policy Implementation Strengthening","Making a push for and strengthening the implementation of the Postal Sector Development Policy 2022-2020.",""],[1,"93","16","Postal Services Law and Regulatory Reform","Enact the Law on Postal Services and related normative legal documents to strengthen service quality management and sector competition",""],[1,"94","1","Integrated Postal Network Development","Develop an integrated postal network that reaches communes and build key infrastructure, including postal logistics warehouses and customs bonded warehouses",""],[1,"94","2","National Addressing and Postcode System","Establish a national addressing and postcode system to improve the speed and reliability of mail receipt and delivery, meeting the needs of businesses and the public",""],[1,"94","3","Digital Postal Ecosystem Development","Build a digital postal ecosystem by creating and using digital postal platforms, such as DGPost, to support postal service delivery and last-mile logistics",""],[1,"94","4","E-commerce Enabling Technology Platforms","Promote enabling technology platforms for e-commerce to facilitate lawful business operations.",""]],"21":[[1,"13","2","Justice Sector Legal and Institutional Strengthening","The government has promoted the development of the legal and justice sector by training qualified human resources, organizing workshops, and disseminating knowledge on criminal and civil law to law enforcement officials, judges, and prosecutors nationwide.",""],[1,"13","2","Justice Sector Cooperation Projects","It has collaborated with international partner organizations and NGOs on numerous cooperation projects in the justice sector.",""],[1,"13","2","Judicial Inspection and Complaints Handling Mechanism","The government has consistently enhanced and strengthened inspection mechanisms, monitored the professional discipline, ethics, and dignity of judges and prosecutors, and addressed complaints related to their professional conduct.",""],[1,"13","2","Legal Aid for Poor Citizens","The government has provided legal aid to poor citizens who cannot afford lawyers, successfully resolved case backlogs by creating a task force to address them in provincial and municipal courts, and helped alleviate prison overcrowding.",""],[1,"13","2","Out-of-Court Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","It has also promoted out-of-court dispute resolution through legal consultations and community-level dispute resolution mechanisms, and promoted gender equality in the justice sector by organizing training, workshops, and disseminating knowledge on relevant topics to law enforcement officials, judges, and prosecutors, with a special focus on the CEDAW Convention and national laws related to women and children.",""],[1,"33","2","National Authority for Non-Judicial Dispute Resolution","the Royal Government has enhanced the quality and effectiveness of the justice system by creating the National Authority for Non-Judicial Dispute Resolution (NANDR).",""],[1,"33","2","Court Case Resolution Campaigns","It launched campaigns to promote and expedite the resolution of cases in courts, successfully addressing nearly 190 000 cases, which accounts for 82.4% of cases nationwide.",""],[1,"62","7","Justice Sector Human Resource Capacity Enhancement","Enhancing the capacity of human resources in the justice sector, both quantity and quality, to increase the work efficiency in the justice sector and the effectiveness and speed of the settlements of disputes, both in court and out of court.",""],[1,"62","9","Law Compliance and Legal Aid Services","Strengthening law compliance and providing legal support services through the promotion of education, the dissemination of the laws, the provision of legal consultation services, and the provision of legal defense services to ensure the rights to justice, particularly for the poor and the vulnerable.",""],[1,"62","10","Law Enforcement and Court Integrity Strengthening","Promoting fairness and effectiveness of law enforcement by law enforcement officers and court officials, particularly strengthening the effectiveness of court proceedings, integrity, professionalism, and ethics of law enforcement officers and court officials, as well as improving the inspection and punishment mechanisms to build trust in law enforcement.",""],[1,"62","11","Court Administration Modernization and Justice Service Improvement","Enhancing the quality and effectiveness of the court system through modernizing the court administration to improve the quality of justice service deliveries and through strengthening the quality of justice.",""],[1,"62","12","Legal Framework and Dispute Settlement Mechanism Development","Promoting the development of the legal frameworks and dispute settlement mechanisms for adjudicating and mediating disputes both in and out of court in ways to increase the effectiveness and speed of the settlements of disputes; and bringing dispute settlement services closer to the people.",""],[1,"63","5","Out-of-Court Dispute Resolution Framework and Mediation Mechanisms","Enhance the effectiveness of out-of-court dispute resolution by establishing legal frameworks and mechanisms for mediation and conciliation both within and outside the court system, to improve efficiency and timeliness, reduce case backlogs at provincial-municipal courts of first instance, bring accessible and diversified services closer to citizens, and help sustain social peace and harmony",""],[1,"63","6","Judicial System Integrity and Access to Justice Reform","Inspect and address irregularities in the courts by strengthening public confidence in the judicial system, a core objective of justice-sector reform, with strong emphasis on facilitating citizens' access to justice and promoting transparency, integrity, and propriety in law enforcement and judicial proceedings",""],[1,"63","7","Judicial Case Adjudication Acceleration","Accelerate adjudication by ensuring cases are resolved by the courts promptly and fairly, a key priority of judicial reform, to raise the quality and efficiency of services delivered to the public in a timely, convenient, and procedurally correct manner",""],[1,"63","8","Justice Sector Human Resource Development Plan","Strengthen human capital in the justice sector by expanding the number and quality of personnel as a foundation for effective law enforcement and system performance; enhancing the quality and effectiveness of the Royal Academy for Judicial Professions of Cambodia; formulating a justice-sector human resource development plan; reinforcing discipline and codes of ethics for judicial officials; incentivizing meritorious officials who demonstrate integrity; providing ongoing training on new legal instruments; and continuing cooperation with international partners on legal and judicial human-resource development projects",""],[1,"63","9","Legal Awareness and Rule-of-Law Promotion","Promote legal awareness in society by fostering a \"culture of respect for the law,\" the foundation of a \"rule-of-law society,\" in line with the Constitution as the supreme law of the land",""],[1,"63","10","Legal Aid Expansion and Access to Justice Reform","Expand legal aid by guaranteeing equal access to justice for all citizens, especially the poor and vulnerable, through digital platforms for legal information, counseling, and public legal education; establishing legal counseling mechanisms at courts; strengthening the pro bono (volunteer lawyer) defense scheme for the poor to ensure timely assistance; assessing legal aid and defense services before the courts; and creating monitoring, evaluation, and ethics/compliance mechanisms for legal counselors and defense providers",""],[1,"63","11","Operationalization of Specialized Courts","Operationalize specialized courts by bringing into operation the Commercial Court and the Labor Court, critical elements of judicial reform, to deliver case resolution that is efficient, credible, and timely, and to respond to demands for an improved investment and business climate in Cambodia.",""]],"22":[[1,"18","2","Education Sector Reform Programme","The education sector has been continuously reformed to create a good environment for inclusive education, aiming to develop human resources with high human capital and skills to meet the demands of national development and the labor market.",""],[1,"33","4","Curriculum, Textbook, and Teacher Capacity Improvement Programme","the government continues to improve curricula, develop textbooks, strengthen teacher capacity and ethics, enhance school management, promote community participation and digital education, encourage the adoption of STEAM subjects, and promote a movement for every young person to learn at least one sport for life",""],[1,"51","9","Education and Skills Training Quality Improvement","by strengthening the quality of education and skills trainings, hard and soft",""],[1,"76","8","Education Governance and Quality Improvement Strategy","The strategic objectives are to create a conducive environment for education and trainings with high quality and expertise, focusing on the strengthening of governance in educational institutions, improving the quality of trainings at all levels, improving the quality and access to education related to science, technology, engineering, arts, and mathematics (STEAM), and strengthening physical education and sports.",""],[1,"76","8","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation Requirement","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector- specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"76","9","Education Quality and Curriculum Updating Initiative","Continuing to enhance quality of education and trainings at all levels, updating curricula at all levels, and creating an environment conducive to lifelong learning.",""],[1,"76","10","School Reform Continuation and Expansion Programme","Continuing to implement school reforms with a focus on further enhancing the existing achievements, promoting the establishment of new generation schools and role-model schools, strengthening governance and management efficiency of the Departments of Education, Youth and Sports, as well as promoting strong participation and ownership from parents, communities, and the private sector.","Departments of Education, Youth and Sports"],[1,"76","11","Teacher Training and Teaching Methods Improvement","Strengthening the quality of teachers' training and teaching methods, as well as continuing to improve livelihoods and promote social values of teaching personnel at all levels.",""],[1,"76","13","School Health Promotion and Scholarship Support for Poor and Vulnerable Students","Promoting school health and increasing scholarships for the poor and vulnerable students.",""],[1,"77","4","Education Quality Enhancement and Curriculum Alignment Programme","Continue to enhance education quality at all levels, update curricula to align with actual labor market needs, expand New Generation Schools and model schools, and foster an enabling environment for lifelong learning",""],[1,"77","5","Education, Youth, and Sports Governance Reform","Deepen reforms and strengthen governance across education, youth, and sports at all levels;",""],[1,"77","6","Teacher Training Quality Improvement and Scholarship Expansion","Improve the quality of training and tutors' training methods; continue raising the livelihoods and social standing of teaching staff at all levels; promote student health; and expand scholarships for poor and high-achieving students",""],[1,"77","8","Equipment and Lab-Based Learning Investment in Schools","Increase investment in equipment and lab-based learning in new generation schools, model schools, general secondary schools, and technical education institutions, to raise the quality of general education and STEM in Cambodia",""],[1,"77","12","Secondary-to-Higher Education Transition and TVET Expansion Programme","Strengthen pathways from secondary to higher education and expand enrollment in technical and vocational education through attractive curricula, scholarships, career counseling, and life-skills training, in collaboration with higher education and TVET institutions.",""]],"23":[[1,"18","4","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Policy and Infrastructure Upgrade","The Royal Government has continued to promote and enhance technical skills training by issuing and implementing various policies and strategic plans related to technical and vocational education and training.",""],[1,"18","4","Expanded Technical and Vocational Skills Training and Labor Force Capacity Development","The government has expanded the provision of technical and vocational skills training to 272 000 people and continues to promote the capacity development of the labor force, both for those already in the job market and those preparing to enter it.",""],[1,"18","4","Apprenticeship, Internship, and Prior Learning Recognition Programme","This has been achieved through an apprenticeship program for 129 000 people, an internship and study visit program to factories and enterprises for 224 000 students, a test to assess and recognize prior learning, and a push to manage and develop the capacity of engineers.",""],[1,"18","5","TVET Governance Strengthening and Quality Assurance","the Royal Government has reinforced governance within the technical and vocational education and training (TVET) system by strengthening the capacity of management committees and civil servants, preparing legal instruments and a draft law on TVET, supervising and evaluating the quality assurance of TVET institutions and the competence of technical and",""],[1,"55","3","Professional Skills Development Programs","Special focus is being placed on professional training programs that meet market demands, particularly in high-tech sectors",""],[1,"78","5","Technical and Vocational Training Transformation","The strategic objectives are to pursue the transformation of the technical and vocational trainings, increase enrollments in the sector, promote reskilling and upskilling, strengthen ecosystems for skills development, address skills mismatches between trainings and actual demands, both in terms of skills and skills quality, and strengthen monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of policies and strategies that have been laid out.",""],[1,"78","5","Skills Development Ecosystem Strengthening","The strategic objectives are to pursue the transformation of the technical and vocational trainings, increase enrollments in the sector, promote reskilling and upskilling, strengthen ecosystems for skills development, address skills mismatches between trainings and actual demands, both in terms of skills and skills quality, and strengthen monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of policies and strategies that have been laid out.",""],[1,"78","5","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning for NSDP Implementation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"78","6","TVET Governance Strengthening and Digitalization Reform","Strengthening system governance, and governance of technical and vocational education and training (TVET) institutions, both public and private, through updating relevant policies and legal instruments, digitalization, and strengthening monitoring and evaluation mechanisms.",""],[1,"78","7","Teacher Capacity and Qualification Improvement in TVET Institutions","Continuing to improve the teachers' capacity and qualifications by encouraging them to conduct further studies and carry out regular research, as well as by attracting highly qualified teachers with strong practical backgrounds to teach in TVET institutions nationwide.",""],[1,"78","8","Technical and Vocational Skills Training Programmes","Strengthening the quality of technical and vocational skills, both soft and hard, through the full implementation of training programs based on capacity and industrial needs.",""],[1,"78","9","Upskilling, Reskilling, and Skills Recognition Programme","Promoting and strengthening upskilling programs; expanding skills training, reskilling, and skill recognition testing programs; promoting research, innovation, and practical techniques in line with actual needs; as well as promoting dissemination in all forms.",""],[1,"78","10","Student Loan Mechanism for Technical and Vocational Skills","Establishing loans mechanisms for students to encourage the acquisitions of technical and vocational skills, especially priority skills.",""],[1,"78","11","Public-Private Partnership and Stakeholder Dialogue Mechanism","Continuing to strengthen public-private partnerships, promoting regular dialogues between the public and private sectors, as well as development partners, and mobilizing funds to support R&D (Research and Development).",""],[1,"79","2","TVET Policy Update and Skills Training Expansion","Strengthen governance and improve the quality of technical and vocational education and training (TVET) by updating policies in alignment with the Cambodia Qualifications Framework (CQF); expand the scale and quality of skills training to raise workforce capability and productivity in line with labor market demand",""],[1,"79","3","TVET Partnership and Resource Mobilization Mechanism","Promote partnerships and collaboration among the Government, the private sector, and development partners to elevate the role of TVET in socio-economic development; institutionalize regular public-private-development partner dialogue and mobilize resources to support research and development",""],[1,"79","4","Research, Innovation, and Applied Technology Center Expansion","Advance research, innovation, and applied technologies by expanding the number of research, innovation, and applied technology centers, particularly in industrial automation and robotics",""],[1,"79","5","Instructor Capacity and Curriculum Development Initiative","Continue enhancing the capacity and qualifications of instructors; develop curricula, internships, and routine research programs; and attract highly qualified practitioners with hands-on experience to teach",""],[1,"79","6","Standards-Based Technical Education Promotion","Promote standards-based technical education by encouraging skills competitions, advancing digitalization of training, and strengthening monitoring and evaluation mechanisms for training.",""],[1,"81","4","Vocational and Technical Training for Target Youth","vocational and technical training programs for target youth",""],[1,"82","6","Targeted Cash Assistance for Youth Skills Training","targeted cash assistance to provide skills training for youth from poor households",""]],"24":[[1,"76","14","Higher Education Governance, R&D, Innovation, and Public-Private Partnership Promotion","Strengthening governance of higher education institutions, promoting research and development (R&D), and innovation, and promoting public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"77","5","Science, Innovation, and Creativity Research Incentive Scheme","promote research and publication in science, innovation, and creativity through appropriate incentive mechanisms;",""],[1,"77","5","Research Output Dissemination and Conference Participation Expansion","and scale up exhibitions of research outputs, competitions, and participation in domestic and international conferences",""],[1,"78","1","Research Capacity Enhancement Programme","Enhance research capacity by advancing research methodology development at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expanding collaborative research with domestic and international higher education institutions, organizing seminars on research methods and academic writing, and conducting study visits with international research institutes",""],[1,"78","2","Scientific Research and Research Cooperation Strengthening","Scale up scientific research in the Royal Academy of Cambodia's areas of specialization; strengthen research cooperation with ministries, national and international institutions; and collect, curate, publish in peer-reviewed scientific journals, and archive research outputs, findings, and evidence for practical application and as inputs to national policies and strategies",""],[1,"78","3","Research Capacity Development Support Mobilization","Mobilize scholars with international research and publication experience, both in Cambodia and overseas, to more broadly support research capacity development and research activities at the Royal Academy of Cambodia",""]],"25":[[1,"77","13","Buddhist Education Quality Improvement Programme","Ministry of Cult and Religion shall focus on implementing priority actions in to strengthening the quality of Buddhist education from primary through postgraduate levels, in line with national and international education standards.","Ministry of Cult and Religion"],[1,"77","13","Teacher Training and Certification for Buddhist Education","Key measures include providing teacher training and certification at all levels",""],[1,"77","13","Buddhist Education Research and Curriculum Development","advancing research and compiling curricula and reference materials",""],[1,"77","13","Library Strengthening in Pagodas and Buddhist Schools","strengthening and expanding libraries in pagodas and Buddhist schools",""],[1,"77","13","Buddhist Education Partnership Cooperation Mechanism","fostering cooperation with national and international partner institutions in Buddhist education",""],[1,"77","13","Community-Level Buddhist School Expansion","continuing to expand Buddhist schools at the community level.",""],[1,"86","1","Buddhist Education and Monastic Affairs Support Measures","upbringing of Buddhist novices, continuing to organize and publicize the National Monastic Congress, collaborating with relevant ministries and the Sangha Council to integrate Buddhist education into the national curriculum, elevating the value of Buddhism through the monastic inspectorate in capitals and provinces, publishing the history and works of the Samdech Supreme Patriarch, reviewing and encouraging publications in the state religious sector, exercising administrative oversight of religious affairs, strengthening the management of pagodas, vipassana centers, and religious ceremonies","relevant ministries | the Sangha Council"]],"26":[[1,"79","7","Non-Communicable Disease Reduction and Health Service Improvement","The strategic objectives are to continue to reduce morbidity and mortality from major non- communicable diseases; continue to promote reproductive health, and infant, child and maternal health; strengthen institutional capacity to lead the transformation and governance in health sector; continue to improve the quality and diagnostic capacity in treatment and care; continue to strengthen the quality of health vocational training; enhance expertise; promote cooperation between relevant ministries-institutions; and encourage community participation.",""],[1,"79","9","Health and Social Welfare System Capacity Enhancement","Enhancing capacity of health and social welfare systems so that they can respond in a timely and effective manner to the endeavors to promote public health and people's well- being, including in the event of disease outbreaks.",""],[1,"79","10","Primary Health Care System Strengthening","Strengthening innovative health care systems, focusing on primary health care;",""],[1,"79","10","Healthy Diet Promotion Initiative","promoting healthy diet for all;",""],[1,"79","10","Health Service Quality and Efficiency Improvement","improving quality, safety, and efficiency;",""],[1,"79","10","Health Care Coverage Expansion","expanding the coverage of health care services, distribution, and use of medicines;",""],[1,"79","11","Health Education and Public Awareness Campaigns","Increasing health-related education and dissemination programs, aimed at raising people's awareness and proper conducts in the prevention and management of diseases or public health problems, as well as ensuring proper behaviors of the people in seeking and using health care services.",""],[1,"79","12","Medical Profession Training Quality Improvement","Improving the training quality of medical professions, as well as supporting professions based on competencies, promoting professional ethics, and making a push for extensive deployment of medical doctors and staff in accordance with technical standards.",""],[1,"80","1","Health Infrastructure Expansion and Medical Supply Strengthening","Expanding physical infrastructures; and strengthening the supply of medicines and equipment, supply of medical equipment to health posts, health centers, referral hospitals, priority referral hospitals of target provinces and national hospitals in accordance with modern technical standards.",""],[1,"80","2","Multi-sectoral Health Service Delivery Coordination","Enhancing multi-sectoral and inter-sectoral cooperation, community participation, and responsibilities of sub-national administrations, to ensure the deliveries of health care services that meet the essential health needs of the local population.",""],[1,"80","6","Primary Health Care-Oriented Service Delivery Model","Ensure universal, comprehensive access to health care provided by public and private health facilities by innovating a high-quality, primary health care-oriented service delivery model;",""],[1,"80","6","Health Literacy and Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","raise health literacy and create enabling environments for individuals, families, and communities to adopt healthy lifestyles and appropriately use health services;",""],[1,"80","6","Health Service Coverage Expansion","develop and expand service coverage;",""],[1,"80","6","Community Participation in Health Service Monitoring","promote community participation in service development, monitoring, and evaluation;",""],[1,"80","6","Multisectoral Health Collaboration Mechanism","strengthen multidisciplinary and multisectoral collaboration, including with the private sector, to improve environmental, social, and economic determinants of health and advance priority interventions",""],[1,"80","7","Health Care Quality Improvement and Patient Safety Programme","Provide health care services at public and private facilities in line with high quality standards by organizing patient and client flow within facilities, enhancing the safety of patients, clients, and providers throughout the care process, strengthening clinical pathway-based care including upgrading diagnostic and treatment knowledge and skills, institutionalizing continuous quality improvement, reinforcing adherence to clinical practice guidelines, and implementing priority interventions",""]],"27":[[1,"79","8","Health Sector Digital Governance and Regulatory Strengthening","Strengthening institutional capacity to lead digital governance and transformation in health sector; formulating health-related laws and regulations; promoting the implementation of regulatory mechanisms over public and private health care services; promoting medical research; and strengthening monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"80","8","Universal Health Coverage and Health Financing Reform","Ensure universal access to quality, safe, effective, and timely health services through social health protection, sustainable and equitable health financing, innovation in provider payment systems, pooling of funds, and strengthened health financing governance",""],[1,"80","10","Health System Foundational Infrastructure Investment","Invest in the foundational infrastructure of the health system to expand service delivery capacity and modernize the system, focusing on: (1) institutional capacity development and health governance, (2) human resources for health, (3) high performing public financial management, (4) supply chain management for medicines, consumables, medical equipment, and technologies together with expansion and upgrading of physical infrastructure, and (5) data systems, health information management, and digitalization in the health sector.",""]],"28":[[1,"80","9","Health System Preparedness and Health Security Strengthening","Strengthen the health system to be robust, responsive, and timely in addressing all forms of public health threats and health emergencies by enhancing preparedness and response capacities, advancing One Health risk prevention and management, upgrading medical laboratory capacity and safe, high quality blood services, and reinforcing cooperation and governance for health security",""]],"29":[[1,"109","7","Youth Reproductive and Sexual Health Services Expansion","Continuing to strengthen and expand the scope of reproductive and sexual health services for young people, especially women and girls;",""],[1,"109","7","Social Protection for Pregnant Women and Children in Poor Families","continuing to implement social protection programs for pregnant women and children in poor families;",""],[1,"109","7","Maternal and Child Nutrition Promotion","and continuing to promote nutrition for pregnant women and children.",""],[1,"111","11","Micronutrient Food Fortification Training for Education Personnel","Organize training for education personnel at national and subnational levels on techniques for micronutrient fortification of foods",""],[1,"112","2","Implementation Coordination of the Cambodia Strategic Framework 2024-2030","Promote and coordinate implementation of the Cambodia Strategic Framework 2024-2030 to realize the program of action of the international conference on population and development",""]],"30":[[1,"119","12","Coordinated Food Safety Risk Management","Enhance food safety through coordinated risk management approaches, leveraging food inspection systems",""],[1,"119","13","Capital-Provincial Coordination Teams for Food Security and Nutrition","Support the implementation of policies and plans via the capital-provincial level leading coordination teams for the food security and nutrition sector, as well as provincial core teams for coordinating interventions in nutrition-sensitive clean water supply and sanitation services",""]],"31":[[1,"20","3","Gender Mainstreaming and Women's Economic Empowerment Initiatives","Gender equality and the role of women have been continuously promoted through institutionalization, the dissemination of gender concepts and the CEDAW Convention, and gender mainstreaming in ministries and institutions at both the national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"20","3","Women's Entrepreneurship and Digital-Green MSME Support","Empowering women in the economic sector has received specific attention through initiatives such as developing female entrepreneurship, supporting women who lead and manage micro, small, and medium- sized enterprises-particularly in the digital and green economies-enhancing knowledge and skills, and implementing measures for financial and digital inclusion.",""],[1,"20","3","Protection of Women's Rights in Formal and Informal Employment","These efforts have also focused on promoting women's household economies and well-being-oriented economic activities, as well as protecting the rights of women engaged in both formal and informal economic sectors.",""],[1,"35","3","Legal Services and Violence Response for Women and Girls","The Royal Government provides legal services to women victims of violence, continues to intervene in and respond to violence against women and girls, and promotes gender mainstreaming in ministries and institutions.",""],[1,"35","3","Gender Mainstreaming in Ministries and Institutions","The Royal Government provides legal services to women victims of violence, continues to intervene in and respond to violence against women and girls, and promotes gender mainstreaming in ministries and institutions.",""]],"32":[[1,"71","16","Comprehensive Social Protection System Development","Promote the development of a comprehensive, coherent social protection system with broad coverage across both the public and private sectors, focusing on governance and",""],[1,"72","5","National Social Assistance Program","Prepare and implement a comprehensive National Social Assistance Program as an integrated family package, and continue to organize and strengthen the social service workforce within the social assistance framework to ensure broad coverage, strong delivery capacity, and effective provision of social assistance",""],[1,"72","6","National Social Assistance Fund Governance Strengthening","Strengthen the governance of the National Social Assistance Fund to make it more robust and effective by modernizing information management systems, enhancing administrative efficiency, developing human resources, deepening partnerships with ministries-institutions, banks, and development partners, and improving budget, financial management, accounting, audit, and oversight of social protection program implementation.",""],[1,"81","3","Centralized and Consistent Social Protection System Development","The strategic objectives are to build and develop centralized and consistent social protection system, both the social assistance system and the social security system,",""],[1,"81","3","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation for Priority Programs","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature,",""],[1,"81","4","National Social Assistance and Livelihood Support Program","Continuing to provide livelihood support to target households through the national social assistance program",""],[1,"81","4","Family Package Social Assistance Expansion","with immediate actions focusing on the national social assistance program as a family package",""],[1,"81","4","Youth Empowerment Programme","as well as their empowerment",""],[1,"81","4","Social Protection Poverty Reduction Programme","and social protection programs to end poverty",""],[1,"81","4","Emergency-Responsive Social Protection Frameworks","institutionalizing social protection frameworks that can respond to emergencies",""],[1,"81","5","Social Security System Development and Social Health Care Expansion","Continuing to develop the social security system, the implementation of the social security schemes, and the continued expansion of social health care services towards universal health coverage (UHC) in line with the evolving socio-economic situation.",""],[1,"81","6","Governance System Strengthening for Social Protection","Continuing to strengthen governance system to make it more robust, effective, and standardized in all three levels, namely the policy level (National Social Protection Council), the regulatory level (Social Security Regulator), and the operational level (National Social Security Fund, National Social Assistance Fund and other relevant operators).",""],[1,"81","7","National Agency for Payment Certification","Launching an independent National Agency for Payment Certification, which covers healthcare and occupational risks.",""],[1,"81","8","Digital Social Protection Identification and Registration System","Promoting the use of information technology within the system; and continuing to enhance and improve the accuracy of the identification system for target households and individuals who are eligible for social protection schemes, with the aim of launching a basic system for registration and national social data.",""],[1,"81","9","Social Protection Awareness and Feedback Mechanisms","Promoting awareness on the important roles of the social protection system, and establishing mechanisms for feedback and suggestions, and mechanisms for monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"81","10","Social Protection and Land Concession Support for Affected Families","Promoting and improving the well-being of the poor families, families of militants with disabilities, families of deceased militants, and families of veterans, by providing various protections, including the continued granting of land, and provision of social land concessions for housing and agriculture purposes.",""],[1,"82","6","Social Protection Pathways Out of Poverty","social protection measures to support pathways out of poverty",""],[1,"82","6","Bridging Programs Linking Social Services to Poor Households","development of bridging programs connecting social services to poor households",""],[1,"82","6","Public Outreach on the Social Protection System","strengthened public outreach on the importance and role of the social protection system",""],[1,"82","6","Social Protection Service Delivery and Policy Framework Improvement","improvements to service delivery modalities and policy frameworks",""],[1,"82","9","Household Identification and Social Assistance Data Strengthening","Continue to strengthen the identification of poor and vulnerable households to provide timely, high-quality data for national social assistance programs and social security schemes",""]],"33":[[1,"109","1","Pension Branch Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Establish and strengthen monitoring and evaluation mechanisms for the pension branch of the social security system, in compliance with international standards",""],[1,"109","1","Civil Service Pension Scheme Reform and Management Plan","pursue reforms to the public-sector pension scheme by developing a management plan for the civil service pension system",""],[1,"109","2","Internal Training for Officials on Financial Risk Assessment","Continue developing institutional capacity through internal training for officials, with a particular emphasis on financial risk assessment",""],[1,"109","3","Informal Sector Pension Scheme","Expand social security coverage to individuals in the informal economy by designing and establishing a pension scheme tailored to the informal sector",""],[1,"109","4","Public Awareness on the Social Security System","Enhance public awareness, with a focus on education about the social security system.",""],[1,"109","5","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"109","8","Elderly Financial Security and Savings Mechanism","Establishing mechanism and savings plans to reduce the risk of financial insecurity for the elderly and to promote investment in the elderly.",""]],"34":[[1,"19","2","Health Equity Fund and Healthcare Social Security Scheme","the implementation of the Health Equity Fund and the social security scheme for healthcare",""],[1,"19","2","Expansion of Social Security Schemes","the expansion of social security schemes",""],[1,"19","2","Contribution-Based Pension Scheme Introduction","the introduction of mandatory and voluntary contribution-based pension schemes",""],[1,"19","2","Financial Support for Pregnant Members and Young Children","the provision of financial support to pregnant members of the National Social Security Fund and children under two years old as well as to women who give birth",""],[1,"19","2","Cash Support for Poor and Vulnerable Citizens","the implementation of cash support programs for poor and vulnerable citizens, for pregnant women and children under two, and for at-risk families during periods of inflationary pressure",""],[1,"20","6","National Social Protection Policy Framework","This is being done through the National Social Protection Policy Framework, which aims to build a Cambodian social protection system comprising social assistance and social security schemes.",""],[1,"20","6","Social Security Regulatory Body","Other key measures include the creation of a Social Security Regulatory Body and a National Social Assistance Fund, adjusting",""],[1,"20","6","National Social Assistance Fund","Other key measures include the creation of a Social Security Regulatory Body and a National Social Assistance Fund, adjusting",""],[1,"21","1","Social Assistance Program Expansion","The Royal Government is implementing social assistance programs that are entirely state-funded",""],[1,"21","3","Expanded Social Security Scheme","the Royal Government is implementing a scheme with an increasingly broad scope in line with socio-economic developments to support and protect citizens from income insecurity due to illness, maternity leave, work-related accidents, inactivity, and old age",""],[1,"21","3","Cash Support for Pregnant Women and Children","the Royal Government has implemented and expanded the cash support program for pregnant women and children under two years old for female members of the National Social Security Fund",""],[1,"34","1","Program for Families","Program for Families, which was created in April 2024 and integrates four existing programs: cash assistance for pregnant women and children under two, scholarships for poor students, cash assistance for people with disabilities, and cash assistance for the elderly, along with basic support for all poor families and assistance for members with HIV/AIDS;",""],[1,"34","1","Health Equity Fund Expansion","the expansion of the Health Equity Fund to cover vulnerable households;",""],[1,"51","10","Integrated Social Protection System Development","to develop and build an integrated and consistent social protection system",""],[1,"51","10","Cost of Living Reduction Measures","to reduce the living costs for the people",""],[1,"51","10","Inclusive Public Services Improvement","to provide quality, efficient, and inclusive public services",""],[1,"144","2","Basic Subsidies for Pregnant Women with Equity Cards","Pregnant women, from households hold equity cards, receive basic subsidies from the National Social Assistance Program",""],[1,"144","3","Basic Subsidies for Equity Card Holders","Elders, from households holding equity cards, receive basic subsidies from the National Social Assistance Program",""],[1,"144","4","Basic Subsidies for People with Disabilities and Equity Card Households","People with disabilities, from households with equity cards, receive basic subsidies from the National Social Assistance Program",""],[1,"144","5","Basic Subsidies for Equity Card Holders in Primary and Lower-Secondary Schools","Primary and lower-secondary school students, from households holde equity cards, receive basic subsidies from the National Social Assistance Program",""]],"35":[[1,"82","4","Social Welfare Services Expansion","Enhance social welfare services by expanding support for older persons and veterans, strengthening child protection services and monitoring of children's rights, promoting family services, and scaling up victim support services",""],[1,"82","5","Victim Rehabilitation and Social Welfare Service Strengthening","Strengthen management of victim rehabilitation services, including juvenile justice rehabilitation, treatment and rehabilitation for people with drug dependence, promotion of the well-being of persons with disabilities, professionalization of social work, expansion of vocational rehabilitation and labor reintegration for persons with disabilities, enhanced monitoring of disability-rights implementation, and effective mobilization and use of social welfare funds to ensure equitable, inclusive, and sustainable service delivery",""],[1,"82","6","Emergency Social Assistance for Disaster-Affected Households","Reinforce implementation of social protection programs through emergency social assistance for households affected by disasters",""],[1,"82","7","Social Service Workforce Capacity and Accreditation Programme","Strengthen institutional development and general support services by building institutional capacity and good governance, developing the social service workforce, advancing social welfare policy, and establishing and accrediting the social service workforce to ensure effective delivery of social assistance and services, while continuing implementation of the Cambodia social service workforce strategic Plan 2022-2031.",""],[1,"82","10","Poverty and Vulnerability Grievance Redress System Enhancement","Enhance transparency and accountability in poverty and vulnerability identification through accessible grievance redress, feedback, and appeals mechanisms, simplifying and streamlining procedures while safeguarding confidentiality, and expanding multiple submission channels, including in-person at commune/sangkat offices and via smartphone applications, moving toward harmonization of the grievance and feedback system grounded in inclusiveness and equity",""]],"36":[[1,"82","2","Targeted Population Social Health Protection Expansion","Ministry of Health shall prioritize targeted population approaches to advance universal social health protection, emphasizing expanded coverage for all individuals, including migrant populations, strengthening the implementation of social health protection mechanisms, integrating informal-economy workers into the social protection system through formalization, and establishing a sustainable health financing architecture to achieve universal health coverage.","Ministry of Health"],[1,"83","1","Expansion and Harmonization of Social Security Regimes","Strengthen and expand the implementation of social security regimes in line with socio- economic developments by increasing registration of institutions, enterprises, and establishments to extend coverage to additional target groups under the mandatory contributory scheme, increasing registration of National Social Security Fund (NSSF) members under the voluntary contributory scheme, supporting effective implementation of the Health Equity Fund, cooperating to review and amend normative legal documents for registration and advance harmonization of registration under a single unified system, developing and revising normative legal documents and promoting international consultations to enable portability of social security benefits, and assessing the feasibility of establishing and operationalizing an unemployment insurance scheme",""],[1,"83","2","Social Security Service Delivery Improvement Programme","Improve the quality and capacity of social security service delivery by enhancing the quality and efficiency of services provided by contracted health facilities, conducting assessments and feasibility reviews to adjust benefit-package unit costs in line with health- market conditions, identifying preventive health services and occupational diseases, strengthening claims and payment services and expanding service delivery modalities for social security schemes, enhancing rehabilitation services, and exploring partnerships with technical and vocational training providers and public employment service agencies",""],[1,"83","3","Social Security Law Awareness and Enforcement Strengthening","Promote awareness and strengthen enforcement of the Law on Social Security Regimes by enhancing customer information and grievance services, scaling up education and outreach on social security, improving education and communication on well-being, occupational risk prevention, and financial management, studying and arranging appropriate commuting options for workers, and reinforcing compliance with laws and normative legal documents through integration of a unified inspectorate system and action by social security inspectors",""],[1,"83","4","Social Security Fund Management and Investment Strengthening","Strengthen the management and administration of social security funds to increase value for NSSF members and related professional sectors by reinforcing contribution collection, inspection, monitoring, and measures to improve financial, budgetary, and accounting management, and by studying, monitoring, and evaluating financial risk to safeguard members' interests, while strengthening fund investment through investment plans aligned with social security fund investment guidelines and robust monitoring, supervision, evaluation, and risk management",""],[1,"83","5","NSSF Institutional Capacity Strengthening Programme","Build the institutional capacity of the NSSF by reviewing and revising normative legal documents for internal management, upgrading organizational infrastructure, developing human resources, establishing mechanisms and a knowledge-management plan, contributing to the formulation, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of policies, strategies, and international instruments, expanding national and international cooperation to mobilize resources, and modernizing information-technology systems to enhance service delivery and institutional management.",""]],"37":[[1,"86","5","Positive Parenting Strategy Implementation","Promote education and empowerment of women and girls to develop high-quality human capital and capable agents of change with strong ethics, knowledge, and skills, while fostering harmony within families and society, through implementation of the Positive Parenting Strategy and well-being-oriented economic empowerment programs, including establishing workplace and community childcare centers and creating lactation rooms",""],[1,"86","5","Well-being-Oriented Economic Empowerment Programs for Women and Girls","Promote education and empowerment of women and girls to develop high-quality human capital and capable agents of change with strong ethics, knowledge, and skills, while fostering harmony within families and society, through implementation of the Positive Parenting Strategy and well-being-oriented economic empowerment programs, including establishing workplace and community childcare centers and creating lactation rooms",""],[1,"86","5","Workplace and Community Childcare and Lactation Facilities","including establishing workplace and community childcare centers and creating lactation rooms",""]],"38":[[1,"110","18","Gender-Based Violence Prevention Legal Framework Implementation","Develop and promote the implementation of legal frameworks, policies, and normative legal documents related to the prevention of gender-based violence and the sexual exploitation of women and girls",""],[1,"111","1","National Action Plan to Prevent Violence Against Women Implementation Support","Prepare, coordinate, support, and drive implementation of the national action plan to prevent violence against women 2024-2030",""],[1,"111","1","Plans Addressing Exploitation and Drug Use","along with national, regional, and subregional plans addressing exploitation and drug use",""],[1,"111","1","Multisectoral Survivor Service-Response Mechanisms","multisectoral service-response mechanisms for survivors at national and subnational levels",""],[1,"111","2","Violence Against Women and Girls Case Management and One-Stop Service Room SOP Implementation","Strengthen case management for violence against women and girls, and reinforce implementation of standard operating procedures for one-stop service rooms at referral hospitals and health centers",""],[1,"111","3","Violence Against Women and Girls Prevention and Survivor Support Programme","Strengthen and expand capacity-building programs and prevention campaigns on violence against women and girls, including digital initiatives, to prevent and respond effectively and to deliver survivor support services for gender-based violence",""],[1,"111","4","Child Marriage and Adolescent Pregnancy Prevention Action Plan Implementation Support","Prepare, coordinate, support, and promote implementation of the action plan to prevent child marriage and adolescent pregnancy.",""]],"39":[[1,"91","2","Road Weight Limit Study and Transport Law Reform","Carrying out a study on roads and amending the law on roads, in order to make adjustments to the maximum weight level; and speeding up the preparation of law on land transport, law on water transport and seaports, and law on railway; as well as formulating policies, strategies, and legal frameworks related to the law enforcement and promotion of logistic skills development.",""],[1,"92","2","Ministerial Monitoring and Evaluation of Action Plans and Indicators","coordinating monitoring, inspection, and evaluation of ministerial and institutional action plans and indicators;",""],[1,"122","5","Transport and Logistics Legal and Policy Reform Programme","Ministry of Public Works and Transport shall continue to advance reforms, prepare draft laws, and implement relevant policies and normative legal instruments","Ministry of Public Works and Transport"]],"40":[[1,"92","3","Air Transport Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Strengthen the air transport economy by reinforcing implementation of the regulatory framework to improve economic efficiency, expand consumer benefits and choice, create business opportunities in the air-transport market, and widen Cambodia's domestic, regional, and global air connectivity",""],[1,"92","4","Aviation Safety and Public Order Enhancement","Enhance safety, maintain public order, and ensure safe aviation operations, strengthening management effectiveness and public confidence in air transport in line with international standards",""],[1,"92","5","Civil Aviation Security Reinforcement","Reinforce security through rigorous application of civil aviation security measures consistent with national and international standards, to protect against, prevent, and counter all unlawful acts, including bombing, terrorism, sabotage, and threats to life and property",""],[1,"92","6","Air Navigation Services and Infrastructure Upgrade","Improve air navigation efficiency by upgrading air navigation services to ensure high safety and service reliability, and by developing air navigation system infrastructure in accordance with international standards",""],[1,"92","7","Civil Aviation Operations and Services Modernization","Manage civil aviation operations and services by strengthening air-transport support services and preparing for digital transformation through automation and digitalization, to raise operational efficiency and service quality across the civil aviation sector",""],[1,"92","8","Airport Infrastructure Expansion and Environmental Performance Improvement","Develop infrastructure and advance environmental protection by expanding airport facilities commensurate with growth in passenger and air-cargo volumes, ensuring safe, economically efficient operations and better environmental performance for travel, cargo handling, and aircraft movements",""],[1,"92","9","Civil Aviation International Cooperation and Policy Harmonization","Strengthen international cooperation by expanding national and international partnerships in civil aviation and harmonizing policies and development roadmaps at subregional, regional, and global levels",""],[1,"92","10","High-Quality Training for Officials","Develop human resources and institutional capacity through high-quality training for officials to meet sector requirements and align with Royal Government guidance.",""]],"41":[[1,"117","11","Rural Development Strategy Implementation through Physical Infrastructure and Rural Roads","Continuing the implementation of Rural Development Strategy through the development of physical infrastructure and rural roads; improving the quality of rural road infrastructure,",""],[1,"118","1","Rural Road Construction and Rural Connectivity Improvement","especially the construction of rural roads that are connected with farms and national roads to transform the areas into integrated rural areas;",""],[1,"118","1","Rural Community Development and Livelihood Diversification Initiative","improving living conditions of rural communities; and diversifying rural economy and fostering rural community development, especially promoting multifaceted development and continued promotion of the \"One Village, One Product Movement\" and \" Role Model Village Movement\".",""],[1,"118","9","Resilient Rural Infrastructure Development Programme","Develop resilient rural physical and communications infrastructure by expanding rural road infrastructure and conducting technology research to strengthen the resilience of core infrastructure systems",""],[1,"118","10","Rural Community Development and Model Village Programme","Promote rural community development and the Model Village movement by improving the effectiveness of community development activities, enhancing quality, value, and innovation in rural communities, advancing digital technologies for rural communities, and supporting the development and cultural preservation of indigenous peoples.",""]],"42":[[1,"21","5","Logistics System Development and Intermodal Transport Transformation","This work is ongoing, with a focus on developing the logistics system and transforming it into an intermodal transport system to serve",""],[1,"22","2","Port Infrastructure Development and Modernization","Moreover, the government is continuing to develop, expand, and modernize port infrastructure, especially the waterway navigation and logistics system project connecting the Bassac River to the sea in Kep province.",""],[1,"22","3","High-Speed Rail Upgrade and Expansion Studies","Furthermore, the Royal Government is studying projects to upgrade the existing railway lines-Phnom Penh-Poipet and Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville-into high-speed rail systems.",""],[1,"22","3","New High-Speed Rail Corridor Studies","It is also studying new high-speed rail lines, including one from Phnom Penh to Siem Reap and Poipet, a line connecting Phnom Penh to Bavet City, and other new high-speed lines to connect with Thailand and Laos.",""],[1,"22","3","Underground Railway and Light Rail Feasibility Studies","It is also studying the feasibility of constructing an underground railway in Phnom Penh to connect the new Techo Takhmao Airport to Phnom Penh city and a light rail line connecting the new Siem Reap Airport to Siem Reap city.",""],[1,"22","5","Civil Aviation Infrastructure Development and Airport Expansion Programme","Infrastructure in the civil aviation sector has been developed and improved, with Cambodia building and restoring a total of 11 domestic and international airports, including 1) the new Phnom Penh International Airport (Techo International Airport), 2) a large-scale 4F-class international airport; the new Siem Reap International Airport, a 4E-class international airport; 2) the Dara Sakor International Airport; 4) the upgraded Sihanoukville International Airport, where major infrastructure and facilities have been expanded; and 5) seven other secondary airports are being built or restored-namely Poipet, Koh Rong, Koh Kong, Mondulkiri, Battambang, Kampong Chhnang, and Stung Treng airports-alongside the construction of an Aeronautical Meteorological Information Center to further strengthen Cambodia's aviation infrastructure.",""],[1,"34","4","Funan Techo Canal Project","the Funan Techo Canal project is currently underway",""],[1,"55","5","Implementation of Existing Industrial, Automotive, Logistics, and Coastal Development Strategies","Priority is being given to implementing policies and strategies such as the \"Industrial Development Policy 2015- 2025,\" the \"Cambodia Automotive and Electronics Industry Development Roadmap,\" the \"Master Plan for Sihanoukville Province as a Multi-purpose Special Economic Zone and the Coastal Provinces' Economic Development Plan,\" and the \"Comprehensive Intermodal Transport and Logistics System Master Plan 2023-2033\".",""],[1,"90","9","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"90","9","Supportive Infrastructure Efficiency Enhancement","The strategic objectives are to continue to build and strengthen the foundation and key prerequisites to increase productivity, enhance competitiveness, and accelerate diversification through enhancing efficiency of supportive infrastructures, and construction and development of new infrastructures.",""],[1,"90","9","New Infrastructure Construction and Development","The strategic objectives are to continue to build and strengthen the foundation and key prerequisites to increase productivity, enhance competitiveness, and accelerate diversification through enhancing efficiency of supportive infrastructures, and construction and development of new infrastructures.",""],[1,"90","10","Intermodal Transport Connectivity and Logistics Master Plan Implementation","Continuing to encourage the implementation of Interim Master Plan on Intermodal Transport Connectivity and Logistics System 2021-2030, as well as making a push for the endorsement and the implementation of the Comprehensive Master Plan on Cambodia Intermodal Transport and Logistics System 2023-2030.",""],[1,"90","12","Capital Investment and Financing Mobilization for Key Physical Infrastructure","Continuing to increase capital investments and mobilization of financing, as well as strengthening the efficiency of their utilization to continue to develop key physical infrastructures, namely roads, railways, waterway, ports, and airways, especially navigation projects and logistics systems, project on modernization of Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville railway network; and Poipet-Siem Reap-Phnom Penh new railway network, as well as",""],[1,"91","1","Expressway Development for Economic Corridors","considering the development of more expressways connecting important economic poles and domestic key economic corridors to the neighboring countries.",""],[1,"91","13","Transport Infrastructure Management Modernization","Enhance transport services and the use of modern and digital technologies by modernizing road-asset and transport-infrastructure management systems, using high-quality construction materials for construction, rehabilitation, and maintenance, improving management of all transport modes, expanding dissemination of and access to the Road Traffic Law, the Law",""],[1,"92","1","Transport Infrastructure Laboratory Equipment and Digital Transformation","deploying and regularly updating advanced laboratory equipment for training, research, construction, rehabilitation, and maintenance of transport infrastructure, and continuing digital transformation to improve service delivery, vehicle and transport management, and the monitoring and supervision of infrastructure projects",""],[1,"92","2","Integrated Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Development","Develop physical infrastructure, multimodal connectivity, and logistics by advancing implementation of the Cambodia Intermodal Transport and Logistics System Master Plan 2023-2033, preparing a Waterway Transport Master Plan, updating the Railway Master Plan, and continuing maintenance, rehabilitation, and modernization of railway infrastructure and services;",""],[1,"92","2","International Transport Agreement Implementation and Cross-Border Facilitation","continuing implementation of relevant international conventions and multilateral and bilateral agreements to strengthen infrastructure management and facilitate cross- border transport;",""],[1,"92","2","Funan Techo Canal Construction Project","accelerating implementation of the Funan Techo Canal construction project.",""],[1,"97","7","Goods Transport and Logistics Infrastructure Development","Contribute to infrastructure development to improve the efficiency of goods transport and logistics between SEZs and national or international seaports and border checkpoints",""]],"43":[[1,"29","1","Implementation of the National Mineral Resources Policy","During the 6th legislature of the National Assembly, the Royal Government of Cambodia strengthened the implementation of the National Mineral Resources Policy 2018-2028 to optimize these important resources for national benefit and maintain a balance between development and conservation.",""],[1,"29","1","Mineral Sector Governance and Illegal Mining Suppression","The government has also improved governance and resource management by almost completely eliminating illegal mining activities nationwide and has enhanced the efficiency of national revenue collection, with non-tax revenue from the mining sector reaching approximately $177.2 million.",""],[1,"29","1","Mineral Fund Community Development Project","It has also implemented a mineral fund project to support the development of 58 local communities in 13 provinces and is managing mining operations to ensure the sustainable supply of mineral products by adhering to all legal and regulatory guidelines.",""],[1,"112","5","Implementation of the National Policy on Mineral Resources","Continuing to promote the implementation of the \"National Policy on Mineral Resources 2018-2028\" by continuing to promote investments in extractive industries and supporting industries; mapping and demarcation of potential areas with mineral and oil resources and re- operationalization of oil wells; optimization of national revenue collections; enhancing governance in resource management and mining; increasing community participation, improving the livelihoods of local communities, and minimizing environmental and social impacts; and strengthening sand conservation and management mechanisms by minimizing social and environmental impacts, especially riverbank collapses.",""],[1,"115","1","Geoscientific Mineral Resource Assessment and Licensing Zoning Plan","Conduct geoscientific research and compile mineral resource data to underpin assessments of the economic potential of mineral resources for investment promotion, and prepare a strategic plan to designate licensing areas for mineral resources and identify potential zones for minerals, construction stone, and construction sand",""],[1,"115","2","Mineral Operations and Development Potential Mapping","Develop maps showing locations of mineral operations and areas with potential for mineral development to facilitate investors in the mining sector",""],[1,"115","3","Mining Site Health and Safety Compliance Modernization","Continue to update, modernize, and strengthen compliance with normative legal documents related to health and safety at mining sites",""],[1,"115","4","Online Mining License and Non-Tax Revenue Management System","Establish an information technology system for online management of licenses and non- tax revenue from the mining sector, including electronic filing and payment of financial obligations related to mineral operations",""],[1,"115","5","Mineral Resource Management and Inspection Strengthening","Continue strengthening the management and inspection of mineral resource operations, and cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to enhance revenue mobilization and prevent national revenue leakage from the mining sector","relevant ministries and institutions"],[1,"115","6","Community Benefit-Sharing and Local Economic Opportunity Enhancement in Mining Areas","Enhance community benefit-sharing and local economic opportunities in mining areas through capacity building and the use of local goods, services, and labor",""],[1,"115","7","Mineral Fund Support for Local Community Development","Continue promoting the use of the Mineral Fund to support local community development in areas with mineral operations",""]],"44":[[1,"47","12","Peace Dividend for Macroeconomic Stability and Private Investment","The peace dividend will provide advantages for economic and social development by continuing to create an indispensable and favorable environment for maintaining macroeconomic stability, and promoting private investment and business, that are the backbones of economic growth and job creation",""],[1,"51","8","Economic Diversification and Competitiveness Promotion","accelerating the diversification of economic; promoting competitiveness;",""],[1,"51","9","Investment Climate Improvement Measures","and making the investment climate more attractive to investors",""],[1,"51","11","Business, Investment, and Trade Enabling Environment Promotion","continuing to promote a favorable environment for business, investment, and trade.",""],[1,"52","3","Economic Diversification and Competitiveness Enhancement Package","Economic diversification and competitiveness enhancement by focusing on development of key sectors and new sources of economic growth; enhancement of connectivity and efficiency in transport and logistics, energy, water supply and digital sectors; improvements of business and investment environment; strengthening of efficiency and attractiveness of special economic zones (SEZs), including industrial parks, agro-industrial parks, and domestic free-trade zones; and innovation of financing mechanisms and financial products to support investment.",""],[1,"54","7","Investment Attraction and Investor Facilitation Policy","the government has identified investment attraction policies as a critical opportunity to drive economic growth.",""],[1,"54","8","Quality Investment Attraction Policy","Investment attraction policies must focus on attracting quality investments with high added value and allowing Cambodia to integrate into regional and global value chains, aiming to create decent and quality jobs for Cambodian people.",""],[1,"54","8","Special Economic Zone Development","In this endeavor, special economic zones (SEZs) will continue to play a key role in promoting industrial and economic diversification.",""],[1,"54","8","Public-Private Dialogue Mechanism","the Royal Government has been continuing to implement public-private dialogue mechanisms to guide the development of the private sector and address all challenges faced by investors and businesspeople, aiming to ensure the success and growth of private sector business operations in Cambodia.",""],[1,"55","2","Compliance Cost Reduction for Investment and Business","Efforts are being made to reduce compliance costs for investments and businesses by ensuring fairness, convenience, and the avoidance of unnecessary interference for investors while maintaining compliance with policies and legal regulations",""]],"45":[[1,"73","12","Economic Diplomacy for Trade, Investment, and Market Diversification","Deploy economic diplomacy to strengthen and broaden economic ties with foreign partners and to leverage multilateral cooperation, including mobilizing foreign direct investment, attracting international tourist arrivals, and promoting market diversification to expand Cambodia's exports.",""],[1,"73","12","Cultural Diplomacy and Soft Power Promotion","Continue cultural diplomacy by promoting Cambodia's culture, heritage, arts, and cuisine, in order to build soft power and enhance Cambodia's recognition on the international stage.",""],[1,"74","5","Export Market Diversification and E-Commerce Trade Negotiation","Continuing to negotiate, through both bilateral and multilateral mechanisms, to open new potential markets which can be elevated to more comprehensive and to a new height; and undertaking negotiation of international agreements related to e-commerce by focusing particularly on bilateral agreements that are found to be effective with high potentials to diversify export markets and products.",""],[1,"74","6","Strategy and Action Plan for Deeper International Integration","Developing strategies and action plans to deepen Cambodia's integration through existing multilateral and bilateral mechanisms to intensively expand Cambodia's linkages with regional and global value and supply chains.",""],[1,"74","7","Trade Cost Reduction and Trade Barrier Removal Measures","Developing policy measures to reduce trade costs and related costs and eliminate unnecessary trade barriers to increase Cambodia's competitiveness",""],[1,"74","7","SME Standards and Regulatory Compliance Promotion","the development and the promotion of compliance to standards and regulations by micro, small, and medium enterprises, especially young and new industries with high exports and competitiveness potentials",""],[1,"74","8","International Cooperation and Multilateral Trading System Participation","Continuing to promote Cambodia's active participation in major international cooperation frameworks and initiatives, and in the promotion of a global multilateral trading system, based on the principles of openness, transparency, inclusiveness, and fair competition.",""],[1,"74","9","Inter-Ministerial and Stakeholder Coordination for Competitiveness","Strengthening and expanding cooperation and coordination between ministries, public institutions, and all other development stakeholders to enhance competitiveness and industrial and commercial capacity in line with regional and global trends, especially linking domestic production to international product markets.",""],[1,"74","10","LDC Graduation and Economic Integration Policy Frameworks","Formulating strategic frameworks for a smooth graduation with momentum from the Least Developed Countries, and formulating orientation policy frameworks for long-term strategic economic integration, while continuing to negotiate for other trade preferences during the transition period to ensure export market stability and new market accesses for Cambodian products.",""],[1,"74","13","Trade Market Integration and Expansion","Continue integrating Cambodia's economy into subregional, regional, and global markets by consolidating existing markets and expanding into new ones through trade partnerships",""],[1,"75","1","Trade Agreement Implementation and Negotiation Initiative","effectively implement existing bilateral and multilateral trade agreements and pursue negotiations for additional agreements",""],[1,"75","1","Cross-Border Trade Facilitation","by facilitating cross- border trade with neighboring countries and other international trading partners, in order to improve the trade balance",""],[1,"75","2","WTO Compliance and Trade Policy Reform Programme","Continue fulfilling the Royal Government's obligations under the World Trade Organization framework by preparing laws and normative legal documents, advancing trade policy and regulatory reforms, and strengthening implementation mechanisms in line with relevant international agreements and instruments",""],[1,"75","3","Trade Competitiveness and Market Diversification Strategy","Contribute to the implementation of the graduation strategy from least developed country status by enhancing trade competitiveness, diversifying markets and products, improving product quality, and fostering the development of new products to meet market demand and requirements;",""],[1,"75","3","Implementation of Existing Free Trade Agreements","continue promoting the implementation of existing free trade agreements to offset the potential loss of preferential schemes after graduation",""],[1,"75","3","Cambodia Trade Sector Policy Framework Development","advance the establishment of a policy framework for Cambodia's trade sector development.",""],[1,"75","6","ASEAN Market Access Negotiation Participation","Continue participating in negotiations to upgrade market-access commitments under ASEAN frameworks, including ASEAN and the ASEAN-Japan Comprehensive Economic Partnership, and pursue additional market-opening negotiations within ASEAN",""],[1,"87","3","Free Trade Agreement Establishment and Implementation","Continuing to make a push for the establishment and implementation of free trade agreements-either bilateral, multilateral, or regional-to its highest efficiency, particularly strengthening inter-institutional coordination.",""],[1,"88","6","Free Trade Agreement Negotiation and Implementation Programme","Ministry of Commerce shall continue advancing the development of key sectors and new drivers of economic growth by promoting the conclusion and effective implementation of bilateral, multilateral, regional, and subregional free trade agreements","Ministry of Commerce"]],"46":[[1,"75","5","Bilateral Investment Promotion and Protection Agreements","Assess the feasibility of concluding reciprocal Memoranda of Understanding on investment promotion and, where appropriate, agreements on the promotion and protection of investments between Cambodia and new partner countries, to create favorable conditions for bilateral investment",""],[1,"75","7","ASEAN Investment Engagement and Forum Participation","Continue engaging in ASEAN investment-related initiatives, including contributing to the annual ASEAN Investment Report and organizing the ASEAN Investment Forum, in cooperation with relevant international institutions",""],[1,"75","8","Country Strategy for Investment Attraction and Facilitation","Contribute to the development of a country strategy to attract and facilitate investment by leading firms, as set out in the Cambodia Automotive and Electronics Sector Development Roadmap",""],[1,"75","9","Implementation of Investment Protection Agreements","Strengthen the implementation of bilateral investment protection agreements and effectively implement relevant bilateral and multilateral investment agreements and memoranda of understanding",""],[1,"75","10","Sustainable Development Supplier Database Promotion","Promote the use of the Sustainable Development Supplier Database (SD2), a platform profiling domestic suppliers with sustainability attributes, to enable foreign companies to identify and partner with local providers of goods and services",""],[1,"75","11","Special Economic Zones Development and Investment Attraction","Promote the establishment of special economic zones and attract investment into these zones.",""],[1,"75","13","Agro-industrial Processing Investment Attraction","Contribute to diversification of the industrial sector by attracting investment in agro- industrial processing plants for export-potential agricultural products,",""],[1,"75","13","Automotive and Electronics Assembly Investment Promotion Plan","prepare a strategic plan to promote and attract investment in automotive and electronics assembly, anchored in the Cambodia Automotive and Electronics Sector Development Roadmap",""],[1,"87","4","Industrial Investment Attractiveness Enhancement","Encouraging and enhancing investment attractiveness into the industries with high values added and green industry through the implementation of Cambodia Automotive and Electronics Sectors Development Roadmap; Cambodia Garment, Footwear and Travel Goods (GFT) Sector Development Strategy 2020-2027; and Law on Investment of the Kingdom of Cambodia.",""],[1,"87","8","Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone Development Plan","Accelerating Sihanoukville development as a multi-purpose special economic zone that serves as an important economic pole for tourism sector, financial service center, industrial zones and so on, through defining comprehensive and clear-cut implementation mechanisms and preparing a master plan for developing Cambodia coastal provinces as multi-purpose and inter-connected economic corridors.",""],[1,"88","2","Automotive and Electronics Sector Roadmap Coordination and Monitoring","Continue coordinating, promoting, and monitoring implementation of Cambodia's Automotive and Electronics Sector Development Roadmap, and undertake studies to identify and catalyze investment in emerging strategic industries",""],[1,"88","2","Studies on Investment Opportunities in Emerging Strategic Industries","undertake studies to identify and catalyze investment in emerging strategic industries",""],[1,"88","3","Investment Law Implementation and Promotion Forums","Further strengthen effective implementation of the Law on Investment of the Kingdom of Cambodia and its Sub-Decree on Implementation, and continue organizing dissemination forums and workshops on these instruments, along with domestic and international investment-promotion forums and related events",""],[1,"88","4","Industrial Development Policy Formulation and Research Programme","Expand research to draw on global best practices in industrial development, identify priority investment sectors, and collaborate on drafting a new Industrial Development Policy for Cambodia",""],[1,"88","5","Input to Master Plan for Preah Sihanouk Special Economic Zone Development","Contribute inputs to the master plan to develop Preah Sihanouk Province into a model multi-purpose special economic zone, and to the development of Cambodia's coastal provinces as multi-purpose economic corridors and clusters.",""],[1,"88","13","State-Invested Economic Zones","Support the establishment of state-invested economic zones at strategic locations to foster clustering of domestic and foreign enterprises for production and processing, and to back high-potential sectors where private investment is currently limited, in order to create jobs and promote economic diversification",""],[1,"96","10","Cluster and Develop Production Networks","The strategic objectives are to cluster and develop the production networks to play an important role in increasing efficiency and competitiveness of Cambodia industries, aiming at enhancing attractiveness for foreign and domestic direct investments, promotion of production and innovation for exports, and especially facilitating the creation of jobs and the improvements of the livelihoods of rural population.",""],[1,"96","10","Preparation of Sector-Specific Strategic Plans","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector- specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"96","11","SEZ Legal and Regulatory Framework for Industrial and Trade Zones","Introducing and implementing laws and regulations to manage and encourage the establishments of, and investment in SEZs, including industrial parks, agro-industrial parks, and domestic free-trade zones, to promote clusters of enterprises, aiming at enhancing efficiency and facilitating the ease for promoting the development of potential and key products, such as agricultural produces and agro-industrial products, electronic components, automobiles, textiles and/or furniture.",""],[1,"96","12","Study on Developing State Private Land for SEZs","Conducting a study and examining the possibility of developing and utilizing state's private land for SEZs, including industrial parks, agro-industrial parks, and domestic free-trade zones, to ensure job creation and production diversification.",""],[1,"97","1","State-Owned Economic Zones Development","Establishing state-owned economic zones in some strategic locations, with the aim of supporting concentration/clustering of factories and domestic and foreign enterprises, to produce and innovate products, as well as support potential sectors in which private sector are unable to invest.",""],[1,"97","2","Expansion of Public Infrastructure Investments for SEZs","Continuing to strengthen and expand public investments in the construction of connecting infrastructures, such as roads, transport and logistics systems, electricity networks, water supply systems, and wastewater treatment systems, for SEZs, including industrial parks, agro-industrial parks, technology parks, and domestic free-trade zones.",""],[1,"97","3","FDI-Enterprise Connectivity Support in SEZs","Enhancing connectivity between foreign direct investment and micro, small, medium, and large enterprises located in SEZs, including industrial parks, agro-industrial parks, and domestic free-trade zones, to support domestic enterprises' readiness for their participation in the regional and global supply chains.",""],[1,"97","6","Special Economic Zones Legal and Investment Promotion Package","Continue drafting the Law on Special Economic Zones and its implementing Sub-Decree, promote production value-chain linkages among investment projects within SEZs, and assess the feasibility of establishing state-invested SEZs at specific strategic locations to catalyze industrial clusters and ancillary industries",""],[1,"97","8","SEZ Electricity, Water, and Wastewater Infrastructure Support","Support development of electricity infrastructure in SEZs, with emphasis on renewable energy, as well as clean water supply and wastewater treatment systems",""],[1,"97","9","Overseas Study Missions on Industrial Parks for MSMEs","Organize or undertake overseas study missions on industrial parks for micro, small, and medium enterprises to foster linkages between large foreign firms and domestic enterprises.",""],[1,"97","13","Special Economic Zone Single-Window Trade Facilitation Mechanism","Ministry of Commerce continues to enhance the efficiency and attractiveness of special economic zones by operationalizing an effective, expedited single-window trade facilitation mechanism for on-site commercial services, certificates of origin, and related support, and by integrating the Ministry's automated public service systems across all SEZ and industrial park administrations","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"102","10","Domestic Enterprise Linkage and Entrepreneurship Support in Special Economic Zones","Strengthen the capacity and entrepreneurship of domestic enterprises to connect with and benefit from large foreign investors and enterprises in special economic zones",""],[1,"111","13","SME Development Medium-Term Plan and Action Framework","Develop a medium-term plan and a concrete action framework to advance SME development, prioritizing enterprises with export potential, new product development, and integration into multinational value chains and regional production networks",""]],"47":[[1,"64","9","Private Sector Good Governance Policy and Regulatory Frameworks","Strengthening and promoting good governance in the private sector and businesses through formulating and implementing policy frameworks relevant to good governance, laws and regulations, and other related principles in the private sector and businesses.",""],[1,"64","10","Private Sector Environmental and Social Responsibility Frameworks","Accelerating the formulation and implementation of policy frameworks that promote the private and business sector's environmental and social responsibility",""],[1,"64","11","Legal and Regulatory Review and Enforcement Mechanism Strengthening","Reviewing, updating, revising, and amending relevant laws and regulations, as well as monitoring and implementing law enforcement mechanisms.",""],[1,"64","12","Private Sector and Civil Society Governance Standards Development","Encouraging and supporting the private sector and civil society organizations in developing the code of ethics and professional conduct, as well as encouraging the private sector and civil society organizations to set the qualification standards for their respective Board of Directors to enhance accountability and to reduce conflict of interests.",""],[1,"65","2","Private and Business Sector Inspection Reform","Promoting the effectiveness and transparency of the private and business sector's inspection through encouraging the use of information technology systems in the inspection procedure; strengthening capacity building and integrity of inspectors; and accelerating the implementation of inspection measures.",""],[1,"65","9","Private Sector Governance and Commercial Law Enforcement Reform","Continue strengthening governance of the private sector and business, and build stakeholder confidence, through the development and amendment of laws, and by promoting the enforcement of laws and normative legal documents related to the commerce sector",""],[1,"65","13","Industrial Sector Management and Productivity Strengthening","Continue implementation and strengthening management of the industrial sector, protection of industrial property, industrial techniques and safety, and productivity, in accordance with laws and normative legal documents, sectoral needs, and the pace of industrial development, to build confidence among the private sector and businesses",""],[1,"65","14","SME Registration, Coordination, and Advisory Support","Strengthen the development of small and medium enterprises, especially registration, management, necessary coordination, and progress monitoring, to attract enterprises and handicrafts to register and to provide sufficient information to the Royal Government for supportive policymaking, and enable registered enterprises to access information on benefits and receive business advisory services to expand their operations and investments",""],[1,"66","1","Implementation of the National Strategy on Informal Economy Development 2023-2028","Promote implementation of the National Strategy on Informal Economy Development 2023-2028",""],[1,"66","3","Development Partner Cooperation for SME and Handicraft Planning","Continue to promote cooperation with development partners to formulate development plans for small and medium enterprises and handicrafts",""],[1,"66","4","Delegation of Authority for SME and Handicraft Licensing","Strengthen delegation of authority to municipal and provincial departments for registration or establishment and licensing, as well as for the operation of small and medium enterprises and handicrafts.",""],[1,"66","5","Private Sector Anti-Corruption Cooperation Expansion","priority action shall continue strengthening cooperation with the private sector by signing additional memoranda of understanding with new companies, to mainstream anti-corruption in the private sector and to reinforce transparency and integrity in business operations in Cambodia, while improving the public services provided by state institutions and authorities to companies.",""],[1,"89","1","MSME and Start-up Enabling Environment Reform","Formulate policies, strategies, and regulations, and improve governance to create an enabling environment for micro, small, and medium enterprises and start-ups, while enhancing efficient public service delivery for all actors in the entrepreneurship ecosystem",""]],"48":[[1,"65","1","Strengthening Dialogue Mechanisms and Public-Private Partnerships","Promoting the effectiveness of dialogue mechanisms and public-private partnerships at policy and technical levels and at national and sub-national levels to stimulate policy discussions and to find solutions to challenges by leveraging the roles of domestic and external chambers of commerce and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"65","5","Government-Private Sector Forum Dialogue Mechanism","Continue to strengthen and broaden the scope of the Government-Private Sector Forum dialogue mechanism, and continue coordinating the organization of this forum at least twice per mandate, while monitoring and evaluating progress on the measures adopted by the forum, and reporting to the Prime Minister every six months",""],[1,"65","6","Government-Private Sector Dialogue Mechanism","Continue convening meetings and dialogues between the Royal Government and the private sector, such as meetings of the Cambodia-Japan Joint Committee under the Agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and Japan on the Liberalization, Promotion and Protection of Investment, and the Advisory Council for the development of the automotive and electronics sectors, among others",""],[1,"65","7","Targeted Investment Aftercare Service Mechanism","Promote a more active, proactive, and targeted investment aftercare service mechanism, and ensure harmony within Cambodia's private sector.",""],[1,"65","10","Private Sector Coordination and Capacity Support","Continue coordinating with and supporting the private sector to raise its effectiveness, by promoting the capacity and accountability of Chambers of Commerce, business associations, and business federations, and by strengthening close cooperation with the private sector",""],[1,"65","11","Public-Private Partnership Dialogue and Problem-Solving Mechanism","Continue implementing public-private partnership at both policy and technical levels to develop the private sector, by improving problem-solving effectiveness and fostering new initiatives within dialogue and partnership mechanisms at the national and subnational levels, aiming to facilitate trade, and to diversify products and markets.",""],[1,"72","13","Public-Private Partnership Mechanism Strengthening","Continuing to implement the public-private partnership mechanisms by strengthening the implementation of the Law on Public-Private Partnerships.",""]],"49":[[1,"119","1","Local and Border Market Development Programme","promoting establishment of local markets, wholesale markets, and weekend markets for traders, entrepreneurs, and smallholder farmers, developing and implementing action plans for construction of border and provincial markets, and establishing online marketplaces via e-commerce platforms.",""],[1,"120","1","OVOP Registration and Market Promotion Programme","Expand the registration of one village one product (OVOP) initiatives and producer clusters, while continuing to organize key events, national days promoting Cambodian products, exhibitions, sales showcases during various national festivals, and producer-buyer forums to disseminate information and elevate markets for OVOP and domestic products",""],[1,"120","2","OVOP Product Standards and Online Market Expansion","Establish standards for OVOP products, incorporating quality grading classifications, as well as increasing sales and market exploration through online platforms",""],[1,"120","4","OVOP Partnership Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen relationships, cooperative efforts, and partnerships with development partners, civil society, and the private sector to support and advance the OVOP movement in Cambodia.",""]],"50":[[1,"16","1","Commercial Registration and E-Permit System","This has been accomplished by issuing e-commerce permits and licenses, an automatic system for registration, and the issuance of e-permits/licenses.",""],[1,"16","1","Legal Dissemination and Intellectual Property Strengthening","Other achievements include the dissemination of related laws and legal instruments, the strengthening of intellectual property through relevant legal instruments and a national intellectual property policy, and the suppression of counterfeit goods and services to ensure food safety, protect consumers, and promote fair competition.",""],[1,"16","1","Food Safety Awareness and Sanitary-Phytosanitary Information System","Furthermore, the government has reinforced mechanisms to raise public awareness of food safety, and it has researched, compiled, and selected notifications on sanitary and phytosanitary measures from various sources.",""],[1,"16","1","Halal Product Certification System","It has also issued certificates to confirm the technical standards of Cambodian Halal products, implemented an automated system for issuing Certificates of Origin, and delegated the issuance of Form D Certificates of Origin for agricultural goods.",""],[1,"16","1","ASEAN Self-Certification and Exporter Registration Initiative","The government has also implemented the ASEAN-wide Self-Certification of Origin and an exporter registration project for exports to the European Union, Switzerland, Norway, and Turkey.",""],[1,"17","2","Trade Preference and Export Promotion Measures","At the same time, the Royal Government has coordinated with the United States to resume the Generalized System of Preferences (GSP) and continued to disseminate information about new trade preference systems to the private sector.",""],[1,"17","2","ASEAN Trade Connectivity and SME Support Coordination","It has also organized and led relevant meetings covering four key strategies: increasing digital connectivity in ASEAN, supporting and promoting the growth of ASEAN small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), and coordinating and cooperating to reduce export and import costs with countries in the ASEAN region.",""],[1,"17","2","Trade Promotion and Market Access Mechanisms","A wide range of trade promotion mechanisms have been established to increase exports and enhance integration, including the implementation of the Cambodia Trade Integration Strategy 2019-2023; the organization of domestic and international trade fairs; the creation of Cambodian private trade centers abroad; the monitoring of market situations and collection of price indices for essential goods; the establishment of the Cambodia-Vietnam border market; and the organization of forums to connect sellers and buyers.",""],[1,"17","2","Trade Statistics Data Management System","In addition, measures have been undertaken such as the creation of a data management system for trade statistics and information; the preparation of legal instruments to promote competition, consumer protection, and e-commerce; the amendment of the Law on Commercial Enterprises, trade rules, and the food safety commercial registry; the conduct of feasibility studies on Free Trade Agreements and the development of a strategic plan to maximize their benefits; and the strengthening of Cambodia's Permanent Mission to the World Trade Organization and other international organizations in the economic and trade sectors.",""],[1,"17","2","Trade Competition, Consumer Protection, and E-Commerce Legal Reform","In addition, measures have been undertaken such as the creation of a data management system for trade statistics and information; the preparation of legal instruments to promote competition, consumer protection, and e-commerce; the amendment of the Law on Commercial Enterprises, trade rules, and the food safety commercial registry; the conduct of feasibility studies on Free Trade Agreements and the development of a strategic plan to maximize their benefits; and the strengthening of Cambodia's Permanent Mission to the World Trade Organization and other international organizations in the economic and trade sectors.",""],[1,"17","2","Free Trade Agreement Feasibility and Benefit Maximization Plan","In addition, measures have been undertaken such as the creation of a data management system for trade statistics and information; the preparation of legal instruments to promote competition, consumer protection, and e-commerce; the amendment of the Law on Commercial Enterprises, trade rules, and the food safety commercial registry; the conduct of feasibility studies on Free Trade Agreements and the development of a strategic plan to maximize their benefits; and the strengthening of Cambodia's Permanent Mission to the World Trade Organization and other international organizations in the economic and trade sectors.",""],[1,"17","2","Strengthening of Cambodia's Permanent Mission to the WTO","In addition, measures have been undertaken such as the creation of a data management system for trade statistics and information; the preparation of legal instruments to promote competition, consumer protection, and e-commerce; the amendment of the Law on Commercial Enterprises, trade rules, and the food safety commercial registry; the conduct of feasibility studies on Free Trade Agreements and the development of a strategic plan to maximize their benefits; and the strengthening of Cambodia's Permanent Mission to the World Trade Organization and other international organizations in the economic and trade sectors.",""],[1,"54","10","Internal Structural Reform and External Market Expansion","Continuing to implement internal structural reforms and expanding external markets",""],[1,"54","11","Trade Facilitation Simplification Measures","Strengthening trade facilitation by reducing documentation requirements and redundant",""],[1,"55","4","Market Expansion through Free Trade Agreements","Efforts include leveraging existing markets and promoting the opening of new ones through bilateral and multilateral free trade agreements, and",""]],"51":[[1,"26","4","SME and Entrepreneurship Promotion Package","The government has also promoted the role of women in entrepreneurship, encouraged the use of digital systems for SMEs, and fostered green development.",""],[1,"26","4","SME Regulatory and Administrative Support Measures","Other efforts include strengthening intellectual property law enforcement, providing benefits for SME registration, offering online business registration and one-stop-shop services, giving incentives to SMEs in priority sectors, developing SME clusters, and fostering connections between foreign direct investment companies and local SMEs.",""],[1,"47","14","Domestic Supporting Industries Capacity Building","The capacity building of domestic supporting industries will create opportunities for the industries to increase their value-added, efficiency, productivity, and competitiveness, by improving the efficiency of input supply for production processes, reducing costs of",""],[1,"52","4","Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprise and Startup Promotion","promotion of micro, small, and medium enterprises, startups, entrepreneurship, and development of informal economy;",""],[1,"53","6","SME and Informal Economy Support Programme","Continue to promote the private sector by supporting the development of small and medium-sized enterprises and the informal economy, while creating a favorable environment by strengthening the implementation of the Law on Investment of the Kingdom of Cambodia, introducing specific incentive measures, and improving the business environment with competitiveness and equity",""],[1,"98","7","Formal Business Registration Promotion","Promoting formal registration of businesses, especially micro, small, and medium enterprises, to facilitate financial and banking institutions in providing secure credit services, as well as allowing them to receive incentives and interventions.",""],[1,"98","14","Penalty and Debt Amnesty Coordination for Informal Enterprise Formalization","Coordinate implementation of penalty and debt amnesties in 2023-2028 for past noncompliance, enabling informal enterprises to transition and start new businesses in the formal economy without concern",""],[1,"99","1","MSME and Start-up Finance Access Support","Facilitate greater access to finance for micro, small, and medium enterprises and start-ups across credit and capital markets, including grant support, consideration of equity co- investment, expansion of the Entrepreneurship Development Fund, and targeted incentives for MSMEs and start-ups",""],[1,"99","2","Entrepreneurship Ecosystem Strengthening","Strengthen the entrepreneurship ecosystem through market creation and financing mechanisms",""],[1,"99","3","Establishment of Sub-sector Associations","Promote the establishment of sub-sector associations to share knowledge, protect members' interests, and deepen engagement with the Royal Government to secure technical and financial support",""],[1,"99","4","MSME Business Governance and Management Training","Strengthen business governance to foster a culture of social accountability and improve access to finance, through training in general management, production systems management, and technology management for MSMEs",""],[1,"99","8","Special Concessional Financing Programs for SMEs and Agriculture","Continue deploying special financing programs on highly concessional terms through the SME Bank and the Agriculture and Rural Development Bank.",""],[1,"99","10","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation for Priority Programs","Ministries- institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"101","2","Business Management and Entrepreneurship Training for MSMEs and Start-ups","Continue to promote and encourage training in business management and entrepreneurship skills for factory owners and employees of micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSMEs), as well as start-ups, including support for organizing programs to share entrepreneurship experiences",""],[1,"101","7","MSME and Startup Enabling Environment Development","The strategic objectives are to further promote the development of an enabling environment for micro, small, and medium enterprises, and startups, to grow and to be resilient and innovative, contributing to economic growth and job creation, as well as promoting the transition of informal economy into formal economy.",""],[1,"101","7","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"101","9","MSME and Startup Capacity and Skills Development Programme","Continuing to promote and encourage the enhancement of capacity, business management and entrepreneurial skills for owners of micro, small, and medium enterprises, and startups; supporting the mentorship programs from experienced entrepreneurs; and promoting trainings on competencies and skills for employees in micro, small, and medium enterprises, and startups.",""],[1,"102","1","MSME and Startup Finance Expansion Measures","Increasing the access to finance for potential micro, small, and medium enterprises, and startups, through the development of new financial products in the credit and financial markets, providing grants and investing in those companies, continuing to expand Entrepreneurship Development Fund (EDF), and encouraging the private sector to invest in micro, small, and medium enterprises, and startups.",""],[1,"102","3","Entrepreneurial and Business Culture Promotion Mechanisms","Developing and implementing the mechanisms to promote entrepreneurial and business cultures through mainstreaming entrepreneurial values, promoting creativities and inventions, and raising public awareness on risk acceptance.",""],[1,"102","4","Strategy on the Development of Informal Economy 2023-2028","Developing and implementing the Strategy on the Development of Informal Economy 2023-2028.",""],[1,"102","9","SME Training and Production Modernization Support","Assess the feasibility of providing training and supporting investment in production machinery and equipment for small and medium enterprises, and offer additional incentives to SMEs, linked to local content requirements, product quality upgrading, and modernization of processing across the value chain, to connect with multinational companies",""],[1,"102","14","MSME and Informal Economy Market Expansion and Digital Business Services","Ministry of Commerce shall continue to strengthen and expand domestic and international markets for micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs), start-ups, and businesses in the informal economy by deploying automated systems for business registration, licensing and permitting, and for conducting electronic commerce.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"103","1","Private Sector Support Services and Capacity-Building","targeted support, including advisory services, related public services, the establishment of business councils, capacity-building training, and the provision of market information to the private sector.",""],[1,"103","5","Enterprise and Start-up Financing Support","Provide financing to enterprises and start-ups undertaking entrepreneurial and innovation activities",""],[1,"103","6","MSME Skills Development Financing Support","Provide financing for skills development to MSMEs to strengthen business development capabilities, including digital skills",""],[1,"103","7","Tax Incentive Mechanisms for Enterprises, Start-ups, and the Informal Economy","Continue to design and implement tax incentive mechanisms for enterprises, start-ups, and the informal economy.",""],[1,"111","12","Standards and Industrial Property Rights Awareness and Outreach Campaign","Increase awareness and outreach on the benefits of standards, metrology, and industrial property rights to encourage broad participation by entrepreneurs",""],[1,"111","14","Entrepreneurship Information Dissemination Mechanisms","Continue to establish mechanisms and strategies to broaden information dissemination that expands pathways into entrepreneurship for the public, through information sharing among producer groups, businesses, and consumers",""],[1,"111","15","Entrepreneurship and Business Culture Promotion Mechanism","Design and implement mechanisms to promote an entrepreneurial and business culture by mainstreaming awareness and values of entrepreneurship, innovation, start-up creation, and responsible business risk-taking among the public.",""]],"52":[[1,"99","5","Standardization and Conformity Assessment Expansion","Expand the application of standardization and conformity assessment, linked to public procurement, incentives, and other support measures.",""],[1,"102","8","Metrology and Standards Institutional Strengthening","Continue to enhance the institutional framework and management capacity for metrology and standards, which underpin industrial activity, and continue efforts to establish the regulatory framework and secure international recognition for key national institutions, including the national metrology center and the institute of standards of Cambodia",""],[1,"102","11","Metrology and Standards Capacity Enhancement","Support the enhancement of metrology and standards capacities and competencies to ensure conformity in quantity, quality, safety, service, environmental, and governance requirements",""]],"53":[[1,"75","14","Informal Economy Formalization Partnership Initiative","Encourage participation by associations, national and international organizations, development partners, and especially the private sector, to facilitate the formalization of operators and workers in the informal economy into the formal economy",""],[1,"75","15","Technology Transfer Legal and Regulatory Frameworks","Support and promote technology transfer by establishing conducive legal and regulatory frameworks and an enabling ecosystem",""],[1,"76","1","Industrial Production Promotion and Diversification for SMEs","Promote production and diversify industrial output, including among small and medium enterprises",""],[1,"76","2","Expanded International Accreditation Membership Pursuit","Seek full membership in APAC, IHAF, ILAC, and IAF across additional scopes beyond ISO/IEC 17025 testing laboratories, to secure international recognition across all scopes, facilitate trade, reduce business costs, and lower technical, sanitary, and phytosanitary barriers to trade",""],[1,"76","3","Certificate of Conformity Registration and Recognition Procedures","Continue to operationalize procedures for the registration and recognition of certificates of conformity associated with imported and exported goods, in order to reduce substandard products, protect consumer interests, enhance public health, and support Cambodia's trade.",""],[1,"87","9","Cambodia Industrial Development Policy Implementation and Update","Continuing to implement Cambodia Industrial Development Policy 2015-2025; and updating this policy to align with the new context of changing architecture of regional and global trade and economy.",""],[1,"88","14","Industrial Regulatory Instrument Development","Continue strengthening cooperation with development partners and the private sector, and develop industrial regulatory instruments to build high value-added industrial bases and advance green industry",""],[1,"89","2","Accreditation and Mutual Recognition of Conformity Assessment Bodies","Promote accreditation and recognition of competence and capability for conformity assessment bodies that provide certification and related registration services against national and international standards, and continue cooperation with partner-country recognition bodies to conduct joint assessments and recognition of Cambodian conformity assessment bodies",""],[1,"89","3","Industrial Property Registration Efficiency Reform","Increase the efficiency of industrial property registration by implementing cooperative procedures, authorizing registration rights to agents from partner countries, and streamlining the registration of agents who serve as representatives for industrial property applicants",""],[1,"89","4","National Standards Development and Expansion Initiative","Advance development of national standards for new domestic products that are emerging drivers of growth, and expand national standards across sectors to support diversified trade aligned with Industry 4.0",""],[1,"89","5","National Quality Infrastructure Services Expansion","Enhance and expand national quality infrastructure services that support industry, trade, and services",""],[1,"89","6","Analytical Testing and Test Method Update Programme","Strengthen and broaden analytical testing and routinely update test methods to align with evolving international regulations, facilitating trade and market access",""],[1,"89","7","Laboratory Testing Expansion and Accreditation Upgrade","Promote technical excellence and operational efficiency by expanding analytical testing in mechanical, electrical, and electronic fields, achieving accreditation to ISO/IEC 17043, upgrading laboratory equipment, and broadening service offerings.",""]],"54":[[1,"27","1","Public Infrastructure and Service Project Structuring and Implementation","the structuring and implementation of public infrastructure and service projects.",""],[1,"27","1","Private Sector Participation in Public Infrastructure Investment","The government continues to encourage private sector participation in public infrastructure investment, which brings in additional financial resources, knowledge, expertise, and modern technology to the public sector for more innovative and efficient management of public investment projects.",""],[1,"27","1","Joint Operational Management Procedure for PPP Projects","The Royal Government has also introduced a joint operational management procedure for PPP projects, which includes relevant policies, procurement management procedures, and other guidelines.",""],[1,"52","4","Public-Private Partnership Strengthening","strengthening of public-private partnerships;",""],[1,"103","8","Strengthen Public-Private Partnerships","The strategic objectives are to further strengthen public-private partnerships, which are indispensable and effective mechanisms to support economic diversification and growth",""],[1,"103","8","Manage Contingent Liability Risks in Public-Private Partnerships","and to further strengthen the management of risks of contingent liabilities arising from the implementation of public investment projects under the public-private partnership mechanism",""],[1,"103","8","Prepare Sector-Specific Strategic Plans for Priority Programs","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"103","9","Public-Private Partnership Capacity Development for Public Investment Projects","Continuing to promote awareness and develop the institutional and human resource capacity in ministries-institutions related to the design, development, implementation, and management of public investment projects through public-private partnership mechanisms.",""],[1,"103","10","Public-Private Partnership Market Support Mechanisms","Promoting and developing infrastructures to support the public-private partnership market through the establishment of financial support and state support mechanisms, mandated by the Law on Public-Private Partnerships and legal instruments in force.",""],[1,"103","11","Public-Private Partnership Public Investment Project Development","Continuing to develop the public investment projects through public-private partnerships, focusing on state-solicited projects related to infrastructure development and improvement of public service delivery to support economic growth, and reduce budgetary pressures and burdens of public debt services.",""],[1,"103","12","Inter-Institutional Fiscal Risk Coordination Mechanism","Continuing to promote inter-institutional coordination mechanisms to collect project information and data to strengthen analysis and management of fiscal risks.",""],[1,"103","13","PPP Obligation Inspection and Monitoring Mechanism","Formulating a mechanism to inspect and monitor the implementation of public and private obligations in accordance with the public-private partnership agreements and legal instruments in force.",""],[1,"103","15","Public-Private Partnership for Market-Supporting Infrastructure","Ministry of Commerce shall continue to strengthen public-private partnership to develop private-sector and market-supporting infrastructure, ensuring the smooth flow of goods","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"104","2","PPP Public Investment Regulatory and Institutional Review","Continue to review and as needed, adjust relevant regulatory frameworks, institutional arrangements, and operational management procedures for public investment projects implemented through public-private partnership (PPP) mechanisms",""],[1,"104","3","PPP Feasibility Assessment for Social Sector Public Investment","Assess the feasibility of public investment via PPP mechanisms in the social sectors, including public health service infrastructure and education and sports infrastructure.",""]],"55":[[1,"105","4","Financial Sector Legal, Institutional, and Digitalization Reform","The strategic objectives are to further strengthen the banking system and non-banking financial sector to be more efficient, resilient, inclusive, diversified and modernized by continuing to develop legal frameworks, promoting financial deepening, strengthening institutional capacity and financial literacy, and promoting digitalization in these financial sectors.",""],[1,"105","4","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning for Priority Programs and Actions","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"105","5","Financial Sector Development Strategy Update and Implementation","Continuing to implement the Financial Sector Development Strategy 2016-2025, as well as to update this strategy to further develop legal frameworks, financial technology infrastructures and political coordination mechanisms, and to enhance the roles of financial intermediation; promoting institutional and human capital capacity building in banking and non-banking sectors; and diversifying financial products.",""],[1,"106","7","Banking Sector Priority Actions","National Bank of Cambodia shall focus on implementing the following priority actions: Banking sector",""],[1,"106","14","Interbank Market Development and Monetary Instruments Reform","Develop the interbank market and introduce new monetary instruments to reduce transaction costs and improve the effectiveness of monetary policy in maintaining price stability",""],[1,"107","2","Payment and Settlement Systems Infrastructure Expansion","Strengthen and expand payment and settlement systems infrastructure to reduce transaction costs and increase efficiency and security of payments, promoting business, trade, investment, and cross-border transactions",""],[1,"107","4","Financial Services Modernization Initiative","2) modernizing financial services to improve access and convenience nationwide",""]],"56":[[1,"25","5","National Financial Inclusion Strategy Action Plan","Through the implementation of the National Financial Inclusion Strategy's Action Plan 2019-2025 and other initiatives, the number of credit and deposit accounts has steadily increased from 3.1 million and 7.6 million, respectively, in 2019, to 3.9 million and 19.2 million in 2023.",""],[1,"26","1","Cross-Border Payment Infrastructure Expansion","The government has also connected its payment infrastructure with countries in the region and with UnionPay and is expanding cross-border payments with Alipay, other partner countries, and various institutions.",""],[1,"26","1","Consumer Protection and Anti-Scam Regulatory Measures","New regulations have been issued, including public announcements about social media and phone scams, illegal lending and advertising, the dangers of informal loans, and a joint statement between the National Bank of Cambodia and the General Commission of the National Police.","National Bank of Cambodia | General Commission of the National Police"],[1,"43","1","Monetary Policy Tool Development","monetary policy tools have been developed to contribute to increasing the effectiveness of monetary policy.",""],[1,"47","13","Digital Transformation of Financial Services","Digital transformation of the financial services will support the implementation of digital economy policies and increase economic efficiency and financial inclusion",""],[1,"52","4","Competition Promotion and Financial Sector Strengthening","promotion of competition; and strengthening of banking system and non-banking financial sector.",""],[1,"53","11","Monetary Policy Measures for Price, Financial, and Payment System Stability","In this regard, the Royal Government has decided to introduce a number of measures as follows:",""],[1,"54","1","Strengthening Monetary Instruments for Riel Use","Continue to strengthen monetary instruments to support the use of riel in the banking system.",""],[1,"54","1","Riel-Denominated Bond Issuance","corporate bonds and government bonds are issued in riel to demonstrate the development of the riel capital market",""],[1,"54","2","Payment System Modernization and Cross-Border Payment Expansion","Continue to modernize payment systems, especially the Bakong system, to facilitate riel payments to be convenient, safe and efficient, and expand the scope of cross-border payments through connections with regional countries and international payment companies",""],[1,"54","3","Riel Promotion and Public Awareness Campaign","Raise public awareness about the importance of the riel and its use through riel promotion programs, workshops or public forums in Phnom Penh and in the provinces",""],[1,"54","4","Monetary and Interbank Market Development","Develop the monetary and interbank market to support financial intermediation, the use of the riel, and the influence of monetary policy, especially through interest rates",""],[1,"54","6","Riel Usage Promotion and Financial Inclusion Initiative","Encourage the opening of bank accounts in riel, collaborate with relevant public and private institutions to promote the payment of salaries, price tags and payments in riel, and improve the financial environment in rural areas, especially the wider use of riel.",""],[1,"130","8","Cambodia Financial Technology Development Policy Implementation","The strategic objectives are to develop financial technologies by fully grabbing the opportunities and reaping the benefits of digital technologies to promote financial inclusion, financial stability, and financial innovation, through implementing the Cambodia Financial Technology Development Policy 2023-2028.",""],[1,"130","9","Financial Technology Regulatory Reform and Enforcement","Preparing for the amendment and more effective enforcement of laws and regulations related to financial technology to build regulatory ecosystems, harmonize functions, and build user trust.",""],[1,"130","10","Open Finance Framework Development and Study","Undertaking a study and developing open finance frameworks for sharing and opening data to offer new opportunities for financial technology development and innovation for enterprises and startups in financial technology-related businesses.",""],[1,"130","11","Digital Enabling Platforms for Financial Technology","Continuing to build, modernize, and use digital enabling platforms in financial technology sector to promote financial innovation.",""],[1,"130","12","Inclusive Digital Payment System Modernization","Continuing to modernize and finetune digital payment system in an inclusive manner, based on interoperability principles as an ecosystem to ensure national sovereignty of financial technologies.",""],[1,"130","13","Regulatory and Supervisory Technology Development","Developing regulatory and supervisory technologies to facilitate and strengthen regulatory compliance, as well as to enhance analytical and monitoring capacity and support proactive and effective risk controls.",""],[1,"131","1","Financial Technology Skills, Innovation, and Collaboration Development","Developing skills and knowledge, facilitating dissemination, fostering collaboration, and expanding research, development, innovation, experiments, and use of new latest technologies in financial technology.",""],[1,"131","2","Financial Technology Ecosystem Development","Continuing to develop financial technology ecosystem to be more diverse; and strengthening coordination mechanisms for ensuring the interconnectedness and complementarity between banking and non-banking financial technologies.",""],[1,"131","5","Financial Sector Data Protection and Data Sharing Regulatory Framework Assessment","Assess the feasibility of implementing a regulatory framework for data protection and data sharing in the financial sector",""],[1,"131","6","Financial Crime Prevention and AML/CFT Enforcement","Combat financial crime, including anti-money laundering, countering the financing of terrorism, and countering the financing of the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction",""],[1,"131","7","Open Banking Framework Feasibility Review","Review and assess the feasibility of introducing an open banking framework",""],[1,"131","8","Cross-Border Payments and Remittances Cooperation","Promote bilateral and/or multilateral cooperation with countries in the region to support cross-border payments and remittances",""],[1,"131","9","Digital Identity Platform for Financial and Banking Sector","Develop and deploy a digital identity platform for the financial and banking sector",""],[1,"131","10","Payment System Infrastructure Modernization","Develop and modernize payment system infrastructure to support services and enhance interoperability of digital payments",""],[1,"131","11","Financial Technology Awareness Campaigns and Public Outreach","Organize public forums, events, competitions, exhibitions, and campaigns to raise awareness of the benefits and practical applications of financial technologies, in collaboration with relevant stakeholders as needed",""],[1,"131","12","Financial Literacy, Digital Literacy, and Fintech Development Programs","Collaborate with all relevant stakeholders to roll out programs on financial literacy, digital literacy, and fintech development for the general public and entrepreneurs",""],[1,"131","13","Digital Lending Regulation and Guidance Framework","Draft and issue regulations and guidelines for safe and efficient digital lending operations",""],[1,"131","14","Digital Payment Prudential Regulation and Security Strengthening","Strengthen the prudential regulatory framework and security mechanisms for digital payment operations",""],[1,"131","15","Digital Payment Instruments Promotion","Promote the use of digital payment instruments across the public and private sectors",""],[1,"131","16","Innovative Digital Banking Products and Services Promotion","Promote innovative digital banking products and services",""],[1,"131","17","Digital Credit and Savings Product Deployment","Encourage banking and financial institutions to deploy digital credit and digital savings products.",""],[1,"131","19","Consumer Protection and Fintech Capacity-Building Mechanism","Study and design mechanisms to strengthen consumer protection, including data and privacy protection related to fintech in the non-bank financial sector, and contribute to a master plan for fintech capacity building and skills development",""],[1,"131","20","Fintech Regulatory Sandbox for the Non-Bank Financial Sector","Assess the feasibility of establishing, operationalizing, and developing a fintech regulatory sandbox in the non-bank financial sector, with attention to functional harmonization and the development and supervision of innovative fintech activities",""],[1,"131","21","Fintech Products and Services Development and Adoption in Non-Bank Financial Sector","Promote and encourage the development and use of fintech products and services in the non-bank financial sector, including decentralized applications (dApps)",""],[1,"131","22","Research and Development for Innovation and Fintech Diversification","Advance research and development to increase innovation in services and products and to diversify emerging fintech activities",""],[1,"132","1","Fintech Entrepreneurship Ecosystem Support","Foster the fintech entrepreneurship ecosystem in the non-bank financial sector through forums, workshops, and programs, including training and fintech startup acceleration",""],[1,"132","2","Fintech Governance and Digital Finance Regulation Reform","Enhance the effectiveness of fintech governance, supervision, and development by continuing to explore the application of RegTech and SupTech, and by drafting regulations to govern digital asset businesses and person-to-person lending operations.",""],[1,"132","3","Collateral Registry for Movable Assets","Digital Economy and Business Committee shall coordinate with the Ministry of Commerce to develop and promote the implementation of a Collateral Registry for Movable Assets.","Digital Economy and Business Committee | Ministry of Commerce"]],"57":[[1,"105","6","Riel Use Promotion Initiative","continuing to promote the use of Riel.",""],[1,"105","7","Financial Literacy Promotion and CIFRS Implementation","Continuing to promote financial literacy through the continuation of public awareness campaigns, curriculum development and financial management trainings for owners and managers of enterprises, especially SMEs, and continuing to promote the implementation of the Cambodian International Financial Reporting Standards (CIFRS).",""],[1,"106","13","Riel Usage Promotion Policy Measures","Promote broader use of the riel through appropriate and effective new policies and measures to maximize riel usage",""],[1,"106","15","Finance Access Expansion for High-Productivity Sectors and SMEs","Expand access to finance for high productivity sectors and small and medium enterprises",""],[1,"107","3","Consumer Protection Framework Expansion","Review the need to expand the consumer protection framework in existing regulations by clarifying requirements for credit products, advertising and marketing, complaints and dispute resolution procedures, fees, interest calculation, and debt collection practices",""],[1,"107","4","Rural Financial Inclusion Expansion","Advance financial inclusion by 1) expanding financial products and services to rural areas",""],[1,"107","4","Digital and Financial Literacy Promotion","3) promoting digital and financial literacy so citizens can fully benefit",""],[1,"107","5","Green Finance Roadmap and Taxonomy Development","Promote green finance by 1) preparing a green finance roadmap, 2) developing a green finance taxonomy and markets, 3) encouraging banking and financial institutions to finance green projects, 4) establishing frameworks to analyze and assess climate-related risks in the banking and financial sector, and 5) building capacity and raising awareness on green finance.",""],[1,"107","6","Microfinance Sector and Financial Inclusion Strategy Update","Update the national strategy on the microfinance sector and the financial inclusion strategy",""],[1,"107","9","Financial Literacy and Public Awareness Campaigns","Continue to enhance financial literacy by sustaining public awareness campaigns, especially for rural populations, to promote understanding of the financial sector and advance financial inclusion",""],[1,"107","10","Low-Cost Financing and Interest Rate Reduction Measures","Identify low-cost sources of funding, analyze the factors that raise the cost of funds, and explore measures to reduce interest rates in line with market mechanisms",""]],"58":[[1,"108","2","Public Awareness and Insurance Literacy Enhancement","Enhance public awareness and insurance literacy",""],[1,"108","3","Insurance Market Development and Microinsurance Expansion","Develop the insurance market by improving the effectiveness of microinsurance implementation and expanding insurance product offerings",""],[1,"108","4","Supervisory and Risk Management Framework Strengthening","Strengthen and continually refine the supervisory framework, with a particular focus on the risk management framework",""],[1,"108","5","Insurance Technology Advancement and Supervisory Information System","Advance insurance technology by coordinating the technology ecosystem and implementing a supervisory information system",""],[1,"108","6","Cambodia Insurance Institute Establishment","Build human capital by accelerating the establishment of the Cambodia Insurance Institute.",""]],"60":[[1,"134","1","Public Investment Financing for Priority Policy Implementation","These funds will be allocated to implement key investment projects aimed at achieving the priority policies outlined in the Pentagon Strategy - Phase I, the National Strategic Development Plan (NSDP) of the Royal Government for the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly, and various sectoral strategic development plans.",""],[1,"134","2","Public Investment Financing Diversification Framework","The Royal Government is considering a range of funding sources to support public investment expenditures, including: (1) National budget allocations; (2) Foreign financing; (3) Financing through public-private partnership (PPP) mechanisms; (4) Blended financing sources; (5) Proceeds from the privatization of state assets; (6) Financing by public enterprises, public administrative institutions, and similar public entities; (7) Commercial credit; and (8) Other financing sources, as appropriate.",""],[1,"134","3","Capital Investment Mobilization and Concessional Financing Measures","the Royal Government will intensify efforts to mobilize additional capital investment and capitalize on emerging opportunities through the following measures: (1) Maximizing the effectiveness of official development assistance (ODA); (2) Encouraging greater grant support from development partners; (3) Pursuing additional concessional financing in partnership with development partners, with a focus on long-term, high-impact investments, particularly in infrastructure development; and (4) Expanding the use of public-private partnership (PPP) mechanisms and promoting private sector participation in large-scale public investment initiatives, to reduce the fiscal burden on the national budget and enhance private sector contributions to public service delivery and national development objectives.",""]],"61":[[1,"17","1","Agricultural Market Promotion Project for Small-Scale Farmers","The e-Commerce Strategy / Go4eCAM Project and the Agricultural Market Promotion Project for small-scale farmers (AIMS) have also been implemented.",""],[1,"27","3","Agricultural Market Information and Investment Promotion","the government is promoting market information analysis and publicizing the attractiveness of investing in Cambodia's agri-food sector.",""],[1,"27","3","Food Security Strengthening Through Rice Policy and State Food Reserve Stock","it is also strengthening and expanding food security through the implementation of the Rice Policy and State Food Reserve Stock",""],[1,"27","3","Landmine and Unexploded Ordnance Clearance for Agricultural Use","clearing landmines and unexploded ordnance for agricultural use",""],[1,"27","3","Irrigation System Rehabilitation and Expansion","repairing, maintaining, restoring, and constructing irrigation systems.",""],[1,"27","3","Flood and Drought Management for Agriculture","Furthermore, it is managing floods and droughts",""],[1,"27","3","Agricultural Community Development and Union Formation","encouraging the growth of agricultural communities, establishing agricultural community unions",""],[1,"27","3","One Village One Product Promotion Plan","implementing a national strategic plan and policy to promote the \"One Village One Product\" movement.",""],[1,"34","6","Agricultural Production, Market Access, and Price Stabilization Support","It has introduced a coordination mechanism and financing programs to promote production, find markets, and stabilize prices for key agricultural products.",""],[1,"34","6","Deployment of Agricultural Technical Officers","It has deployed 250 agricultural technical officers to 250 communes (in 89 districts and 17 provinces),",""],[1,"34","6","Modern Agricultural Communities Initiative","organized and launched nine modern agricultural communities,",""],[1,"34","6","Irrigation Infrastructure Development","and focused on promoting the construction of irrigation",""]],"62":[[1,"49","1","Agricultural Processing Investment and Public Support Measures","The crop subsector is expected to achieve good growth due to increasing domestic and foreign investment in agricultural processing, public investment, and government interventions.",""],[1,"49","1","Local Livestock Production Promotion Mechanisms","The livestock subsector is gradually recovering through mechanisms to encourage and promote local livestock production.",""],[1,"49","1","Illegal Fishing Control and Aquaculture Investment","the fisheries subsector will continue to grow, supported by optimism for increased freshwater fish production as recovery continues following the implementation of policies to combat illegal fishing and investments in aquaculture.",""]],"63":[[1,"112","7","Strategic Fisheries Management and Development Programme","Improving the management of fisheries resources by promoting the implementation of the Strategic Planning Framework for Fisheries; promoting aquaculture; strengthening the management and development of the fishing communities; promoting the development of capacity and technologies to improve fisheries quality; developing fisheries value chains and export promotion; and strengthening the enforcement of the Law on Fisheries in the fight against illegal fishing.",""],[1,"113","4","Community Livelihood Development in Protected Areas","Promoting the development of community livelihoods in natural protected areas by linking with tourism through the transformation of natural protected areas into tourist attractions; capacity building for forest communities, communities in the protected areas and the adjacent areas; and equitable benefit-sharing.",""]],"64":[[1,"117","3","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"117","4","Agricultural Legal and Institutional Strengthening","Continuing to build legal frameworks and policies and strengthening institutions to support and create enabling environment for agriculture sector.",""],[1,"117","5","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Production and Modernization Programme","Promoting agricultural production with a focus on enhancing productivity, quality, safety, diversity, values added and resilience through research and development of climate- resilient crops, animal breeds and aquaculture that meet the market demand; management and improvements of soil quality; zoning of cultivation areas and mapping of crop cultivation; promoting agricultural insurance services; strengthening entrepreneurship of agricultural communities; deploying agricultural technical officers to local communities; and strengthening modern, intelligent, digital and secure agricultural techniques.",""],[1,"117","6","Rationalization of Irrigation Investments","Strengthening the rationalization of irrigation investments to ensure water security for agriculture and rural development.",""],[1,"123","2","Smart and Green Agricultural Policy","introducing a smart and green agricultural policy",""],[1,"124","4","Irrigation System Efficiency and Water Security Improvement","Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology shall continue to improve the efficiency of waterworks and the performance, quality, and resilience of irrigation systems, and will strengthen water security and disaster risk management to build climate resilience.","Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology"]],"65":[[1,"117","8","Agricultural Price Stability Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","Ensuring price stability of agricultural products through the establishment and strengthening of coordination mechanisms for monitoring and control, expanding the scope of special financing packages to maintain the price stability for agricultural products, and enhancing the whole value chains of the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"117","8","Special Financing Packages for Agricultural Price Stability","expanding the scope of special financing packages to maintain the price stability for agricultural products",""],[1,"117","8","Agriculture Value Chain Enhancement Initiative","enhancing the whole value chains of the agriculture sector.",""],[1,"118","7","Agricultural Commodity Price Stabilization Strategy Enhancement","Enhance the effectiveness of price-stabilization strategies for key agricultural commodities through proactive monitoring of demand-supply balance, forecasting agricultural production and commodity demand by domestic and international subsector for wide dissemination to farmers, coordinated work with relevant agencies on production, quality processing, sanitary and phytosanitary control, and implementation of targeted financial interventions.",""],[1,"118","13","Market Management and Price Monitoring Strategy","Formulate a strategy to strengthen market management to maintain price stability and safeguard producer and consumer interests through compiling and managing trade statistics as an analytical base, enhancing mechanisms for monitoring commodity prices",""],[1,"119","7","Agrifood Sector Support Mechanisms and Investment Roundtable","Enhance support mechanisms focused on the agrifood sector and establish an agrifood investment roundtable",""]],"66":[[1,"118","4","Modern Agricultural Cooperative Development Support","Advance strategies to build modern agricultural cooperatives through coordinated financing and low-interest credit, together with advisory services and human resource support for cooperatives",""],[1,"118","5","Community-Based Producer Cooperative Support Strategy","Promote strategies for community-based producer cooperatives, including preparation of bankable business plans to access support from financial institutions, effective management and use of community resources, creation and expansion of supplementary community livelihoods, provision of finance and credit for community infrastructure, and development of networks and trust between agricultural communities and business partners to enable effective contract farming",""],[1,"118","6","Agricultural Technical Support and Extension Services","Promote strategies for agricultural technical support services for farmers by deploying agricultural extension officers to communes and sangkats with active agricultural production, and conducting applied agricultural research to increase productivity",""],[1,"119","10","Multi-sectoral Coordination and Partnership Strengthening Mechanism","Promote and strengthen existing multi-sectoral and multi-stakeholder coordination and cooperation mechanisms, while enhancing partnerships at national and sub-national levels",""],[1,"119","11","Capacity Building for Commune Agricultural Officials","Contribute to advancing the Royal Government's priority policies in capacity building for commune agricultural officials, supporting modern agricultural communities, maintaining price stability for agricultural products, and participating in the development of technical and vocational training plans for youth from poor and vulnerable families",""],[1,"119","11","Support for Modern Agricultural Communities","Contribute to advancing the Royal Government's priority policies in capacity building for commune agricultural officials, supporting modern agricultural communities, maintaining price stability for agricultural products, and participating in the development of technical and vocational training plans for youth from poor and vulnerable families",""],[1,"119","11","Youth Technical and Vocational Training Plan Development","Contribute to advancing the Royal Government's priority policies in capacity building for commune agricultural officials, supporting modern agricultural communities, maintaining price stability for agricultural products, and participating in the development of technical and vocational training plans for youth from poor and vulnerable families",""],[1,"119","16","Legal Framework and Technical Standards Development for Producer Services","Develop legal frameworks, technical standards, and associated mechanisms in accordance with essential requirements, while enhancing institutional capacities at all levels and advancing digitalization to improve the efficiency of service delivery to producers",""]],"67":[[1,"24","1","Cultural Heritage Infrastructure and Site Enhancement","Cambodia has improved infrastructure and enhanced the aesthetics of World Heritage sites and key cultural locations to increase their appeal to tourists and promote sustainable development, especially at the Angkor site.",""],[1,"24","1","Cultural and Creative Industries Development Support","At the same time, the production capacity and market for Cambodian cultural and creative goods are also improving through increased domestic demand, entry into foreign markets, the advantages of digital technology, and partnerships among the government, the private sector, and civil society organizations.",""],[1,"24","1","Copyright and Related Rights Strengthening","It has continued to strengthen copyright and related rights and collaborated with various partners to promote the development of arts and culture in Cambodia and the ASEAN region.",""],[1,"30","4","Cultural Conservation Partnership and Anti-Illicit Trade Cooperation","Cambodia has collaborated with various partners to promote cultural conservation in Cambodia and the ASEAN region, especially in preventing the illegal trade of cultural properties.",""]],"68":[[1,"90","7","Sustainable Development Promotion in World Heritage and Cultural Sites","Continue promoting sustainable development in World Heritage sites and other high- potential cultural locations, with a focus on establishing laws and normative legal documents for the management and promotion of cultural aesthetics and cultural landscapes",""],[1,"113","5","Cultural Resource Conservation Guideline","the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts who needs to enact a conservation guideline for this purpose.","Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts"],[1,"113","6","Cultural Heritage Conservation and Registration Programme","Continuing to strengthen the effectiveness of the conservation of cultural heritages - tangible and intangible - through reparations, maintaining in safe places, cleaning, inventory registration, registration in the database, and the preparation of certificates of occupancy and state's title deeds; preparation of applications to register Cambodian cultural and historical heritages, as well as natural and geological heritages, on the National and World Heritage Lists, the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, Memory of the World Register, and other lists of heritages of UNESCO and/or other international institutions; promoting regional and global campaigns about these cultural heritages; and continuing to focus on restoring and strengthening the extinct intangible cultural heritages or those with dangers of disappearance.",""],[1,"113","7","Eco- and Cultural Tourism Policy Development and Implementation","Formulating and implementing policies for the development of eco- and cultural tourism of Cambodia for the medium and long-terms under the approach of \"Development for Conservation, Conservation for Development\" to optimize the attraction of tourists, and their lengths of stay through connecting tourism with land and nature.",""],[1,"115","10","Heritage Structure Conservation and Restoration Programme","Continue conserving heritage structures through repair and other techniques, with emphasis on restoring the integrity and appearance of key monuments that have been degraded or nearly lost due to human, natural, and age-related factors",""],[1,"115","11","Antiquities Conservation and Recovery Initiative","Continue conserving antiquities, works of art, and ethnographic objects through repair and other methods, including monitoring and legal research to secure the return of antiquities that are illegally held or trafficked, domestically and abroad",""],[1,"115","12","Archaeological Site Conservation and Protection Programme","Continue conserving archaeological sites by increasing and accelerating state registration and titling, installing protective boundary markers, reducing offenses at heritage sites, and preparing conservation guidelines",""],[1,"115","13","Intangible Cultural Heritage Safeguarding and Promotion Programme","Continue safeguarding and promoting intangible cultural heritage by revitalizing and strengthening elements that have been lost or are at risk, ensuring their sustainable presence in society, reinforcing cultural artistic productions in line with Khmer standards and protocols, showcasing classical and traditional performing arts, and preserving and promoting the diversity of cultural expressions, especially those of indigenous peoples and vulnerable groups",""],[1,"115","14","Arts and Culture Promotion and Artist Support Programme","Continue promoting Cambodian arts and culture by sending artistic troupes to perform at various events and by supporting talented and professional artists across all art forms, to strengthen national identity, prestige, soft power, and the country's image",""],[1,"115","15","Heritage Nomination Dossier Preparation and Assessment","Continue assessing feasibility and preparing nomination dossiers for the inscription of Cambodian cultural and historical heritage on the national heritage list, the world heritage list, the intangible cultural heritage of humanity list, the memory of the world register, the UNESCO creative cities network, the tentative list, and other UNESCO culture-related lists, as well as those of other international institutions",""],[1,"115","16","Strategic Cross-Sectoral Coordination Mechanisms","Continue strengthening and expanding systems and mechanisms for strategic cross- sectoral coordination, including national and international cooperation, in particular the",""],[1,"116","1","Cultural Heritage Financing and Technical Support Mechanisms","ICC-Angkor, Preah Vihear, and Sambor Prey Kuk mechanisms, to mobilize financing and technical support for conservation and promotion of national cultural heritage, with a focus on key public investment and technical assistance projects.",""]],"69":[[1,"91","3","Electricity Tariff Reduction and Supply Stability Measure","Continuing to maintain price stability and considering the possibility of reducing the electricity tariffs, as well as ensuring sufficiency and stability of electricity supplies for industrial and agricultural sectors.",""],[1,"91","4","Renewable Energy Promotion and Energy Efficiency Program","Promoting the use of renewable energy and implementation of energy efficiency program to the utmost potential.",""],[1,"92","11","Power Source Diversification and Grid Stability Programme","Expand development of new power sources with a focus on lowering the cost of the generation mix, reducing day-night and dry-wet season imbalances, strengthening transmission quality and system stability, and maximizing integration of clean, sustainable energy in the national master plan",""],[1,"93","1","Energy Efficiency Improvement Measures","Improve energy-efficiency in the industrial, residential, building, public, and transport sectors",""],[1,"97","11","Electricity Transmission and Distribution Network Upgrade","Improve electricity supply quality by expanding and upgrading transmission networks, substations, and distribution systems to achieve nationwide, mutually reinforcing interconnection, meeting actual demand, and strengthen supply stability",""],[1,"97","12","National Grid Integration and Electricity Supply Upgrading","Continue integrating remaining areas into the national grid so nationwide supply operates under the national system, and conduct reviews, studies, and investments to enhance the quality, safety, and reliability of electricity supply across all types and voltage levels nationwide.",""],[1,"101","4","Electricity Grid Connection Expansion","Promote electricity grid connections for industries, businesses, and households that do not yet have access to electricity, while expanding the implementation of the \"Electricity for poor households\" project, and strengthening effective monitoring and resolution processes for initial electricity connection requests",""],[1,"101","5","Electricity Tariff Reduction Plan","Develop and implement plans to reduce electricity fees to further ease the burden on low- and middle-income households, and to lower electricity costs for industry and commerce in order to enhance the competitiveness of Cambodia's industrial and commercial sectors, while continuing to explore further possibilities for additional tariff reductions.",""]],"70":[[1,"122","7","Nationwide Electricity Distribution Network Expansion","Expand nationwide electricity distribution network coverage to ensure households and businesses receive power commensurate with demand",""],[1,"122","8","Advanced Metering and Data Logging Installation","Install mechanical meters, electronic metering systems, and advanced data-logging technologies to ensure high accuracy and efficiency",""],[1,"122","9","Public Concern Redress Mechanism for Consumption Issues","Strengthen mechanisms to address public concerns regarding increased consumption, ensuring accuracy and fairness between suppliers and consumers.",""]],"71":[[1,"23","2","Revised Electricity Development Master Plan","the Royal Government has issued a revised master plan for electricity development for 2022-2040",""],[1,"23","2","Rooftop Solar Energy Use Policy","a policy to permit the use of rooftop solar energy has been announced",""],[1,"23","2","Energy Transition Project","The first phase of the Energy Transition Project for 2023-2025 is being implemented",""],[1,"23","2","Electric Vehicle Roadmap","a roadmap for the use of electric vehicles ... are being prepared",""],[1,"23","2","Carbon Neutrality Roadmap","a roadmap toward carbon neutrality by 2050 are being prepared",""],[1,"123","12","Climate Finance Mobilization Mechanism","Mobilize climate finance from external sources, such as the Green Climate Fund, the Adaptation Fund, and the Loss and Damage Fund, to support implementation of national plans and strategies, Cambodia's Nationally Determined Contribution under the UNFCCC, and the long-term low-carbon development strategy",""],[1,"124","2","Renewable Energy Policy and Regulatory Update","Update policies and normative legal instruments to increase the share of renewable energy in Cambodia's energy mix",""]],"72":[[1,"87","10","National Petroleum Company Establishment and Operationalization","continuing to accelerate the development of extractive industries and supporting industries through establishing and operationalizing a national petroleum company",""],[1,"87","10","Oil Well Re-Operationalization Programme","continuing to accelerate the development of petroleum and gas sector, especially re- operationalizing oil wells",""],[1,"87","10","Mineral Resources Investment Promotion","continuing to encourage the investments into mineral resources industries",""],[1,"87","10","Policy Formulation for Resource-Based Production","considering the possibility of formulating policies for producing resources with which Cambodia is well endowed",""],[1,"88","8","National Petroleum Sector Policy","Formulate a national policy on the petroleum sector",""],[1,"88","8","Sustainable Mineral Resource Development Strategy","a strategy to promote sustainable mineral resource development",""],[1,"88","8","LPG Supply Chain Master Plan","a master plan for the LPG supply chain",""],[1,"88","8","Strategic Petroleum Reserve Master Plan","a master plan for a strategic petroleum reserve",""],[1,"88","8","Pipeline Gas Supply and Distribution Regulatory Framework","a regulatory framework for the supply and distribution of gaseous fuels via pipeline networks",""],[1,"88","9","Petrochemical and Petroleum Investment Incentive Policy Development","Study and develop incentive policies to attract investment in the petrochemical industry and the petroleum sector across upstream and downstream segments",""],[1,"88","10","National Geoscience Infrastructure and Geopark Development","Operationalize the national geoscience laboratory, establish a national mineral core repository, a national geoscience museum and archive, and designate national geopark areas",""],[1,"88","11","Construction Minerals Market Assessment and Compliance Improvement","Assess demand and supply of construction minerals, develop a construction-mineral price index, and inspect and raise compliance of fuel and gas stations to at least 90 percent",""],[1,"88","12","Petroleum Production Resumption and Maritime Joint Development Negotiations","Seek options to resume petroleum production in Block A and continue facilitating negotiations to reach agreement on joint development in areas of overlapping maritime claims.",""]],"73":[[1,"93","2","Nuclear Safety and Security Governance Framework Strengthening","Strengthen and expand safety and security governance frameworks for the peaceful use of nuclear energy, including radiation",""],[1,"93","3","Civilian Nuclear Energy and Radiation Framework Development","Continue developing the legal, regulatory, and technical framework for civilian nuclear energy and radiation",""],[1,"93","4","Nuclear Safety and Technical Inspection Regulatory Strengthening","Reinforce regulatory functions for safety, security, and technical inspection to ensure compliance with applicable regulatory and technical instruments across all services involving the peaceful use of nuclear energy, including radiation",""],[1,"93","5","Civilian Nuclear and Radiation Sector Capacity-Building Programme","Build human capital and institutional capacity by training staff to international best practice, equipping them with appropriate tools and technical materials, and strengthening management and support for the three S's 'safety, security, and safeguards' in the civilian nuclear and radiation sector",""],[1,"93","6","Technical Assistance Mobilization for Radiation Safety and Security Frameworks","Broaden cooperation with international organizations and development partners to mobilize technical-assistance projects that strengthen radiation safety and security frameworks in support of the energy, health, agriculture, water resources, environment, research, industry, and cultural heritage sectors",""],[1,"93","7","Public Outreach and Awareness on Peaceful Nuclear Energy Use","Scale up public outreach and awareness on the peaceful use of nuclear energy and radiation and its benefits, to contribute to Cambodia's future socio-economic development.",""]],"74":[[1,"124","6","Private Sector Energy Investment Mobilization Mechanism","Promote investment mechanisms through (1) attracting additional private sector participation beyond public investment capacity to develop projects in line with the power development master plan 2022-2040, Cambodia's energy efficiency development plan, and Cambodia's pathway toward carbon neutrality, and (2) implementing investments in energy projects in accordance with Cambodian laws and procedures, with innovation and dynamism, to maximize economic and social benefits",""],[1,"124","7","Private Participation in Electricity Supply and Tariff Reform","Promote business mechanisms through (1) opening electricity generation, transmission, and distribution to private participation to attract investment, reduce price gaps between urban, peri-urban, and rural areas, and move toward uniform nationwide tariffs, (2) assessing options to further reduce electricity tariffs to meet economic and social objectives while maintaining the financial sustainability of the power sector, and (3) assessing the feasibility of capital subsidies or viability gap funding to develop energy supply in remote areas in an environmentally responsible manner",""],[1,"124","8","Energy Development Environmental and Social Safeguards Coordination","Promote other enabling mechanisms, including (1) maximizing avoidance and mitigation of environmental and social impacts in energy development through close coordination with relevant ministries and institutions","relevant ministries and institutions"],[1,"124","8","Electricity User Environmental Compliance Support","assisting electricity users to comply with environmental and climate requirements",""],[1,"124","8","International Power Trade and Energy Cooperation Expansion","strengthening and expanding international cooperation within and beyond the region to enable power trade, diversify electricity sources and enhance complementarity, exchange experience, share new technologies, and expand financing sources",""],[1,"124","8","International Climate and Carbon Neutrality Engagement","engaging with international organizations on mechanisms to address climate change and advance carbon neutrality",""]],"75":[[1,"109","9","Gender-Related Investment and Women’s Empowerment Initiative","Increasing investment in gender-related agenda, and empowering women and girls in the fields of economy, education, health, and public leadership",""],[1,"109","12","Gender Mainstreaming Framework","Ministry of Women's Affairs shall focus on the following priority actions: Gender mainstreaming framework","Ministry of Women's Affairs"],[1,"110","1","Gender Situation Research and Supportive Initiatives","Promote research and studies on the gender situation across sectors in line with societal developments, and design initiatives on supportive measures and related programs",""],[1,"110","2","Gender Mainstreaming and Gender-Responsive Budgeting in Sectoral Policies and Programs","Strengthen and expand gender mainstreaming in the formulation and implementation of sectoral policies and programs, including the application of gender-responsive budgeting",""],[1,"110","3","Gender Equality Outreach and Mindset Change Programme","Expand programs and outreach to foster changes in societal mindsets and behaviors in support of gender equality",""],[1,"110","4","Gender Mainstreaming Monitoring and Evaluation System","Strengthen monitoring, oversight, and evaluation systems and mechanisms for gender mainstreaming in all sectors, alongside efforts to enhance women's economic empowerment.",""],[1,"110","10","Inter-Agency Coordination Mechanisms for Multisectoral Social Protection Measures","Lead and coordinate inter-agency mechanisms at national and subnational levels to advance multisectoral measures that prevent and address all forms of negative societal influences, through the implementation of necessary interventions contributing to the promotion of social ethics, women's status and value, and Cambodian families",""],[1,"110","11","Social Ethics and Family Outreach Programs","Design and coordinate the implementation of education and outreach programs to promote social ethics, women's status, and the Cambodian family, using modern platforms and all media channels",""],[1,"110","13","Gender Mainstreaming Across the Health Sector","Mainstream gender across the health sector, including policies, strategic plans, action plans, and programs such as reproductive health, maternal and child health, mental health, eye health, nutrition, food security, communicable and noncommunicable diseases, and prevention of substance use including drugs and alcohol",""],[1,"110","16","Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment in Social Protection Framework","Contribute to advancing gender equality and women's empowerment throughout the formulation and implementation of the social protection framework.",""],[1,"110","17","Gender Mainstreaming in Legislative Drafting and Justice Reform","Mainstream gender throughout legislative drafting and implementation, and within legal and justice system reform programs",""]],"76":[[1,"112","6","Sustainable Forest and Wildlife Resource Management","Strengthening harmonious and sustainable management, conservation, protection and development of Cambodia's important ecosystems through the continued management of forest and wildlife resources by maintaining the forest cover of at least 60% of the total land area; reforestation; prevention and timely response to wildfires and conservation of peatlands; promoting the development of environment friendly and sustainable plantations; sustainable reduction of reliance on non-timber forest products; preventing encroachment on forest lands and natural protected areas; promoting the conservation of natural protected areas, forests and wildlife; and cracking down on forest crimes, wildlife trafficking, and natural resource crimes.",""],[1,"113","1","National Action Programs for Soil Conservation and Productivity","Continuing to promote the management of agricultural land resources through the implementation of national action programs to combat soil degradation, prevent soil corrosion, and enhance soil productivity.",""],[1,"113","2","Sustainable Land Use and Protected Area Management","Promoting sustainable land use through strengthening the implementation of national land use plans; demarcation and zoning of management areas; registration of natural protected areas; as well as the formulation of management plans for each protected area in accordance with the National Protected Area Strategic Management Plan and the Law on Natural Protected Areas.",""],[1,"113","3","National Protected Area Strategic Management Plan Implementation","through the implementation of the National Protected Area Strategic Management Plan",""],[1,"113","3","Protected Areas Data Modernization and Digitalization","modernization and digitalization of data related to natural protected areas and their geographical locations",""],[1,"113","3","Payment for Ecosystem Services Promotion","encouraging Payment of Ecosystem Services (PES) to ensure financial sustainability in the management and conservation of natural resources",""],[1,"113","3","Natural Resource Crime Prevention and Suppression","prevention and suppression of natural resource crimes",""],[1,"113","3","Nature-Based Solutions Promotion","the use of nature-based solutions (NBS)",""],[1,"113","3","Ecosystem and Forest Cover Data Updating","updating data on forest cover, wetlands, peatlands, mangrove forests, natural floodplains, and other important ecosystems",""]],"77":[[1,"29","2","Forest Community Creation and Restoration Programme","In the agriculture, forestry, and fisheries sector, the Royal Government has promoted the creation of forest communities, forest conservation, and forest restoration through tree planting.",""],[1,"29","2","Timber Plantation Preservation and Agroforestry Plot Maintenance","Additionally, 468 community forest agreements have been made, covering 385 938 hectares, and 115 community forest management plans covering 79 250 hectares have been approved.",""],[1,"29","2","Forest Restoration and Promotion Stations","The government has created 91 forest restoration and promotion stations, covering a total area of 506 822 hectares, with 16 of these stations having land titles for 106 907 hectares.",""],[1,"29","2","Private Sector Tree Planting Partnership Support","This is done to prepare and encourage private sector and partner investment in tree planting, in the form of company partnerships and family plantations on a total area of 81 802 hectares.",""],[1,"29","2","Economic Land Concession Tree Planting Project","A project to plant trees on economic land concessions is being implemented on a contracted area of 280 870 hectares.",""],[1,"29","2","Forest Law Enforcement and Timber Trade Control","The government is also collaborating with relevant parties to enforce laws effectively, especially by monitoring and strengthening the management of timber industries, processing factories, and wood businesses, and responsibly preventing the unauthorized export of timber and all types of processed wood products.",""],[1,"29","2","Forest Destruction and Land Encroachment Prevention Measures","Strict measures are being implemented to prevent and eliminate forest destruction and land encroachment.",""],[1,"29","3","REDD+ Project Expansion Studies","Feasibility studies are being conducted to establish more REDD+ projects on an additional 1.19 million hectares, bringing the total REDD+ project area to 2.46 million hectares, or 34.1% of all protected areas",""]],"78":[[1,"113","10","Policy Implementation Evaluation and Coordination Mechanism","Strengthen the effectiveness of policy implementation through evaluations of policies, strategies, and action plans, reviews of the implementation of laws, regulations, and normative legal documents, enhanced coordination mechanisms with ministries, institutions, development partners, and the private sector, and dissemination of environmental policies, strategies, action plans, guidelines, decisions, and technical reports",""],[1,"114","1","Environmental Information Outreach and Green Initiative Promotion","Enhance outreach by increasing the dissemination of environmental information, strengthening the environmental data management center, encouraging green schools and green pagodas as well as legal entities and individuals participating in environmental initiatives, and promoting reduced use of plastics",""],[1,"114","2","Pollution Control and Environmental Compliance Strengthening","Strengthen pollution control through increased compliance monitoring of laws, management plans, and agreements related to environmental impact assessment and strategic environmental assessment, monitoring the implementation of normative legal documents, management plans, and agreements related to impact assessments, upgrading solid, liquid, plastic, and hazardous waste management, modernizing environmental quality management, promoting implementation of integrated waste management policies linked to decentralization and deconcentration and the Safe Village-Commune-Sangkat policy, modernizing pollution monitoring systems, and strengthening research on archaeological sites and fossil stations inside and outside protected areas",""]],"79":[[1,"114","3","Protected Areas Management Strengthening Programme","Improve management of protected areas by strengthening the management of national parks, wildlife sanctuaries, protected landscapes, multiple-use zones, Ramsar sites, natural heritage areas, and marine national parks, promoting biodiversity conservation, strengthening monitoring of forest cover change, expanding and restoring forest cover, preparing and revising legal instruments to support and manage community protected areas and cultural heritage, building the capacity of subnational officials and community committees on sustainable agroforestry, harvesting, and processing of forest products, strengthening community-based management of protected areas, and strengthening the operations and management of protected area community networks and women's networks",""],[1,"114","4","Community Livelihoods and Heritage Conservation Programme","Improve community livelihoods by enhancing food security, nutrition, and clean living, promoting and establishing green tourism destinations, strengthening conservation and management of natural and cultural resources, promoting preservation of the traditions and customs of local communities, especially indigenous peoples in protected areas, and expanding cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions on the dissemination, establishment, management, conservation, and development of natural heritage areas and natural resources.","relevant ministries and institutions"],[1,"114","9","Agricultural Resource Conservation Fund","Establish an agricultural resource conservation fund by defining funding sources, mobilizing and collecting resources from all channels including the private sector and development partners, and strengthening the management of conservation funds for agricultural, fisheries and forestry community groups.",""]],"80":[[1,"121","7","Cambodia Coastal Zone Land Use Planning and Boundary Demarcation","- Promote the management and development of Cambodia's coastal zones by formulating the Cambodia coastal land use plan with a vision to 2050, developing land use plans for Kampot, Kep, and Koh Kong Provinces, and updating the land use plan for Preah Sihanouk Province; prepare master plans and land utilization strategies for islands and coastal strips; construct and install boundary markers for coastal zones, sea inlets, rivers, canals, streams, lakes, waterways, and water surfaces linked to the sea; conduct inspections and evaluations of scenic recreational sandy beaches and canals, and organize",""],[1,"122","1","Coastal Biodiversity Assessment and Marine Resource Zoning","study biodiversity and delineate potential resource areas within Koh Rong marine national park and the offshore marine domains of Kep and Koh Kong provinces",""]],"81":[[1,"116","7","Water Resources and River Basin Management Support","Support and strengthen operations and effective management of water resources and river basins",""],[1,"116","8","River Basin Cooperation and Partnership Initiative","Promote cooperation and partnerships to ensure sustainable river basin development and management",""],[1,"116","9","Public Awareness and Outreach for CNMC Knowledge Products","Enhance public awareness and outreach to increase participation and the use of CNMC knowledge products, tools, and services for sectoral management and development.",""]],"82":[[1,"91","6","Water Supply Master Plan Development and Implementation","Developing and implementing water supply master plans, in order to achieve the goal of 100% access to water supply in 2030.",""],[1,"91","7","Water Supply Sector Regulatory and Legal Framework Reform","Continuing to undertake a review and establishing legal frameworks for the management of water supply sector, especially simplifying the process for network connection request, strengthening the implementation of permit condition, and preserving the raw water sources, as well as establishing important institutional mechanisms, and setting up the water supply regulator in order to manage, develop and address challenges, aiming at achieving water security.",""],[1,"91","8","Public-Private Investment Incentives for Water Supply in Priority Locations","Enhancing the strategic roles and participation of the state and creating incentives for the private sector for their investments in water supply sector in the prioritized geographic locations, such as SEZs, clusters of micro, small, and medium enterprises, industrial parks, and economic poles in cities and provinces.",""],[1,"91","9","Urban Water Supply Automation and Incentive Support","Continuing to promote automation and incentivize water supply authorities in municipal- provincial urban areas.",""],[1,"93","9","National Clean Water and Sanitation Policy Update","Update the National Policy on clean water and Sanitation in line with socio-economic conditions, develop a sector development plan for clean water, and strengthen the strategic role of state-owned water utilities",""],[1,"93","10","Water Supply Service Quality Improvement","Improve the quality of water supply services to comply with applicable norms and technical standards, and with national drinking water quality standards",""],[1,"93","11","Water Supply Management Law Implementation and Public Awareness Campaign","Strengthen implementation and broad dissemination of the law on water supply management and raise public awareness of the benefits of clean water and participation to achieve \"clean water for all.\"",""],[1,"93","12","Establishment of a Cambodian Water Supply Regulator","Reinforce the regulatory function by studying the establishment of a Cambodian water supply regulator, with a focus on oversight of private operators",""],[1,"93","13","Clean Water Sector Human Resource Development and Service Expansion","Promote human resource development in the clean water sector, expand service coverage, and continue implementing the connection fee subsidy policy for household access to clean water",""],[1,"93","14","Investment Project Financing Support in Low-Potential Areas","Provide financing support for investment projects to accelerate development in low- potential areas, and enhance cooperation with development partners, particularly to operationalize a clean water sector development fund.",""],[1,"93","15","Rural Clean Water Infrastructure and Technology Development","Ministry of Rural Development shall focus on implementing priority actions, including establishing rural clean water infrastructure, improving the efficiency of rural clean water use, and conducting research and development on clean water technologies.","Ministry of Rural Development"]],"83":[[1,"119","2","Integrated Water Resources and Irrigation Systems Improvement","Improve the efficiency of waterworks and the performance, quality, and resilience of irrigation systems by enhancing integrated water resources management within river basins and sub-basins, and by strengthening the management, development, and operation of irrigation systems",""],[1,"119","3","Water Security and Disaster Management for Climate Resilience","Strengthen water security and disaster management to build climate resilience through improved management and impact mitigation using both structural and non-structural measures",""],[1,"119","4","National Water and Meteorological Data Management Center","Strengthen management and the use of new technologies and innovation for water and meteorological information and data systems by establishing and operationalizing a national center for water and meteorological data management, upgrading water and irrigation information systems, and building capacity to manage hydrological and meteorological data and innovation",""],[1,"119","5","Water Resources Protection and Conservation Regulatory Reform","Enhance the effectiveness of protection and conservation in the water resources sector through the development and updating of relevant laws, regulations, and procedures, and by strengthening measures for prevention, protection, and conservation of water resources.",""],[1,"120","10","Water Reservoir and Source Restoration","restoring water reservoirs and sources",""],[1,"123","3","Water Infrastructure Development and Treatment Systems","Making a boost for and building water infrastructures, including water treatment systems to ensure water security and environmental sustainability and to respond to climate change.",""],[1,"123","4","IT and AI for Water Security and Environmental Management","Continuing to increase the use of IT, to promote environmentally friendly and climate friendly practices, such as technologies, the use of nature-based solutions, and the uses of AI model and technology in the management of water security, environment and so on.",""],[1,"123","5","Environmental, Water, and Disaster Policy Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen laws, regulations and policies related to the environment, water, natural disasters, as well as green diplomacy, to ensure sustainable ecosystem and contribution to the mitigation of climate change.",""]],"84":[[1,"81","2","Rural Environmental Sanitation Strengthening Program","Ministry of Rural Development shall focus on implementing priority actions to strengthen rural environmental sanitation, including the development of rural sanitation infrastructure, the promotion of hygienic living practices, health and sanitation education, and rigorous, applied research on sanitation technologies, with the aim of advancing equitable, resilient, and sustainable rural development.","Ministry of Rural Development"]],"85":[[1,"120","5","Urban Expansion and New Urban Area Development","The strategic objectives are to expand the existing urban areas and to develop new ones in the capital city and provinces;",""],[1,"120","5","Public Gardens and Green Parks Development","to create public gardens and green parks;",""],[1,"120","5","Urban Management and Modernization Strengthening","to strengthen urban management and modernization to ensure safety, beauty, good environment, and well-being of people, as well as socio-economic efficiency.",""],[1,"120","5","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:","Ministries-institutions"],[1,"120","7","Urban Management Capacity Strengthening and Land Use Planning","Strengthening the urban management competency, developing plans for land management and urbanization for municipalities-districts-Khans, communes-Sangkats throughout the country, formulating guiding strategies for land use zoning and management of residences, based on topographic and IT data.",""],[1,"147","18","District-Level Land Use Master Plan","Master plan for land use at district level",""]],"86":[[1,"11","3","UN Peacekeeping Participation","They also contributed to humanitarian efforts in the region and globally by participating in UN peacekeeping operations",""],[1,"56","7","Armed Forces Institutional and Human Capital Development","Further improving the capability of the armed forces through institutional and human capital development; emphasizing on raising living standards and welfare of the armed forces; and implementing appropriate policies for the retired armed forces, and for those who have lost their ability to work, as well as for those with disabilities in their sacrifices for the sake of national security.",""],[1,"56","7","Armed Forces Welfare and Retirement Support Policies","Further improving the capability of the armed forces through institutional and human capital development; emphasizing on raising living standards and welfare of the armed forces; and implementing appropriate policies for the retired armed forces, and for those who have lost their ability to work, as well as for those with disabilities in their sacrifices for the sake of national security.",""],[1,"58","1","Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Professional Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the professional capability of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces through the implementation of the \"3 Strategies and 10 Development Actions\", as well as updating and promoting the effectiveness of the armed forces in fulfilling their roles and responsibilities",""],[1,"58","2","Armed Forces Modernization and Training Capacity Development","Develop human resources and strengthen the capacity of the armed forces by advancing modernization, integrating appropriate technologies, and enhancing the quality of training, with particular emphasis on professional military education and development of a younger generation of armed forces personnel to ensure continuity, while reinforcing cooperation with allied countries",""],[1,"58","3","Veterans and Military Families Support and Social Land Concessions Project","Continue to pay attention to veterans, disable soldiers, the families of fallen soldiers, and the families of armed forces personnel, in accordance with policies of the Royal Government, particularly sustained efforts to provide and enhance the effectiveness of social land concessions management and development project for communities, military families, and armed forces units along the border areas",""],[1,"58","4","Armed Forces Inter-Branch and Civilian Cooperation","Promote cooperation among all branches of the armed forces, as well as between the armed forces and relevant ministries-institutions.",""],[1,"58","5","Military Human Resources Skills Development Programme","Develop human resources within Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in professional skills in agriculture sector (crop, livestock raising, and self-employ skills), handicraft, micro small and medium enterprises, mining, and information technology.",""],[1,"58","6","Technology and Innovation Cooperation Mechanism","Establish cooperation with ministries-institutions and private sector partners to promote the development of technology and innovation, as well as to ensure timely sharing of information and experiences.",""]],"87":[[1,"76","5","LDC Graduation Transitional Strategy","Prepare and implement a smooth transitional strategy for Cambodia's graduation from least developed country (LDC) status with dynamism",""],[1,"89","9","Tourism Sector Recovery and Revitalization Roadmap","Continue implementing the Roadmap for the Recovery and Revitalization of Cambodia's Tourism Sector during and after COVID-19, delivered in three phases: crisis management under the new normal with restoration planning, post-COVID-19 sector recovery, and preparation for a new future for Cambodian tourism",""],[1,"89","11","Domestic Tourism Strengthening and International Market Expansion","Strengthen domestic tourism and expand international visitor attraction to new markets, while reactivating key source markets including China, the Republic of Korea, Japan, and long-haul markets",""],[1,"89","12","National Brand Management Strengthening","Implement priority initiatives, including: (1) strengthening management of Cambodia's national brand",""],[1,"89","12","Tourism Promotion in Priority Markets","enhancing promotion of Cambodia's tourism appeal in priority markets",""],[1,"89","12","Competitive and Diversified Tourism Product Development","developing competitive and diversified tourism products",""],[1,"89","12","Tourism Sector Resource and Attraction Strategy Strengthening","strengthening sectoral resources and competitive visitor-attraction strategies",""]],"88":[[1,"89","13","Tourism Development Strategic Plan Preparation","Accelerate preparation of the Tourism Development Strategic Plan 2025-2035",""],[1,"89","14","Tourism Master Plan Implementation and Scenic Route Development","Continue implementing the master tourism development plans for Siem Reap, Kep, and Mondulkiri, and develop scenic routes and tourism corridors connecting priority tourism poles",""],[1,"89","14","Digitalization of Tourism Industry Governance","while further strengthening industry governance through digitalization",""],[1,"89","15","International Tourism Cooperation Promotion","Continue promoting international cooperation within UNWTO, regional, subregional, and bilateral frameworks to elevate Cambodia's profile on the international stage.",""]],"89":[[1,"100","5","Overseas Labor Market Expansion and Migrant Worker Protection","Continuing to expand labor market abroad; preventing illegal Cambodian labor migration; training and promoting the rights, interests, and dignity of Cambodian migrant workers; developing mechanisms for skills recognition; and activating the mobility of the social security system.",""],[1,"100","5","Skills Recognition Mechanism for Migrant Workers","developing mechanisms for skills recognition",""],[1,"100","5","Social Security Portability Mechanism","activating the mobility of the social security system.",""],[1,"100","10","Labor Migration Management and Protection Program","Strengthen the safe, quality, and effective management of labor migration by expanding overseas labor markets with favorable working conditions, enhancing transparency, accountability, and efficiency in the recruitment, training, and deployment of workers abroad, strengthening management mechanisms and protection services for Cambodian migrant workers in destination countries, improving reintegration mechanisms for returning migrant workers, and reinforcing the management of foreign labor in Cambodia.",""]],"90":[[1,"104","1","Wholesale Market Establishment","Measures include establishing wholesale markets, facilitating memoranda of understanding between the public and private sectors to promote processing of agricultural products for domestic markets and export, and setting up Cambodian private trade centers abroad to promote information on trade, investment, culture, tourism, and Cambodia's potential products.",""],[1,"104","1","Public-Private Agricultural Processing MoUs","Measures include establishing wholesale markets, facilitating memoranda of understanding between the public and private sectors to promote processing of agricultural products for domestic markets and export, and setting up Cambodian private trade centers abroad to promote information on trade, investment, culture, tourism, and Cambodia's potential products.",""],[1,"104","1","Cambodian Private Trade Centers Abroad","Measures include establishing wholesale markets, facilitating memoranda of understanding between the public and private sectors to promote processing of agricultural products for domestic markets and export, and setting up Cambodian private trade centers abroad to promote information on trade, investment, culture, tourism, and Cambodia's potential products.",""]],"91":[[1,"120","9","Revival of Investment in Unfinished Buildings and Affordable Housing Conversion","Stimulating the revival of investment in the construction of the unfinished buildings in Preah Sihanouk province; incentivizing the transformation of those buildings into affordable housing;",""],[1,"121","6","Affordable and Climate-Resilient Housing Investment Initiative","Expedite housing and social land concession initiatives by mobilizing private sector involvement, non-governmental organizations, and relevant stakeholders to invest in affordable and climate-resilient housing construction; secure financing for the establishment and/or administration of housing funds and credit facilities; promote the development of housing credit service information systems in capitals and provinces;",""],[1,"121","6","Social Land Concession Allocation and Land Titling Programme","continue facilitating the allocation of social land concessions to former armed forces personnel, general poor civilian families, and military and national police families along border areas; sustain collaboration with provincial administrations to identify lands for distribution to landless or land-deficient citizens, families, or former armed forces members; persist with land registration and issuance of land titles to eligible concessionaires in accordance with established criteria; and implement the social land concession initiative titled \"program for providing land for forest protection to foster joint sustainable development.\"",""]],"93":[[1,"120","10","Land, Urbanization, and Construction Law Review","Undertaking a study on the feasibility of amending laws and regulations related to land management, urbanization and construction that came into effect in 1994, to be in alignment with current social, economic, cultural, and environmental context",""],[1,"121","4","Land Use Planning and Urbanization Reform Programme","Advance land use planning and urbanization initiatives by promoting the execution of land management and utilization policies to transform Preah Sihanouk Province into a model multi-purpose special economic zone, and to develop Cambodia's coastal provinces into interconnected multi-purpose economic corridors; additionally, prioritize the development of land use and urbanization master plans, enhance the efficiency of land and urban development management, foster human resource development, institutional strengthening, and good governance in the sectors of land use planning, urbanization, and construction, conduct research and develop digital systems for land use and urbanization data, and expedite the preparation of physical plans across all administrative levels along with associated legal instruments for land use planning and urban management",""],[1,"121","5","Construction Sector Regulatory Enforcement and Digital Management Upgrade","Enhance management and development in the construction sector by continuing to bolster the effective enforcement of construction laws, improving oversight and public service delivery in construction, integrating information technology for construction data management, advancing digital urban visual mapping programs, and piloting initial registration applications for enterprises or companies examining blueprints via digital platforms",""],[1,"122","2","Construction Technical Regulations and Standards Development","Develop and reinforce technical construction regulations by establishing technical standards for construction in areas including concrete building components, steel construction elements, load calculations, geotechnical soil and foundation aspects, fire safety, electrical systems, clean water and wastewater infrastructure, and fire safety protocols under the Secretariat of the National Council for Construction Technical Regulations;",""],[1,"122","2","Construction Technical Glossary and Legal Instruments Smartphone Access Program","create the \"construction technical glossary\" program and the \"Laws and Legal Instruments in the Construction Sector\" program for smartphone accessibility;",""],[1,"122","2","Smart City Technology Research and Application in Construction","research, develop, and apply smart city technologies within the construction domain",""],[1,"122","3","National Construction Laboratory Strengthening","Strengthen the operations of the national construction laboratory by providing efficient and timely responses to requests for testing construction materials, equipment, and products; managing and enhancing the quality of construction materials, equipment, and products; overseeing construction testing to ensure result accuracy; conducting research and development on domestic construction materials, equipment, and products; managing and improving public service delivery in testing activities; and preparing and administering data related to geotechnical elements, construction materials, equipment, and products",""],[1,"122","4","Construction, Urbanization, and Land Governance Policy and Legal Framework Reform","Formulate policies, laws, and strategic frameworks by developing the national policy on construction sector development, the national policy on urbanization, the national policy on architecture, the national policy framework on promoting domestic construction materials usage, land use and urbanization plans integrated with economic corridors, and by drafting the land law, the law on land use planning and urbanization, the law on housing, the law on surveying and mapping, the law on management and development of Cambodia's coastal zones, along with sub-decrees and related legal documents pertaining to land use planning, urbanization, and construction activities.",""]],"94":[[1,"107","7","Microfinance Supervision Strengthening and Basel Principles Implementation Plan","Strengthen supervision of microfinance institutions and develop a plan to promote implementation of the Basel committee on banking supervision's core principles for effective banking supervision for microfinance activities, through ongoing supervision and issuance of necessary regulations in line with international standards",""],[1,"107","8","Enforcement Against Illegal Microfinance Operators","Continue to reinforce law enforcement by taking stringent measures against microfinance operators that refuse to register and continue to operate illegally",""],[1,"107","12","Non-Bank Financial Sector Policy and Institutional Framework Development","Continue to develop the policy, strategic, and institutional framework through ongoing research and the development of indicators for the non-bank financial sector, while strengthening and expanding cooperation with regional financial authorities",""],[1,"107","13","Non-Bank Financial Market Regulatory Development","Continue to develop the non-bank financial market by issuing key regulations that promote market growth, innovation, and diversification of financial products and services",""],[1,"107","14","Non-Bank Financial Sector Customer and Consumer Protection Framework","Establish a customer and consumer protection framework by preparing a draft law and normative legal documents for the non-bank financial sector",""],[1,"107","16","Non-Bank Financial Services Authority Capacity and Supervision Strengthening","Continue to enhance the operational effectiveness of the Non-Bank Financial Services Authority by developing technical frameworks to support supervision and monitoring, and by strengthening staff capacity.",""]],"95":[[1,"11","5","Public Service Reform and Human Resource Management Enhancement","the Royal Government has enhanced human resource management and development at both the national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"12","1","Civil Service Salary and Identification Modernization","The government has reformed the salary system, ensuring on-time and regular bi-weekly payments through bank transfers, and increased data security.",""],[1,"12","1","Public Sector Compensation and Pension Enhancement","The government has increased salaries and functional allowances for civil servants, armed forces, and other officials within the limits of the national budget.",""],[1,"12","1","Civil Servant and Veteran Social Security Benefit Expansion","It has also consistently increased social security benefits for former civil servants and veterans, especially their monthly pensions, and reduced the gap between minimum and maximum pensions by raising the minimum monthly pension.",""],[1,"12","1","Merit-Based Civil Service Recruitment Reform","1) improving the civil servant recruitment system to be merit-based, transparent, fair, efficient, and inclusive;",""],[1,"12","1","Public Administration Performance Incentive System","3) establishing and implementing a performance- based incentive system within the public administration that is coherent, equitable, efficient, and sustainable.",""],[1,"33","2","Merit-Based Civil Servant Recruitment System","the government has implemented a new civil servant recruitment system based on meritocracy, transparency, fairness, inclusivity, and efficiency.",""],[1,"33","2","Civil Service Institutional Capacity and Performance Improvement","It has also improved institutional capacity and performance to enhance work quality, professional ethics, and effectiveness, and has introduced a new incentive system to support performance with consistency, equity, and sustainability.",""],[1,"33","2","Civil Service Incentive System","has introduced a new incentive system to support performance with consistency, equity, and sustainability.",""],[1,"53","9","Incentive System for Qualified Officials","Continue to strengthen and expand the implementation of the incentive system for qualified officials to strengthen public administration capacity and job performance and increase productivity and efficiency in public service delivery,",""],[1,"56","5","Leadership Capacity Development Framework and Training Programme","Strengthening leadership capacity by way of formulating and implementing frameworks for leadership capacity development; training programs on leadership; assessing and recognizing role-model leadership; and building leadership networks in the public administration.",""],[1,"56","6","Civil Service Management and Administration Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening civil service management system and administration capacity by improving the legal and regulatory frameworks related to civil services; implementing frameworks to enhance work productivity; enhancing performance-based management; and promoting competition and innovation.",""],[1,"57","3","Civil Service Role Rationalization and Public Administration Capacity Strengthening","Conduct role rationalization, strengthen civil service management systems, and enhance public administration management capacity by clearly defining roles and responsibilities, define levels of authority and appropriate delegation of power, and ensure accountability within leadership frameworks",""],[1,"57","8","Human Resource Management Strengthening for Public Service Institutions","Strengthen human resource management in compliance with specific legal frameworks governing civil servants, national police officers, and prison officials, as well as with civil service management reform program",""],[1,"59","2","Merit-Based Human Resource Management and Capacity Building System","Strengthening human resource development and management systems that are based on meritocracy in terms of recruitments, appointments, promotions, and proper incentives, as well as development of a comprehensive capacity building system.",""],[1,"59","3","Public Sector Pay and Incentive System Reform","Developing public sector pay and incentive system in a more effective and comprehensive manner, based on meritocracy aiming at enhancing work productivity, performance, and living standards of the civil servants, in consistent with the economic growth and affordability of the national budget.",""],[1,"59","10","Public Service Management and Human Capital Development","Strengthen the management system, human resource development, and human capital, encompassing both hard and soft skills in the public service sector, to achieve high competency and professional ethics, thereby enhancing productivity and work efficiency",""],[1,"59","11","Remuneration and Incentive System Reform","Develop a more effective and comprehensive remuneration and incentive systems",""],[1,"59","13","Public Administration Capacity and Incentive System Reform","Develop the capacity of public officials and enhance performance, while establishing an incentive system that promotes consistent, equitable, effective, and sustainable outcomes in public administration at both national and sub-national levels, particularly in the education and health sectors",""],[1,"59","14","Human Resource Capacity Partnership Expansion","Strengthen and expand partnerships within the framework of enhancing human resource capacity, engaging national ministries-institutions, sub-national administrations, national and international academic institutions, and relevant development partners","national ministries-institutions"],[1,"59","15","Merit-Based Public Recruitment Reform","Improve the recruitment system for the public officials based on meritocracy, while reviewing and analyzing the functions and organizational structures ministries-institutions",""],[1,"60","1","Public Official Deployment Mechanism","Develop and implement deployment mechanism for public officials, in addition to utilizing existing human resources within ministries-institutions, and sub-national administrations",""],[1,"60","4","Inter-Institutional and Development Partner Cooperation Mechanism","Promote cooperation and strengthen partnerships with ministries-institutions, sub-national administrations, national and international academic institutions, and relevant development partners",""],[1,"60","5","Human Resource Management Strengthening for Civil Service and National Police","Strengthen human resource management in accordance with the Law on the Common Statute of Civil Servants of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Royal Decree on the Specific Statute of the Cambodian National Police Framework.",""]],"96":[[1,"13","1","Civil Service Management Information Systems","Management in the civil service sector has been gradually improved through the continuous issuance of relevant legal documents and the development of new information technology systems for comprehensive civil servant management.","Ministry of Civil Service"],[1,"57","4","Public Administration Reform Action Plans","Prepare action plans for the implementation of key measures in public administration reform and the use of information technology in public administration",""],[1,"58","10","Internal Audit and Digital Transformation Units in Sub-national Administrations","Establish and implement internal audit units and digital transformation units within sub- national administrations",""],[1,"59","7","Public Administration Database Modernization and Information Sharing","Further promoting database modernization and usage, as well as information sharing and exchanges in public administration.",""],[1,"60","8","Digital Personnel Management and Training System for Sub-national Administrations","Establish and implement a digital technology-based system for managing and training personnel in sub-national administrations",""]],"97":[[1,"12","2","Public Sector Integrity and Anti-Corruption Enforcement","It is committed to eliminating corruption through strengthening education, prevention, and the application of anti-corruption laws by consistently building and submitting cases to the courts, and by requiring civil servants to declare their assets and debts.",""],[1,"12","2","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Implementation","This includes implementing duties in line with the National Strategic Plan on Anti-Money Laundering and Combating the Financing of Terrorism and the action plan set by the Asia/Pacific Group on Money Laundering (APG), which resulted in Cambodia's removal from the grey list.",""],[1,"12","3","Strengthened Inspection, Legal Education, and Capacity-Building Programme","the government has continuously strengthened inspections in all sectors, monitored the implementation of laws, legal instruments, and government directives, and addressed complaints.",""],[1,"57","11","Internal Audit, Inspection, and Complaint Resolution Strengthening","Strengthening the implementation of functions of internal audit, inspection, and complaint resolution within the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Interior to ensure accuracy, transparency, and effectiveness through 1) Development and implementation of internal audit plans based on actual needs, and enhancement of internal audit quality across relevant units with the Ministry's jurisdiction, including recommendations and following- up on recommendations from the general department of internal audit 2) Strengthening technical cooperation on internal audit with the National Audit Authority, the General Department of Internal Audit of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and other relevant national and international institutions, and 3) Promoting integrity, inspection, and complaint resolution at both national and sub-national levels withing the Ministry's areas of responsibility.","Ministry of Interior | National Audit Authority | General Department of Internal Audit of the Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"60","14","Civil Service Code of Ethics and Professional Conduct","Developing and implementing a code of ethics and professional conduct in civil service and fostering compliance by public officers with the principles of functional incompatibility and conflict of interests.",""],[1,"60","15","Inspection and Audit Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening the effectiveness of inspection and audit mechanisms and creating rules of audit and inspection systems to ensure the harmonization of inspection and audit functions in public administration.",""],[1,"60","16","Public Service Management and Accountability Reform","Strengthening mechanisms for public service management and deliveries, merit-based incentives, and the adoption of strict legal measures for public conducts and responsibilities to promote trust and to increase effectiveness in public service deliveries.",""],[1,"61","1","Anti-Corruption Education and Enforcement Strengthening","Further strengthening and expanding anti-corruption education and corruption prevention efforts, as well as strengthening stringent enforcement of laws to combat corruption.",""],[1,"61","2","Anti-Corruption Coordination and Focal Person Mechanism","Enhancing cooperation between Anti-Corruption Unit and public institutions, especially through a focal person mechanism, both in the provisions of anti-corruption education and in the prevention of corruption, in order to put in place the monitoring, evaluation, implementation of strategic plans, and plans for promoting integrity in public institutions.",""],[1,"61","5","Public Sector Code of Ethics and Conduct","Develop and implement a professional code of ethics and code of conduct within the public sector, while strengthening management mechanisms and enhancing the effectiveness of public service delivery",""],[1,"61","6","Public Integrity and Conflict-of-Interest Enforcement Measures","Promote and institutionalize integrity, reinforce strict adherence to the principles of functional neutrality and conflict of interest in the performance of public officials' duties, and take stringent legal measures in executing roles and responsibilities to enhance public trust and efficiency in service delivery",""],[1,"61","9","Civil Service Inspection Strengthening","Strengthen civil service inspection functions, including monitoring, evaluation, and effective resolution of challenges to enhance overall efficiency.",""],[1,"61","11","Cross-Sector Public Administration Inspection Programme","Conduct inspections across all sectors within ministries-institutions, public units, public enterprises, national public administrative institutions, and sub-national administrations to strengthen governance and enhance integrity in public administration",""],[1,"61","13","Complaint and Grievance Resolution Mechanisms","Strengthen mechanisms for examining and resolving complaints and grievances from legal entities, natural persons, and all stakeholders, as well as online complaint reception mechanisms, within the jurisdiction of the Royal Government, grounded in a win-win strategy aimed at preserving a harmonious social environment.",""],[1,"61","13","Public Forum and Legal Awareness Outreach","Enhance public forum mechanisms, educational programs, and the dissemination of laws and related normative legal documents to citizens",""],[1,"61","14","Inspection Sector Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","Develop normative legal documents in the inspection sector, including the draft Law on Inspection, the draft law on complaints and denunciations, the draft National Inspection Policy, the draft Sub-Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the Ministry of Inspection, the draft Inspection Operating Standards, the draft Guidelines for Conducting Investigations and Resolving Complaints, the draft Code of Ethics for Inspection Officials, the draft Code of Ethics for Officials Receiving and Resolving Complaints, and several other normative legal documents.",""],[1,"62","1","Citizen Complaint Resolution and Information Provision Mechanisms","Ministry of Interior shall focus on implementing priority actions related to strengthening and improvement mechanisms and procedures for receiving and resolving complaints, as well as providing information to citizens.","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"62","2","Anti-Corruption Priority Actions Implementation","Anti-Corruption Unit shall continue to implement the following priority actions:",""],[1,"62","3","Anti-Corruption Capacity Building for Focal Groups and Offices","Enhance the knowledge and capacity of focal groups and anti-corruption offices in the capital and provinces regarding education, prevention, and suppression of corruption",""],[1,"62","4","Clean Action Plan Review and Development for Public Institutions","Review and evaluate the implementation of clean action plan, and develop clean action plan for the public institutions (or the anti-corruption action plan focal groups, public institutions, and anti-corruption offices in the capital and provinces)",""],[1,"62","5","Anti-Corruption and Anti-Money Laundering Policy Implementation","Continue implementing the United Nations Convention against Corruption Implementation Review Mechanism in Cambodia and continue implementation of anti-money laundering and countering the financing of terrorism policies.",""]],"98":[[1,"19","4","National Strategic Plan for HIV/AIDS Response","Cambodia is implementing its fifth National Strategic Plan for a comprehensive and multi-sectoral response to HIV/AIDS.",""],[1,"80","11","National Multisectoral HIV and AIDS Response Strengthening","National AIDS Authority shall prioritize actions to strengthen the national, multisectoral response to HIV and AIDS, in order to implement the national policy to end AIDS and program sustainability 2023-2028",""],[1,"81","1","Three Ones Coordination and Monitoring Framework","national and subnational levels adhere to the Three Ones principle: one national strategy, one coordinating mechanism, and one monitoring and evaluation system.",""]],"99":[[1,"24","3","Postal Sector Regulatory and Digital Service Modernization","In the postal sector, Cambodia has prepared the Postal Sector Development Policy 2022- 2030 and a new draft law on postal services.",""],[1,"24","3","Online License and Permit Application System","It also launched an online system for license and permit applications and promoted postal diplomacy.",""],[1,"24","3","Digital Government and Telecommunications Modernization","To drive a successful digital transformation and promote a digital government, economy, and society, the government continues to modernize mobile and internet services.",""],[1,"24","3","Digital Public Service Platforms","It has also developed and launched key digital systems to meet Cambodia's specific needs, such as the QR Code system and the StopCovid QR Vaccine digital vaccination card system to combat COVID-19.",""],[1,"24","3","Document Verification Platform","The verify.gov.kh document verification platform was released to eliminate fraud, enhance convenience and trust, and improve the efficiency of public services.",""],[1,"24","3","Scholarship Support for Postal and ICT Capacity Building","Additionally, the government is promoting human resource development in this sector by offering numerous scholarships to build capacity in the postal, telecommunications, and information and communication technology fields.",""],[1,"52","6","Digital Government and Digital Society Development","Development of Digital Economy and Society by focusing on building digital government and digital citizens, development of digital economy, digital business, e-commerce, and digital innovation system, building and development of digital infrastructures, trustworthiness building in digital system, and development of financial technology.",""],[1,"52","6","Digital Infrastructure Development","building and development of digital infrastructures",""],[1,"52","6","Digital Trust and Financial Technology Development","trustworthiness building in digital system, and development of financial technology.",""],[1,"124","9","Digitalization of Public Administration and Services","the RGC is a role model and steers the adoption of digital technologies through digitalization of public administration and services to strengthen the effectiveness and efficiency in the deliveries of services to the people and private sector, and in strengthening data-driven governance.",""],[1,"124","10","Digital Government Infrastructure Optimization and Expansion","Strengthening the utilization of existing digital government infrastructures to their maximum capacity; and expanding the necessary and prioritized digital government infrastructures.",""],[1,"124","11","Public Administration Base Registry Development","Continuing to develop base registries in public administration with high quality and standards.",""],[1,"124","12","Expansion of Digital Public Services","Continuing to expand the digitalization of public services at national and sub-national levels.",""],[1,"125","1","Common Technical Standards for Digital Public Services","Developing common technical standards for the provision of digital public services, interoperability frameworks, security standards and related common technical standards for ministries-institutions.",""],[1,"125","2","Common Digital Enabling Platforms Development","Continuing to develop common digital enabling platforms that act as enablers for building a unified digital government system.",""],[1,"125","10","Government Digital Equipment and Workflow Systems Deployment","Procure and deploy computers and digital devices as required, use properly licensed software, and provide email, document and workflow management systems, and other platforms, with priority on security systems",""],[1,"125","11","National Data Center Establishment","Establish a National Data Center managed by the Ministry of Post and Telecommunications, enabling each ministry and institution to manage its own data directly","Ministry of Post and Telecommunications"],[1,"125","12","Ministerial Digital Platforms and Software Applications Development","Develop ministerial digital platforms and software applications through government-to- government, government-to-business, and government-to-citizen mechanisms",""],[1,"126","7","Digital Public Administration and One-Stop Service Portal Development","Formulate and promote the development of digital public administration governance and civil service information management systems through digital technologies, and accelerate the digital transformation of public administration and public services, including establishing one-stop service portals",""],[1,"126","10","Commerce Sector Digital Government and Automation Programme","Ministry of Commerce shall advance digital government, digital citizenship, and digital business in the commerce sector by developing digital infrastructure, deploying effective automation for public service delivery, commercial administration, and trade data management, enabling trade information sharing via electronic platforms, integrating service systems with the Government's automation platforms, and building officials' capacities in digitalization to create an enabling business environment and facilitate trade.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"126","12","Cambodia Data Exchange Platform Expansion","Continue promoting use of the Cambodia data exchange platform (CamDX) for system- to-system data exchange across ministries and institutions",""],[1,"126","13","Promotion of the Cambodia Digital Identity Platform","Continue promoting use of the Cambodia digital identity platform (CamDigiKey) as the digital identity for users within ministries-institutions' information systems",""],[1,"126","14","Maintenance and Development of Foundational Data Systems","Continue investing in the maintenance and development of foundational data systems of relevant ministries and institutions.",""],[1,"126","16","Digital Government Policy Priority Plan Implementation Coordination","Digital Government Committee shall coordinate with ministries-institutions to implement the priority plan of the Cambodia Digital Government Policy 2022-2035.",""],[1,"127","2","Base Registry Development and Public Service Digitalization","Continuing to develop high quality, high standard, and prioritized base registries for economic and business sectors; and expanding the digitalization of public services to support the economic and business sectors.",""],[1,"127","13","Digital Identity and Digital Signature Adoption","Promote the adoption of digital identity and digital signatures to broadly establish and verify digital identities for citizens, the private sector, and public institutions",""],[1,"128","4","Government-to-Private Sector Data Sharing Initiative","Promote government-to-private sector data sharing to foster new creation and innovation",""],[1,"148","4","Civil Servant Information Management System Strengthening","Strengthening and enhancement of civil servant information management system",""]],"100":[[1,"26","2","Labor Market Development and Employment Services Expansion","The labor market has been continuously developed and improved to provide better employment opportunities, especially for young people entering the workforce.",""],[1,"26","2","Minimum Wage Increases for Garment and Related Sectors","Along with a high employment rate, the minimum wage for the garment, textile, footwear, and travel goods and bag sectors has continuously increased in a harmonious manner, from $170 per month in 2018 to $200 per month in 2023.",""],[1,"26","2","Overseas Employment Opportunities Expansion","Opportunities for overseas employment with good working conditions and high incomes have also been expanded.",""],[1,"26","2","Employment Services and Labor Market Information Strengthening","The effectiveness of employment services and market information has been strengthened and given high priority.",""],[1,"26","2","Labor Center Expansion and Mobile Labor Centers","This has been achieved by increasing the number of labor centers to 14 and establishing numerous mobile labor centers, implementing a digital platform for employment services to help people find jobs and provide career counseling, and organizing job forums that have served a total of 900 000 people.",""],[1,"51","9","Improvement of Employee Working Conditions","as well as improving the working environment for employees",""],[1,"52","4","Labor Market Development and Private Sector Promotion","Development of Private Sector and Employment by focusing on development of labor market; promotion of micro, small, and medium enterprises, startups, entrepreneurship, and development of informal economy; strengthening of public-private partnerships; promotion of competition; and strengthening of banking system and non-banking financial sector.",""],[1,"99","11","Investment Planning and M&E Mechanisms for Training Institutions","Developing additional investment planning, monitoring and evaluation mechanisms for training institutions and modernizing supportive infrastructures for trainings on applied sciences and technologies.",""],[1,"99","12","Employment Services and Career Guidance Programme","Continuing to create job opportunities, expanding employment-seeking services, and career counselling and guidance; continuing to organize job fairs and assigning lead trainers and career focal persons to help with job-seeking at educational institutions.",""],[1,"99","14","Apprenticeship, Internship, Upskilling and Reskilling Strengthening Programme","Continuing to strengthen the implementation of apprenticeship obligations including apprenticeship programs, internships, upskilling and reskilling, to enhance work productivity.",""],[1,"100","8","Active Labor Market Policy Strengthening","Formulate and implement an active labor market policy through strengthening the implementation of labor sector-related policies and programs, and enhancing mechanisms for monitoring, inspection, and evaluation of such policies and programs.",""],[1,"100","8","Employment Services and Job Platform Improvement","This includes improving the effectiveness of employment services and job platforms, expanding and strengthening career counseling and vocational guidance services, enhancing labor force utilization management, and advancing the implementation of the national policy on occupation and employment, as well as programs that promote labor productivity",""],[1,"101","3","Human Resource and Skills Training Programs","Participate in implementing human resource and skills training programs to enhance regional mobility, while strengthening and expanding the scope of the national employment agency.",""],[1,"109","6","Labor Diversification and Youth Employment Support","Continuing to promote labor diversification to absorb youth's labor force through the development of technical skills, increasing investment, and the development of micro, small, and medium enterprises, taking into consideration the development of young entrepreneurs, gender equality and self-employment.",""]],"101":[[1,"26","3","Labor Law Enforcement and Inspection Strengthening","This includes reinforcing the implementation of national and international labor laws and legal instruments and strengthening the labor inspection system in enterprises and institutions, both in-person and through an automated system.",""],[1,"26","3","Child Labor Prevention and Eradication Awareness Campaign","The government has also raised awareness about preventing and eradicating child labor, promoted the rights and freedom of professional organizations, and strengthened mechanisms for out-of-court labor dispute resolution.",""],[1,"26","3","Out-of-Court Labor Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","The government has also raised awareness about preventing and eradicating child labor, promoted the rights and freedom of professional organizations, and strengthened mechanisms for out-of-court labor dispute resolution.",""],[1,"26","3","Tripartite Social Dialogue Partnership","Furthermore, it has fostered a tripartite social dialogue partnership and supported the sustainability of the Arbitration Council.",""],[1,"26","3","Arbitration Council Sustainability Support","Furthermore, it has fostered a tripartite social dialogue partnership and supported the sustainability of the Arbitration Council.",""],[1,"99","13","Foreign Labor Management Compliance and Efficiency Reform","Strengthening the compliance and efficiency of the management of foreign labor in accordance with international standards, establishing mechanisms for skills transfers to Cambodian youth, and preventing illegal cross-border labor trafficking.",""],[1,"100","1","Labor Inspection Strengthening and Professionalization","Continuing to strengthen quality and efficiency of labor inspection, professionalizing labor inspectors, and providing a boost for and strengthening inter-institutional inspection mechanisms.",""],[1,"100","2","Minimum Wage and Worker Benefits Enhancement","continuing to raise the minimum wage and other benefits",""],[1,"100","2","Expansion of Minimum Wage Coverage Feasibility Review","examining the feasibility of expanding the scope of the minimum wage to other sectors",""],[1,"100","2","Special Lease Law Enforcement","promoting law enforcement on special lease",""],[1,"100","3","Occupational Safety and Health Reform and Workplace Support Facilities","Continuing to improve occupational safety and health, introducing occupational safety and health laws, improving the quality of transport, and promoting affordable nurseries, accommodation and canteens in the clusters of factories and SEZs.",""],[1,"100","4","Industrial Relations Harmonization and Labor Dispute Resolution Reform","Continuing to strengthen the harmonization of industrial relations; strengthening capacity and professionalizing mediation officers of labor disputes and personnel officers; strengthening labor dispute resolution mechanisms; ensuring the sustainability of Arbitration Council; introducing a labor court; establishing industrial relations development fund; and launching national campaigns on \"An Enterprise, A Community of Peace.\"",""],[1,"100","9","Labor Inspection and Occupational Safety and Health Strengthening","Improve working conditions, occupational safety and health, and the harmonization of industrial relations in line with labor market developments through strengthening the capacity of labor inspection officials and inspection mechanisms, advancing the implementation of national policies, laws, and normative legal documents related to occupational safety and health, eliminating child labor and its worst forms, enhancing the capacity of institutions and relevant stakeholders in determining minimum wages and worker benefits, and promoting the harmonization of industrial relations to transform enterprises into peaceful communities",""]],"102":[[1,"27","2","Competition Policy and Consumer Protection Framework","Competition has been strengthened to promote a level playing field and achieve economic efficiency.",""],[1,"104","4","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"104","5","Competition and Consumer Protection Law Enforcement","Continuing to enhance the effectiveness of the implementation of the Law on Competition, the Law on Consumer Protection and relevant legal instruments in force, the protection of legal private properties, and the prevention of all business transactions and activities that hinder, restrict, or adversely impact upon the fair and just competition.",""],[1,"104","6","Market Competition Policy and Regulatory Enforcement Mechanism","Continuing to strengthen the institutional capacity, formulate and implement market policies and regulations, and set up mechanisms to monitor and evaluate the nature of businesses, and the mergers of businesses of enterprises that have or may have the objective or power to hinder, restrict, or adversely impact upon the fair and just competition or increase monopoly power in the market.",""],[1,"104","7","Competition Law and Anti-Collusion Enforcement Mechanism","Formulating and launching mechanisms and legal instruments necessary for the effective and efficient management and settlements of issues related to the establishments, agreements or acts of collusion by enterprises in determining geographical areas for sales of goods or services and maintaining or setting prices higher than competitive market prices",""],[1,"104","8","Intellectual and Private Property Protection Strengthening","Further strengthening the protection of legal intellectual properties and private properties to promote the inventions of new products and services, creativity, and innovation in order to ensure competitive market.",""],[1,"104","9","Competition Policy and Regulatory Reform","Continuing to accelerate the preparation, development, amendments and implementation of policies, laws and regulations related to competition;",""],[1,"104","9","Cambodian Competition Commission Capacity Strengthening","continuing to strengthen the capacity of the Cambodian Competition Commission, business dispute settlement mechanisms, and consumer protection mechanisms, in line with the quality, safety and health standards.",""],[1,"104","10","Consumer Protection Mechanisms","Designing and implementing the consumer protection mechanisms that can play a major role in resolving issues on behalf of consumers in the event of disputes related to the purchases and sales of goods and services of all kinds.",""],[1,"105","2","Competition Law Enforcement and Fair Market Regulation","It will prevent business practices that restrict, constrain, or undermine fair and proper competition by strengthening the effectiveness of enforcing the Law on Competition, the Law on Consumer Protection, the Law on Food Safety, intellectual property laws, the Law on the Quality and Safety of Products and Services, the Law on Commercial Rules and Business Registration, the Law on Commercial Advertising, and other related normative legal documents.","Ministry of Commerce | Cambodia Competition Committee | Consumer Protection Committee"],[1,"105","2","Business Dispute Resolution and Consumer Protection Mechanism","The Ministry will establish mechanisms for business dispute resolution and protection of the rights of business operators and consumers, strengthen the capacities of the Cambodia Competition Committee and the Consumer Protection Committee, and promote diversification of new products and services, creativity, and innovation to ensure market competitiveness.","Ministry of Commerce | Cambodia Competition Committee | Consumer Protection Committee"],[1,"105","2","Cambodian Brand and Geographical Indication Promotion Mechanism","It will also develop mechanisms to elevate Cambodian brands, particularly geographical indications and collective marks, to drive export growth.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"105","3","One Village One Product Policy Implementation","National Committee to Promote One Village One Product Movement shall continue to implement the national policy on promoting the One Village One Product (OVOP) 2016-2026, with a focus on five priority strategies",""]],"103":[[1,"41","1","Revenue Mobilization Strategy Implementation","the continued implementation of the 2019-2023 revenue mobilization strategy",""],[1,"41","6","Resource Mobilization and Expenditure Efficiency Strengthening","the Royal Government's tenaciously efforts to mobilize resources to their full potential, both fiscal and non-fiscal, and to strengthen expenditure efficiency",""],[1,"51","8","Macroeconomic Stability and Public Financial Management Strengthening","maintaining macroeconomic stability by keeping inflation rate low, ensuring exchange rate stability, striving to steadily increase reserves, and strengthening PFM, and the efficiency of state assets management and sustainable public debt management.",""],[1,"52","7","Gradual Fiscal Consolidation Policy Framework","over the medium term, the Royal Government will adhere to a Gradual Fiscal Consolidation Stance, a public financial policy that aims to gradually strengthen fiscal efficiency.",""],[1,"52","8","Budget Allocation Rationalization and Value-for-Money Spending","Continue to value the improvement of the efficiency of budget allocation and the effectiveness of national budget spending by prioritizing the rationalization of expenditure items, that is, to properly and purposefully allocate budgets in line with the policy priorities of the Royal Government, and to be smart in spending by focusing on value for money, as well as considering additional financing mechanisms to meet all spending priorities, such as key reforms of the Royal Government, continuing to support the social protection system, increasing productivity, competitiveness promotion, and investment",""],[1,"53","2","Budget Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","Strengthen the monitoring and evaluation of budget implementation more thoroughly on the appropriateness of cost, quantity, and quality, with the aim of further improving the efficiency of budget allocation and improving the quality of setting key indicators appropriately within the framework of implementing the budget information system",""],[1,"53","4","National Budget Management Efficiency Reform","Systematically strengthen the efficiency of national budget management through the implementation of the Budget Reform Strategy 2018-2025 and the 2025-2028 Update, the Sub-National Budget Reform Strategy 2019-2025, and the Public Procurement System Reform Strategy",""],[1,"53","5","Revenue Mobilization Strategy Implementation","Continue to implement the Royal Government's revenue mobilization strategy of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly by strengthening revenue collection to be more effective and efficient, while ensuring fiscal stability and economic resilience by avoiding excessive economic volatility",""],[1,"53","7","Tax Incentive Review and Tax Burden Avoidance Policy","Continue to assess the feasibility of maintaining tax incentives and pursue policies without imposing new tax burdens on citizens and private sectors",""],[1,"53","8","Fiscal Strategy for Government Savings","Prepare fiscal strategies that focus on enhancing government savings to prepare for future crises",""],[1,"53","10","Public Financial Reform Program","Continue implementing reforms within the framework of the public financial reform program as a core part of public financial policy to enhance efficiency and effectiveness, especially in increasing spending efficiency, revenue collection & administration reforms, and IT system structuring, focusing on maintaining and ensuring financial sustainability.",""],[1,"59","5","Public Finance Management Reform","Further reforming the management of public finance by enhancing the budget credibility, financial accountability, linking budget to policies, and performance accountability, in order to build a public finance system in accordance with the international standards and best practices.",""],[1,"71","1","Macroeconomic Stability Maintenance","Continuing to maintain macroeconomic stability to ensure the sustained inclusive growth through managing the inflation rate at an appropriate level, stabilizing the exchange rate, increasing national reserves, and maintaining the stability of people's livelihoods.",""],[1,"71","2","Deep Structural and Inter-Institutional Reform Agenda","Undertaking deeper and sharper reforms, especially to address structural and inter- institutional challenges, aimed at promoting economic diversification and increasing productivity and competitiveness of Cambodia.",""],[1,"71","3","Public Financial Management Reform Programme","Maintaining the sustainability of public finance by continuing to promote the implementation of public financial management reforms, focusing on the strengthening of revenue collections, and enhancing effectiveness of expenditure, strengthening state assets management, sustainably managing public debts, promoting the development of mechanisms to mobilize financing from domestic sources, and gradually expanding national budget space.",""],[1,"71","4","Financial Safety Net Development and Financial Deepening","Strengthening financial stability and resilience, both in the banking and non-banking sectors, especially through the development of the financial safety net and the promotion of financial deepening.",""],[1,"71","5","Promotion of Financial Cooperation","Promoting financial cooperation, both regional and global, to contribute to the strengthening of the stability of financial system, resource mobilization, and development of new financial markets and financial technologies.",""],[1,"71","9","Medium-Term Fiscal Framework Preparation","Continue preparing the Medium-Term Fiscal Framework, in particular setting prudent fiscal policy stances that safeguard macroeconomic stability and fiscal sustainability",""],[1,"71","10","Revenue Mobilization Strategy Implementation","Accelerate implementation of the Royal Government's Revenue Mobilization Strategy for the 7th Legislature to strengthen domestic revenue collection, while safeguarding economic momentum and dynamism, ensuring accuracy, transparency, and fairness in tax assessment for taxpayers, and focusing on high-potential revenue sources that minimize adverse impacts on the economy",""],[1,"71","11","Prudent and Proactive Budget Execution","Maintain high prudence and proactivity in budget execution, grounded in fiscal discipline and spending efficiency at both programmatic and operational levels, targeting expenditures and prioritizing value for money",""],[1,"71","12","Fiscal Reserve Fund Establishment and Operationalization","Formulate measures to rebuild the Government's savings to prepare for future shocks, through establishing and operationalizing a Fiscal Reserve Fund, the state's savings fund",""],[1,"71","13","Public Debt Management Strategy Implementation","Continue managing public debt with strict discipline and high efficiency by rigorously applying the key fiscal rules set out in the Public Debt Management Strategy 2024-2028",""],[1,"71","14","Public Investment Management Reform Strategy Implementation","Continue strengthening the effectiveness of public investment management by implementing the measures and action plans set out in the Public Investment Management Reform Strategy 2019-2025",""],[1,"71","15","Public Financial Management Reform Program Stage 4","Continue implementing the Public Financial Management Reform Program-Stage 4, with a focus on performance accountability to enhance efficiency, quality, and results-based accountability across public institutions",""],[1,"72","2","Financial Sector Development Strategy Implementation","Promote implementation of the Financial Sector Development Strategy 2025-2030.",""],[1,"72","7","Non-Bank Financial Services Development and Strengthening","Non-Bank Financial Services Authority continues to develop and strengthen non-bank financial services, and will regularly conduct research and prepare periodic reports on the state of the non-bank financial sector.",""]],"104":[[1,"66","2","Integrated One-Stop Business Registration System","Establish an integrated information technology system, connected to the CamDX platform, for business start-up applications at the subnational level, tax registration, and registration with the Departments of Labour and Vocational Training, including the National Social Security Fund (NSSF), together with standardized forms and technical procedures for bundled one-stop services, with simplified procedures and reduced time and financial costs",""],[1,"66","6","Permit and License Consolidation through CamDX","Digital Economy and Business Committee shall coordinate and review the feasibility of consolidating permits, licenses, and certificates that have similar value or low additional value, and incorporate these services into business registration mechanisms through the CamDX platform, to build a digital business ecosystem for enterprises and to help improve the domestic business environment.","Digital Economy and Business Committee"]],"105":[[1,"66","11","Crime Prevention and Enforcement Against Organized Crime","Preventing and cracking down of all types of criminal offenses, including the fight against terrorism, transnational crimes, human trafficking, labor trafficking, sex trafficking, money laundering and terrorism financing, financing of weapons of mass destruction, combatting illegal activities related to illicit drug trafficking and use, illegal gambling, as well as continued strengthening of the implementation of 'Safe Village/Commune' Policy.",""],[1,"67","1","Urban Traffic Safety and Order Improvement","Continuing to strengthen traffic safety and order on the streets in cities and towns to solve traffic congestions and reduce road accidents, aimed at reducing related costs and increasing economic optimization.",""],[1,"67","3","Fire Prevention and Social Hazard Safety Measures","Preventing and addressing fires issues and social hazards to ensure safety for people at the time of expansion in urbanization, large congregation of people in towns, and number of high-rise buildings.",""],[1,"67","5","Cybercrime Prevention and Law Enforcement Capacity Building","Strengthening law enforcement and capacity building to effectively prevent cybercrimes.",""],[1,"68","1","Safe Village-Commune-Sangkat Policy Implementation Strengthening","especially by strengthening the implementation of the Safe Village-Commune-Sangkat Policy",""],[1,"68","2","Police Capacity and Management Strengthening","Strengthen and develop the police by reinforcing roles and duties and enhancing officers' capacities, improving management, leadership, and inspection mechanisms for police work, conducting research, expanding auxiliary forces at the grassroots level, and promoting an E-Police system for receiving and providing information to improve interaction between police and the public",""],[1,"68","3","Public Security and Service Infrastructure Development","Develop infrastructure for police posts, border protection posts, police inspectorates, and the 16 May Hospital, to deliver public services to citizens",""],[1,"68","10","National Drug Control Strategy Implementation","The National Authority for Combating Drugs shall continue to implement six strategies, namely: 1) reduce drug demand, 2) reduce drug supply, 3) strengthen effective treatment, rehabilitation, and social reintegration, 4) enhance the effectiveness of law enforcement, 5) strengthen and expand international cooperation, and 6) reinforce coordination mechanisms at the national and subnational levels.","The National Authority for Combating Drugs"],[1,"68","11","National Counter-Terrorism Committee Secretariat Priority Actions","The Secretariat of the National Counter-Terrorism Committee shall focus on key priority actions, including counter-terrorism, anti-money laundering, combating the financing of terrorism and the proliferation of weapons of mass destruction, implementation of the National Counter-Terrorism Strategy, exercises and preparedness, intelligence collection both covert and open-source, strengthened domestic and international cooperation related to terrorism, and contributions to safeguarding national security and public safety.",""]],"106":[[1,"77","9","Study Clubs and Youth Councils Development Initiative","Promote the creation of study clubs, including digital technology clubs; strengthen youth councils; and build an ecosystem of science fairs, student showcases, competitions, and partnerships between secondary and higher education institutions and the private sector, to meet 21st-century needs and leverage technological progress",""],[1,"77","10","Youth Skills and Leadership Development Programme","Develop youth with both hard and soft skills, focusing on 21st-century competencies and leadership; provide opportunities to voice ideas, showcase talents, build positive peer relationships, and access internship pathways that build resilience, maturity, and rigorous critical thinking",""],[1,"77","11","Physical Education and Sports Reform and Active Living Promotion","Deepen reforms and elevate physical education and sports; cultivate a culture of active living to improve health, well-being, fitness, determination, perseverance, and creativity, thereby raising labor productivity and improving international sporting performance; continue the movement encouraging \"one youth plays at least one sport for life\"",""],[1,"85","7","Youth Development and Moral Education Program in Schools","Strengthen emphasis on soft skills development by mainstreaming youth development programs in schools to cultivate positive student habits, develop a moral education program focusing on respect for elders through the 'sampeah', appropriate dress, and good hygiene, and implement effective measures to promote awareness of Khmer culture and civility and to foster positive behavior among children and youth",""],[1,"85","8","Children's and Youth Councils Engagement in Community and School Initiatives","Promote the engagement of Children's Councils and Youth Councils in community and school initiatives, including peer-to-peer education, remedial tutoring, study clubs, community service, classroom and restroom cleaning, tree planting and school gardens, clean and green school environment campaigns, self-directed learning, health-promoting sports and physical activity, volunteerism, and drug-use prevention education.",""]],"107":[[1,"78","4","Khmer Language and Literature Conservation and Promotion Programme","Conserve, develop, and promote the sustainable use of the Khmer language and literature;",""],[1,"78","4","Natural and Cultural Resources Research and Conservation Initiative","research, conserve, and develop Cambodia's natural and cultural resources, including at the Techo Sen Russey Treb Park of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.",""],[1,"84","10","National Cultural Heritage Preservation and Promotion Programme","Promoting knowledge about national identity and ownership in the preservation and development of national culture, promoting the creation of new cultural products by maintaining the Khmer art styles, and, based on national identity, promoting the participation from senior art masters who are living human heritages and cultivating successors for those ancient forms of arts, and strengthening public participation in these endeavors.",""],[1,"85","1","Heritage Research, Compilation, and Dissemination Programme","Strengthening the effectiveness in research, compilation, and dissemination of historic values of heritage buildings, artifacts, ancient sites, sleuk rith manuscripts, ancient teachings, traditions, customs, Khmer virtuous attitude, and the sense of gratitude towards the nation.",""],[1,"85","10","National Arts and Culture Promotion Programme","Promote broad-based public participation, especially among youth, to elevate national arts and culture, strengthen national identity, prestige, Khmer values, dignity, and social ethics, by cultivating patriotism and cultural pride, encouraging consumption of domestic products, expanding international and social-media promotion of Khmer arts and culture, compiling and disseminating traditional customs and social practices, fostering creativity and the production of high-quality cultural works including for digital platforms, and enhancing compliance with laws, particularly on cultural heritage protection, copyright, and related rights",""],[1,"87","6","Tourism Sector Development and Diversification","Continuing to promote tourism sector, especially promoting cultural and natural tourism development in addition to green, clean, and smart tourism; making a push for the development of new types of tourism with high values added and business tourism through formulating and enhancing the implementation of policies and tourism sector development master plans.",""],[1,"87","7","Creative Industries Promotion Policies and Plans","Continuing to promote the development of entertainment service sector, literatures, arts, animation, films, and creative industries with high potentials, with relevant ministries- institutions formulating and implementing policies, strategies, and plans to promote these sectors.",""]],"108":[[1,"74","4","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""],[1,"76","6","Accelerated Implementation of the Cambodia Strategic Framework 2024-2030","Accelerate implementation of the Cambodia Strategic Framework 2024-2030 to operationalize the program of action of the International Conference on Population and Development (ICPD), reaffirming the Royal Government of Cambodia's strong commitment to contribute to global implementation of the Nairobi ICPD program of action and relevant United Nations conventions",""],[1,"76","7","Strengthening the National Statistical System for CSDG Monitoring","Continue engaging with the United Nations system to advance Cambodia's Sustainable Development Goals (CSDGs) by further strengthening the national statistical system to produce data for monitoring and evaluation of CSDG implementation",""],[1,"87","1","Sector-Specific Strategic Plan Preparation","institutions are required to prepare sector-specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature",""]],"109":[[1,"97","14","Financing Framework and Market Liquidity Mechanism","The strategic objectives are to design and improve financing frameworks and mechanisms, and product diversification and financial services that guarantee market liquidity and financing options for investments, aimed at contributing to promoting investment and economic diversification.",""],[1,"98","2","Securities Market Product Diversification and Green Finance Instruments","Continuing to promote product diversification in the securities sector through issuing green bonds, social bonds, sustainability bonds, and bonds linking to sustainability for private sector, launching of digital assets, futures bonds, SWAP Securities, and collective investment scheme; and promoting the development of trust mechanisms.",""],[1,"98","3","Legal Frameworks and Roadmaps for Public Financial Products","Establishing legal frameworks and/or roadmaps for developing public financial products, such as state securities, state green securities, state climate securities, and state social securities, to promote public investment and prioritized sectors.",""],[1,"98","5","Enterprise Development Support Framework","Establishing strategic frameworks for supporting the development of micro, small, medium, and large enterprises through generating support for securities listing registration, establishing legal frameworks, and creating the environment conducive for the implementation of new financial mechanisms and instruments.",""],[1,"98","6","Development of New Financial Products for Agricultural Finance","Encouraging banking and financial institutions to develop new financial products in line with market demand, such as agricultural loans with payment options appropriate to seasonal incomes and so on, as well as encouraging the innovation of financing mechanisms linked to insurance products, especially in agricultural sector, to enhance the financing inclusiveness.",""],[1,"98","8","Diversification of Technology-Based Financial Services and Mechanisms","Promoting the diversification of technology-based financial services and mechanisms, with environment, society, and governance being taken into consideration.",""],[1,"98","9","Development of National Financing Strategies","Building policy frameworks, strategies, and roadmaps for the development of national financing strategies to mobilize financing and seek out sources of funding to support the implementation of policies, strategies, and agendas of the RGC.",""],[1,"98","10","Domestic Savings Mobilization Mechanism","Developing and activating mechanisms to encourage people and enterprises to increase domestic savings in the banking system to provide private sector with the possibility for mobilizing financing for additional investments.",""],[1,"98","12","Secured Transactions Finance Operationalization","Ministry of Commerce shall continue to operationalize secured-transactions finance and related financial products by administering and accepting notice filings for secured transactions, and by encouraging private-sector compliance with the Law on Secured Transactions, to expand access to finance for businesses and investment.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"99","6","National Financing Policy Framework","Develop a National Financing Policy Framework as a tri-sectoral framework to guide and mobilize finance and investment",""],[1,"99","7","Government Thematic Bonds Guidelines Development","Study and prepare guidelines for issuing government thematic bonds, covering the full cycle, including feasibility assessment, pre-issuance preparation, issuance, and post- issuance monitoring and reporting",""]],"110":[[1,"110","5","Women's Economic Empowerment Support and Inclusive Investment Initiative","Expand supportive and enabling environments, as well as inclusive investment, to promote women's economic empowerment",""],[1,"110","6","Women’s Entrepreneurship and Leadership Support Programme","Promote women's entrepreneurship and support women leaders and managers in micro, small, and medium enterprises, with a focus on innovation, creativity, and inclusivity",""],[1,"110","7","Women’s Skills and Occupations Support Programme","Foster enabling conditions for women through addressing gender gaps in skills and occupations and providing professional and vocational skills development in line with labor market needs and societal transformation",""],[1,"110","8","Women's Workplace Support and Work-Life Balance Programme","Promote consideration of women's well-being, work-life balance programs, and a friendly, supportive workplace environment for women in economic activities",""],[1,"110","9","Women's Household Economic Empowerment Initiative","Enhance women's household economies within communities through the use of digital technology, business development, and inclusive financial services.",""],[1,"110","12","Positive Parenting and Workplace Childcare Services","Promote family well-being through positive parenting programs and workplace childcare services across public and private institutions at national and subnational levels.",""],[1,"111","6","Girls' Leadership Promotion Programs and New Initiatives","Promote girls' leadership through the implementation of programs and new initiatives in educational institutions and communities.",""]],"111":[[1,"67","2","Mine Clearance and Unexploded Ordnance Reduction Programme","Continuing efforts to achieve the goal of a \"Mine-Free Cambodia by 2025\" and to reduce unexploded ordinances to a minimum.",""],[1,"68","13","National Mine-Clearance Planning and Mine-Free Village Mechanism","Prepare and implement national mine-clearance plans and the Mine-Free Village mechanism with efficiency and success, and prepare the request to extend the anti-personnel mine clearance deadline to the relevant committees under the Ottawa Convention",""],[1,"68","14","National Mine Action Policy and Strategy Development","Formulate national policies and strategies for managing explosive remnants of war, risk reduction, and post-threat contexts, and continue sharing experiences in the mine action sector",""],[1,"68","15","Mine Action and Clearance Resource Mobilization","Continue mobilizing financial resources from development partners, friendly countries, investors, and philanthropists, to support mine action and clearance",""],[1,"68","16","Anti-Personnel Mine Ban Convention Implementation","Continue implementing the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use, Stockpiling, Production and Transfer of Anti-Personnel Mines and on their Destruction, by participating in meetings and submitting regular reports to the Royal Government",""],[1,"69","1","Mine-Risk Education and Mine Clearance Cooperation","Continue cooperating with ministries, institutions, and all relevant partners to deliver mine-risk education, reduce dangers from mines and explosive remnants of war, and prepare normative legal documents and policies to promote the rights and livelihoods of persons with disabilities caused by mines.",""],[1,"69","1","Legal and Policy Support for Mine-Disabled Persons","Continue cooperating with ministries, institutions, and all relevant partners to deliver mine-risk education, reduce dangers from mines and explosive remnants of war, and prepare normative legal documents and policies to promote the rights and livelihoods of persons with disabilities caused by mines.",""]],"113":[[1,"3","3","Urgent Promulgation of the Law","This law shall be promulgated as a matter of urgency.",""],[1,"11","2","Institutional Reform and Capacity Building","The Royal Government, under the 6th legislature of the National Assembly, has placed a high priority on institutional reform and capacity building to create strong institutions and a solid foundation for socio-economic development.",""],[1,"11","2","Sectoral Policy Framework and Legal Instruments Development","This inter-institutional work has been implemented by all ministries and institutions through the development and application of sectoral policy frameworks, laws, legal instruments, and human resource development, in line with the core of the Rectangular Strategy - Phase IV.",""],[1,"57","5","Normative Legal Framework and Institutional Coordination Reform","Formulate and implement necessary normative legal documents to enhance the effectiveness of institutional mechanisms; establish standards for service delivery by ministries, national-level institutions, and subnational administrations; and strengthen institutional coordination mechanisms and public service integration",""],[1,"57","10","Ministry of Interior Legal Drafting and Regulatory Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the development of laws drafting and legal norms within the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Interior through 1) enhancing the capacity of legal advisory council and policy development units 2) providing strategic guidance for the drafting of laws and legal documents to ensure their alignment with prescribed format, procedures, and consistency, and 3) conducting legal research, developing appropriate legal frameworks to support the effective execution of the Ministry's roles and responsibilities, ensuring accountability, and monitoring and evaluating the effectiveness of legal and regulatory implementation","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"61","12","Cross-Government Legal Implementation Monitoring and Promotion","Monitor and promote the implementation of laws, normative legal documents, and other decisions issued by the Head of the Royal Government across ministries-institutions, public units, public enterprises, national public administrative institutions, and sub- national administrations to improve operational efficiency",""],[1,"62","8","Legal and Regulatory Effectiveness and Compliance Reform","Promoting effectiveness, consistency, and legal compliance in introducing laws and regulations aimed at achieving the national vision and at meeting societal needs.",""]],"114":[[1,"15","2","Safe Village, Commune, and Sangkat Policy Implementation","the Royal Government has promoted and strengthened the implementation of the \"Safe Village, Commune, and Sangkat\" policy.",""],[1,"15","2","Crime Suppression and Public Safety Enforcement","It has cracked down on drug offenses, combated human trafficking, sex trafficking, and gang activity, enforced traffic laws, and provided fire-fighting and rescue interventions to ensure the normalcy and well-being of citizens.",""],[1,"15","2","Civil Registration and Identification Services Expansion","Work on civil registration and identification has been strengthened through the creation of laws and legal instruments and the provision of registration and identification services to all citizens, ensuring everyone has a complete legal identity and access to necessary basic services in accordance with the law.",""],[1,"15","3","Immigration Control and Border Security Management","Immigration work has been strictly implemented, and measures have been taken to genuinely ensure national sovereignty, prevent the occurrence of terrorism on Cambodian soil, thwart the clandestine activities of various terrorist organizations, and control the illegal entry and stay of foreign immigrants.",""],[1,"15","3","Border Checkpoint Management Strengthening","Border checkpoint management has been strengthened, and drug offenses have been effectively suppressed in a timely manner.",""],[1,"15","3","Drug Prevention Education and Public Awareness Campaign","Moreover, work to prevent, educate, and raise awareness about the dangers of drugs has been conducted to educate and disseminate information to the public.",""],[1,"15","3","International Law Enforcement Cooperation on Drug Crime","At the same time, coordination and cooperation with international law enforcement agencies, especially with neighboring countries, have been strengthened to increase the effectiveness of law enforcement and lead to the destruction of drug-related criminal organizations.",""],[1,"15","3","Law Enforcement Capacity and Integrity Strengthening","Moreover, the capacity, will, virtue, honesty, and professionalism of law enforcement officials have been reinforced in line with the national slogan 'Three Don'ts, One Report'- (1) Don't get involved, (2) Don't intervene, (3) Don't make exceptions, and report all cases of drug offenses to the authorities - while a draft national policy on establishing drug- free villages, communes, and sangkat has also been prepared.",""],[1,"32","5","Drug Control and Security Enforcement Measures","In the security sector, the Royal Government issued a directive to combat drugs through testing over 100 000 civil servants and armed forces.",""],[1,"32","5","Traveler and Foreigner Management System Modernization","The government also modernized the Traveler Management System (TMS) and the Foreigner Management System (FMS), launched an online passport application process, and created a mobile team to provide passport services at home for the sick, elderly, and disabled.",""]],"115":[[1,"19","5","Food Security and Nutrition Strategy","The nutrition sector has been consistently strengthened and promoted through the strategy on food security and nutrition, and the transformation of the food system to move toward ending hunger.",""],[1,"19","5","Micronutrient Food Fortification Expansion","The expansion of micronutrient fortification to other appropriate foods is being pursued to ensure quality, safety, and sufficient quantity to meet demand.",""],[1,"19","5","Public Awareness Campaign on Fortified Foods","The importance of using fortified foods is also being increasingly publicized.",""],[1,"19","5","Clean Water Service Expansion","Furthermore, the government has expanded the provision of clean water services to promote public health and the well-being of citizens, in line with four key conditions: \"quality, safety, sustainability, and affordability.\"",""],[1,"19","5","Clean Water Subsidy Guidelines for Poor Families","It has also put into use guidelines on subsidizing the cost of clean water access for poor families and implemented measures to lower the cost of clean water for garment workers",""]],"116":[[1,"25","3","Digital Transformation in Education","In the education sector, the Royal Government has implemented reforms to align with the Cambodia Digital Economy and Society Policy Framework, respond to the Fourth Industrial Revolution, and promote digital transformation.",""],[1,"25","3","Digital Learning and Literacy Promotion","This is being done by using digital technology in education, encouraging the study of science and technology subjects in both general secondary and higher education, and promoting foreign language skills, 21st-century skills, and digital literacy.",""],[1,"25","3","Technical Education and Lifelong Learning Expansion","The government is also providing technical education in general and technical high schools and encouraging lifelong learning.",""],[1,"25","3","Scientific Research and Cyber University Network Participation","The government also promotes scientific research and participation in the cyber university network to strengthen the capacity of professors through both in-person and online learning.",""],[1,"60","2","Academic Programs and Research Promotion Initiative","Develop academic programs, promote research and documentation, by expanding the training courses, promoting study tour programs and other social activities.",""]],"117":[[1,"28","3","Transboundary Water and River Basin Cooperation under the Mekong River Commission","the Royal Government continues to collaborate to strengthen and promote regional cooperation and the effective implementation of river basin and sectoral plans under the Mekong River Commission mechanism",""],[1,"28","5","National Clean Water Service Delivery and Water Management Implementation","It also produces and provides clean water services nationwide by implementing various activities and the Law on Clean Water Management.",""],[1,"28","5","Climate-Resilient Rural Road Upgrading","The continuous improvement of rural roads with double bituminous surface treatment or concrete pavement has yielded good results, making them more resilient to climate change.",""]],"118":[[1,"34","2","Science, Technology, and Innovation Laboratory Institutional Reform","In the industry, science, technology, and innovation sector, the government has transformed the Science, Technology, and Innovation Laboratory into a public administrative institution, promoted the issuance of quality, safety, and hygiene certificates, encouraged the development of local standards for priority products, and adopted international or ASEAN standards as national standards to promote domestic products for export and ensure the safety of imported goods.",""],[1,"34","2","National Strategic Plan for Informal Economy Development","It also launched the National Strategic Plan for Informal Economy Development 2023-2028 to encourage people in the informal economy to join the formal economy and officially launched the \"Digital Platform for Informal Economy Registration\" to identify the types of occupations and jobs within this sector.",""]],"119":[[1,"35","3","Registration and Legal Compliance Strengthening for Entities","In information and public relations, the government has strengthened the registration and legal compliance of both local and foreign entities, and improved the quality of information by drafting laws and legal instruments and reducing and suppressing fake news, disinformation, and misinformation.",""],[1,"35","3","Legal and Regulatory Measures Against Fake News and Disinformation","In information and public relations, the government has strengthened the registration and legal compliance of both local and foreign entities, and improved the quality of information by drafting laws and legal instruments and reducing and suppressing fake news, disinformation, and misinformation.",""]],"120":[[1,"39","1","Strategic Framework and Program to Restore and Promote Cambodia's Economic Growth in Living with COVID-19 under the New Normal","the Royal Government introduced appropriate and timely policy measures, especially through the \"Strategic Framework and Program to Restore and Promote Cambodia's Economic Growth in Living with COVID-19 under the New Normal for 2021-2023.\"",""],[1,"40","11","Incentives and Support Measures for Key Sectors","include incentives and favorable intervention to ease the burden and stabilize economic activity in key sectors.",""],[1,"41","1","Livelihood Stabilization Measures for Workers and Vulnerable Families","continued measures to stabilize the livelihoods of people, especially workers and poor and vulnerable families",""]],"121":[[1,"41","8","Prudent Public Debt Management and Diversified Sovereign Financing","the continued and consistent implementation of five key principles in public debt management",""],[1,"53","3","Public Debt Management Strategy Implementation","Continue implementing the 2024-2028 Public Debt Management Strategy, focusing on financial stability by investing in priority sectors, especially those that enhance productivity and add value, promoting connectivity, strengthening competitiveness, and economic restructuring",""]],"122":[[1,"63","3","Justice Sector Legal Modernization Programme","Develop and modernize justice-sector legislation by continuing to draft essential laws for the sector; reviewing and updating laws and subordinate legislation; and preparing legal frameworks for various specialized courts to respond to the context of digitalization.",""],[1,"63","3","Treaty and Draft Law Review and Preparation","Continue to examine and draft selected treaties and international agreements in criminal and civil matters, as well as other necessary draft laws and regulatory instruments",""],[1,"63","4","Justice Sector Legal Modernization","Develop and modernize justice-sector legislation by continuing to draft essential laws for the sector; reviewing and updating laws and subordinate legislation; and preparing legal frameworks for various specialized courts to respond to the context of digitalization and industrialization.",""],[1,"63","4","Treaty and Draft Law Review and Preparation","Continue to examine and draft selected treaties and international agreements in criminal and civil matters, as well as other necessary draft laws and regulatory instruments",""],[1,"64","1","Legal Reform Program","Lead and implement the legal reform program to build robustness, clarity, and long-term public confidence, ensuring the strengthening of the rule of law and the effective, successful implementation of the Pentagonal Strategy-Phase 1",""],[1,"64","2","Legal Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Establish mechanisms to monitor and evaluate the implementation of laws and normative legal documents by ministries and institutions, to ensure high accountability and effectiveness",""],[1,"64","3","Digital Legal Review and Dissemination System","Create systems to review draft laws and other normative legal documents, including a modern, digital legal data repository and dissemination platform, to improve the efficiency of drafting and implementation, and to raise public awareness of laws and normative instruments",""],[1,"64","4","Regulatory Impact Assessment Strengthening Mechanism","Strengthen the regulatory impact assessment mechanism, with a focus on training and capacity building for ministry and institution RIA teams, and require that RIA reports accompany submissions of draft laws, normative regulations, policy or strategy frameworks, and related documents for review and feedback",""]],"123":[[1,"64","5","Pentagonal Strategy Implementation Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Develop a monitoring, inspection, and evaluation framework for implementing the Pentagonal Strategy-Phase 1, and carry out monitoring, inspection, and evaluation of ministries, institutions, committees, councils, and authorities responsible for implementation, with reports submitted to the Prime Minister",""],[1,"64","6","Evidence-Based Policy Research and Monitoring System","Regularly research, monitor, analyze, and evaluate economic, social, and cultural conditions, to provide specific policy inputs through rigorous, evidence-based analysis (evidence- based policy implications), and report to the Prime Minister",""],[1,"64","7","Public Archives Management System Strengthening","Establish and strengthen public archives management systems that meet appropriate technical standards, raise awareness among public officials of the importance of managing public archives, and reinforce archival management structures across ministries, institutions, and subnational administrations.",""]],"124":[[1,"66","8","National Sovereignty and Political Stability Protection","Safeguarding the independence, national sovereignty, and territorial integrity from external interference in the internal affairs of Cambodia, as well as preventing and resolutely opposing any attempt to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia or any incitement to cause political instability or social unrests.",""],[1,"67","9","National Sovereignty and Territorial Integrity Safeguarding","Continue safeguarding peace, sovereignty, independence, and territorial integrity, and oppose interference in internal affairs in any form",""],[1,"67","12","Armed Forces Chain of Command Strengthening","Strengthen the chain of command within the armed forces, particularly within the ranks of the military at all levels, to ensure the effectiveness of management",""],[1,"67","13","Frontline Logistics and Troop Welfare Support","Provide essential technical equipment and improve troop welfare, especially by increasing the efficiency of supply and financial logistics management for standing units on frontline readiness lines and for the defense of islands",""],[1,"67","14","Armed Forces Development and Peacekeeping Cooperation","Strengthen and expand international cooperation to develop the armed forces in all areas, and continue participation in United Nations peacekeeping missions",""],[1,"67","15","Defense Industry Development","Continue developing the defense industry, an essential driver of military modernization, to ensure sustainable development, autonomy, progress, and reduced reliance on costly foreign procurement.",""],[1,"67","17","National Security and Sovereignty Safeguarding Measures","Continue safeguarding peace, independence, national sovereignty, territorial integrity, and national security through necessary measures, and continue maintaining security, public",""],[1,"69","13","Independent Rule-Based Foreign Policy Implementation","The strategic objectives are to continue to strengthen the implementation of independent, rule-based foreign policy in national defense and in promoting the core national interests; and building good friendships and cooperation with all countries in the world and international organizations; as well as actively participating in the cause of peace, stability, security and prosperity in the region and the globe, in accordance with the approach of \"keeping the old and establishing the new\".",""],[1,"70","2","Independent Foreign Policy Implementation","Continuing to implement an independent foreign policy, based on international laws and strict respect for sovereignty, territorial integrity, and independence of member states in accordance with the United Nations Charter and universally recognized principles",""],[1,"70","3","Non-Interference and Sovereignty Protection Policy","Continuing to adhere to the principle of not supporting the threats or use of the force in international relations, invasion against an independent state, separatism, seizure of territory from a sovereign state and interference in the internal affairs of other countries, as well as continuing to take a firm stand against the presence of a foreign military base in the Cambodian territory",""],[1,"70","5","Foreign Policy Implementation to Uphold National Interests","Continuing to uphold the core national interests in the implementation of foreign policy",""],[1,"70","6","Regional and Strategic Partnership Strengthening","Promoting good relations with neighboring countries to achieve the vision of transforming the border into an area of peace, stability, and prosperity, while continuing to strengthen and expand relations with strategic partners within the region and beyond",""],[1,"70","7","ASEAN Participation and Regional Integration Support","Continuing to strengthen Cambodia's role in ASEAN through active and constructive participation in the work of maintaining internal ASEAN unity and regional integration in accordance with the ASEAN Charter, especially the decision-making based on dialogues and consensus principle without interfering in the internal affairs of member state countries",""],[1,"70","8","Multilateral Engagement and Peacekeeping Participation","Continuing to strengthen multilateralism through active participation in regional and international forums; contributing to the UN peacekeeping operations; participating in maintaining stability and peace by promoting dialogues and peaceful settlements of disputes; and promoting free, open, rule-based, and multilateral trade",""],[1,"70","9","Multidimensional and Multifaceted Foreign Policy Implementation","Continuing the implementation of multidimensional and multifaceted foreign policy, aimed at enhancing defense efficiency and promoting national interests by actively participating in relevant sectors creating synergy to leverage negotiation power; and aims to respond in a timely manner to expand strategic flexible space in international relations",""],[1,"70","10","International Confidence and Country Promotion Initiative","Continuing to strengthen international confidence and shape perceptions towards Cambodia with regard to the real and actual situations of Cambodia, to improve partnerships, prestige and global promotion of Cambodia, aimed at increasing attractiveness and promoting economic relations, investment, and tourism",""],[1,"70","11","Institutional Reform and Human Resources Training in Foreign Affairs","Continuing to deepen institutional reforms and to provide the trainings of human resources in foreign affairs to achieve high capacity, sufficient skills, and competencies to protect the core interests of the nation.",""]],"125":[[1,"66","10","Border Development Strategy Implementation","continuing to develop and promote the implementation of the border development strategy as borders for peace, friendships, cooperation and development",""],[1,"67","4","Nationality and Immigration Law Implementation Strengthening","Continuing to strengthen the implementation of the Nationality Law and Immigration Law; continuing to make a push for the development of legal frameworks and mechanisms to ensure that \"one person possesses one identity\" and \"all people are identified\"; the entry-exit Cambodia control; management of stay and employments of foreigners; and the modernization of the immigration data management system to prevent illegal border crossings, illegal stay and illegal businesses by foreigners.",""],[1,"67","4","Entry-Exit Control and Foreigners Management System","the entry-exit Cambodia control; management of stay and employments of foreigners; and the modernization of the immigration data management system to prevent illegal border crossings, illegal stay and illegal businesses by foreigners.",""],[1,"67","6","National Population Data Management Center","by establishing a national center for population data management; introducing the use of individual identification numbers; and promoting the implementation of the Law on Registration, Registration Statistics and Identification, and relevant legal instruments.",""],[1,"67","10","Border Area Development Strategy","continue preparing and implementing the Border Area Development Strategy to make border regions zones of peace, friendship, cooperation, and development.",""],[1,"68","4","Border Gate Management and Immigration Services Strengthening","Strengthen the border gate management, management of foreign migrants, and the provision of immigration services, and deepen national and international friendship and cooperation",""],[1,"68","8","Border Area Development Strategy","continue preparing and implementing the Border Area Development Strategy to make border regions zones of peace, friendship, cooperation, and development",""],[1,"68","9","Border Demarcation and Border Infrastructure Programme","Continue negotiations, surveying and demarcation, and installation of land boundary markers, the delimitation of maritime boundaries and production of border maps, the conservation and maintenance of boundary markers and their precincts, and the construction of the border belt road.",""]],"126":[[1,"84","8","Moral, Virtue, and Ethics Education Cooperation","Strengthening and increasing cooperation in education on morality, virtues, and ethics for students and youth, both inside and outside the education system.",""],[1,"84","9","Moral and Civic Education Curriculum Integration","Formulating a roadmap to nurture behaviors with morality, virtues and ethics, and respect for laws and discipline, and incorporating education on Buddhism and Khmer's arts and culture, both tangible and intangible, into school curricula at all levels, and disseminating and mainstreaming these endeavors to all ministries-institutions, both at national and sub- national levels.",""],[1,"85","11","Lifelong Learning and Reading Promotion Initiative","Foster a culture of learning and lifelong education, particularly among Cambodian youth, by promoting reading and writing through National Culture Day, the Cambodia book fair, remembrance-night events, cultural and literary writing competitions, continued implementation of the \"Culture for education, education for culture\" movement, collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions to translate emerging foreign technical terms in the arts into Khmer, advancement of traditional Khmer knowledge and customs, and organization of supportive programs and events.",""],[1,"86","2","Social Ethics and Religious Values Outreach Programme","Promote social ethics by expanding education and outreach on the benefits of social morality and religious values, especially for youth, issuing standard guidelines for conducting religious ceremonies consistent with Khmer customs, organizing workshops on the correct use of monastic terminology for media and communications entities, producing short educational videos on religious topics, disseminating programs on the role of Buddhism in combating illicit drugs and in fostering social cohesion, and conducting training on the roles, responsibilities, and codes of ethics for Khmer achars, as well as training for monastic officials, achars, and temple Achar Committees, with emphasis on Sangha governance and Buddhist status",""],[1,"86","6","Social Norms and Civic Responsibility Promotion Initiative","Strengthen compliance with the law and address harmful social norms to preserve Khmer national identity and reinforce civic responsibility in an ethical, equitable, and inclusive society in which women are central, focusing on: (1) valuing women's roles, family values, parenthood, positive male role models, and a culture of non-violence, (2) promoting intergenerational relations and well-being in daily life, and (3) educating children on ethics, virtues, and civility",""],[1,"86","7","Social Morality and Family Values Coordination and Public Outreach","Lead, coordinate, and accelerate implementation by the National Committee for the Promotion of Social Morality, Women's Values, and Khmer Families through standard operating procedures that ensure timely interventions and responses, alongside expanded public education and outreach via traditional and modern channels.",""]],"127":[[1,"85","13","Law on Religion Drafting","Promote the state religion by drafting the Law on Religion, establishing the Khmer Tripitaka Commission, formulating a policy on the protection of Buddhism, developing joint procedures on social protection in the religious sector, issuing guidelines on the",""],[1,"85","13","Khmer Tripitaka Commission Establishment","Promote the state religion by drafting the Law on Religion, establishing the Khmer Tripitaka Commission, formulating a policy on the protection of Buddhism, developing joint procedures on social protection in the religious sector, issuing guidelines on the",""],[1,"85","13","Buddhism Protection Policy","Promote the state religion by drafting the Law on Religion, establishing the Khmer Tripitaka Commission, formulating a policy on the protection of Buddhism, developing joint procedures on social protection in the religious sector, issuing guidelines on the",""],[1,"86","1","Buddhist Pagoda Development and Religious Tourism Initiative","preparing a development plan for Buddhist pagodas, issuing architectural design standards for religious constructions, establishing mechanisms for outstanding pagoda awards, and developing selected pagodas as religious tourism sites",""],[1,"86","3","National Religious Harmony Policy and Interfaith Dialogue Initiative","Maintain religious harmony through cooperation with leaders of all faiths in fulfilling duties in the sector of cults and religion, concluding memoranda of understanding and agreements with development partners in this sector, encouraging all religions to participate in social and humanitarian activities, preventing the commercialization of religion and other improper acts that affect public order, resolving administrative matters across religious domains, developing policies on the protection of religious marriages and religious schools, formulating a national policy on religious harmony in Cambodia, organizing interfaith dialogue forums, and compiling documentation on beliefs, religions, traditions, and customs of indigenous minority groups.",""]],"128":[[1,"89","10","Tourism Workforce Training Alignment Programme","Promote economic growth and decent work in tourism through training aligned with the Cambodia National Qualifications Framework and the ASEAN Tourism Professional Competency Standards",""],[1,"89","12","Visitor Travel Coordination and Infrastructure Improvement","improving inter-agency management and coordination of visitor travel, including hard and soft infrastructure",""],[1,"89","12","Tourism Institutional Development","developing institutions",""],[1,"89","12","Tourism Digital Transformation","advancing digital transformation",""],[1,"89","12","Tourism Workforce Development","building the tourism workforce",""]],"129":[[1,"90","1","Cultural Innovation and Creative Development Support","Enhance creativity and innovation in cultural development by leveraging new technologies and initiatives, providing technical support, incentives, and facilitation, and strengthening research and original creation in cultural and artistic works",""],[1,"90","2","Cultural Sector Productivity and Entrepreneurship Promotion","Increase productivity and entrepreneurship in the cultural sector, and continue to promote new cultural products and services, especially inspection of cultural objects for import and export, film and video services, copyright and related-rights services, and book and reading services",""],[1,"90","3","Arts and Culture Human Capital Strengthening Programme","Continue strengthening the quality and quantity of human capital in arts and culture to build knowledge, professional skills, and jobs in the cultural sector, contributing to socio- economic development and poverty reduction through formal and non-formal education and training, investment, and harnessing Cambodia's demographic dividend, while expanding youth participation, especially of women, as producers and consumers of cultural products and services",""],[1,"90","4","Cultural Artefacts Production Promotion","Promote the production of cultural artefacts, particularly high-quality works rooted in ancestral Khmer artistic skills",""],[1,"90","5","Copyright and Related-Rights Management System Strengthening","Further strengthen copyright and related-rights management systems to keep pace with technological and digital developments, in order to deter and combat piracy more effectively",""],[1,"90","6","Cultural and Artistic Events and Programs","Organize major cultural and artistic events and programs to support and energize private actors and civil society to play a more dynamic role in the cultural and creative industries",""],[1,"90","8","Cultural and Creative Industries Resource Mobilization Mechanism","Strengthen and expand systems and mechanisms to ensure strategic interlinkages, including national and international cooperation, to mobilize financial and technical resources in support of cultural and creative industry development.",""]],"130":[[1,"92","2","National Wastewater Systems Master Planning","preparing a national master plan and development plans for wastewater systems nationwide;",""]],"131":[[1,"95","3","Cambodia e-Invoicing System","Ministry of Economy and Finance shall establish a Cambodia e-Invoicing System to enable the electronic transmission, receipt, and validation of invoices between buyers and sellers, reducing paper-based documentation and advancing trade facilitation for digital commerce.","Ministry of Economy and Finance"],[1,"95","4","Business, Trade, and Investment Facilitation Reform","The strategic objectives are to improve the favorable climate for businesses, trade, and investment through facilitation and simplification of various procedures, digitalization of public service deliveries and administration, strengthening institutional capacity, and enhancing the efficiency of inter-ministerial coordination.",""],[1,"95","4","Sector-Specific Strategic Planning Requirement","Ministries-institutions are required to prepare sector- specific strategic plans to implement the priority programs and actions identified in the Royal Government's NSDP for the 7th Legislature, with the aim of contributing to the achievement of the Royal Government's key policy priorities, as follows:",""],[1,"95","5","Commercial and Trade Law Reform","Continuing to introduce and amend laws and regulations, such as law on commercial regulation and commercial registration, law on commercial enterprises, bankruptcy law; and finalizing trade secrets and confidential information law to ensure the sound management of intellectual property and prevent the leakage of commercial information.",""],[1,"95","8","Strengthening Governance and Private Sector Participation in ASEAN Business Forums","Continuing to strengthen governance and to expand the roles of private sector in the business forums under ASEAN frameworks, and those of ASEAN with partners and RCEP, in order to promote trade and attract foreign investment and tourism.",""],[1,"95","9","Cross-Border Paperless Trade Facilitation Framework Implementation","Accelerating the enactment by the legislature of the Framework Agreement on Cross Border Paperless Trade Facilitation and increasing effective cooperation in implementation, aimed at promoting exports and imports by using digital system.",""],[1,"95","10","Trade Dispute Resolution Reform","Promoting trade dispute resolutions - either in court or out of court - effectively, skillfully, and competently through introducing regulations and commercial courts mechanisms.",""],[1,"95","11","Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism for Business and Investment Climate Improvement","Establishing monitoring and evaluation mechanisms; and improving business and investment climate, based on the assessment of the ease of doing business and investment in Cambodia.",""],[1,"95","11","Business and Investment Climate Improvement Reform","Establishing monitoring and evaluation mechanisms; and improving business and investment climate, based on the assessment of the ease of doing business and investment in Cambodia.",""],[1,"96","1","Single-Window Investment Facilitation Mechanism","Continue strengthening the single-window mechanism and related support mechanisms, and streamline required procedures to facilitate investment and business",""],[1,"96","2","RCEP Market Access and Investment Facilitation Implementation","Continue implementing market-access commitments, streamlining procedures for the review and approval of investment projects, ensuring investment protection, and notifying new state measures related to investment and business, while monitoring and evaluating the State's compliance with these obligations as a member of RCEP",""],[1,"96","3","Information Technology Platform Upgrade and Automation","Upgrade and automate information-technology platforms, especially the eligible investment project registration system, to be more robust, up to date, and fully capable, and promote adoption of these platforms",""],[1,"96","4","Investor and Business Service Delivery Improvement","Further improve the quality and responsiveness of public service delivery to investors and businesses through both in-person and online channels",""],[1,"96","5","Country and Sector Investment Desks","Continue operating country and sector investment desks on a broad and highly effective basis",""],[1,"96","6","Participation in ASEAN Investment Agreement Amendment Work","Participate in work related to the Fifth Protocol to Amend the ASEAN Comprehensive Investment Agreement, with a focus on further sectoral liberalization",""],[1,"96","7","Review and Refinement of Investment-Related Laws and Regulations","Continue reviewing and refining existing investment-related laws and normative legal documents",""],[1,"96","8","Investment Climate Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Contribute to establishing a mechanism to monitor and evaluate improvements in the investment climate, with priority on tracking progress of measures announced at the 19th Government-Private Sector Forum and other measures raised in related forums and dialogues coordinated by the CIB.",""],[1,"96","9","Business and Investment Enabling Environment Enhancement","Ministry of Commerce shall continue to enhance an enabling environment for business and investment through trade facilitation, digital transformation to deliver efficient commercial services, strengthened market governance and protection of producers and consumers, promotion of local marketplaces for traders, entrepreneurs, and smallholder farmers, and development of value and supply chains linking growers, producers, processors, aggregators, and exporters.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"101","1","Electronic Business Registration and Licensing System","Ministry of Commerce shall contribute to labor market development through the registration and establishment of new companies and enterprises, and the issuance of business licenses and permits via an electronic system using automation, in order to provide convenience and speed for investors, entrepreneurs, and start-ups.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"101","1","Business Associations and Chambers of Commerce Promotion","This includes promoting the establishment of business associations, federations, and chambers of commerce to ensure the smooth and dynamic operation of businesses.",""],[1,"101","8","Public Governance and Enterprise Enabling Environment Reform","Continuing to develop and implement policies, strategies, and regulations; ensuring the improvements of public governance; promoting an enabling environment for micro, small, and medium enterprises, and startups; and promoting effective public service deliveries to all actors in the entrepreneurial ecosystem.",""],[1,"102","7","Electronic Enterprise Permit and Business Service Delivery System","Strengthen mechanisms for issuing enterprise operating permits and other public services that support business operations through electronic systems, under the strategy for developing e-services for business 2025-2028",""]],"132":[[1,"105","6","Financial Stability Management and Inspection Strengthening","Continuing to ensure financial stability by strengthening the management and inspection mechanisms of banking and non-banking financial sectors;",""],[1,"105","6","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Efforts","sustaining the efforts to combat money laundering and terrorism financing;",""],[1,"105","6","Shadow Banking Reduction Measures","reducing shadow banks;",""],[1,"106","8","Financial Stability Monitoring Capacity Strengthening","Maintain financial stability by strengthening governance, skills, and capacity of the financial stability monitoring team, enhancing early warning systems, and improving the collection and analysis of essential data and information",""],[1,"106","9","Crisis Preparedness and Response Strengthening","Strengthen preparedness and crisis response by enhancing supervisory oversight, establishing a crisis management cooperation framework and procedures, and developing a national contingency plan",""],[1,"106","10","Deposit Insurance Scheme Feasibility Assessment","Assess the feasibility of establishing a deposit insurance scheme to bolster confidence in Cambodia's banking system",""],[1,"106","11","Implementation of Basel Core Principles for Banking Supervision","Implement the Basel core principles for effective banking supervision and relevant global standards to enhance supervisory effectiveness and risk management",""],[1,"106","12","Capital Adequacy and Risk-Based Banking Supervision Reform","Strengthen regulations on capital adequacy and prompt corrective action, and improve supervisory effectiveness to fully implement risk-based and forward-looking supervision",""],[1,"106","16","Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism Strengthening","Strengthen anti-money laundering and countering the financing of terrorism by enhancing the Financial Intelligence Unit's risk assessments and compliance supervision.",""],[1,"107","11","Shadow Banking Regulatory Reform","Prepare and issue normative legal documents to reduce and ultimately eliminate shadow banking activities, in order to strengthen Cambodia's financial stability.",""],[1,"107","15","Financial Stability and AML/CFT Strengthening Measures","Continue to help ensure financial system stability by preparing a Financial Stability Law, establishing an early warning system for the non-bank financial sector, and further promoting compliance and effectiveness in combating money laundering and terrorist financing",""]],"133":[[1,"99","9","Non-Bank Financial Sector Data Sharing and Open Data Framework","Non-Bank Financial Services Authority shall conduct studies and promote data openness to catalyze fintech development and innovation for enterprises and start-ups engaged in fintech-related activities, by identifying priority actions, programs, and projects, including: (1) researching and contributing to the formulation of a framework for data sharing and open data in the non-bank financial sector, and (2) organizing meetings and/or workshops to collect inputs for that framework.",""],[1,"107","1","Cybersecurity and Data Governance Enhancement for the Financial Sector","Enhance cybersecurity and data governance to safeguard stability and support growth of the banking and financial sector",""]],"134":[[1,"106","1","Securities Market Development and Regulatory Expansion","Continuing to develop securities market through the promotion and encouragement of domestic companies who are qualified to issue securities to the public, establishing incentive mechanisms to institutional investors, establishing futures exchange market operators, and establishing management mechanisms for digital asset trading.",""],[1,"106","2","Derivatives Market Development Framework","Promoting the development of the derivatives market, which is a platform to promote financial risk management and future interest rate setting mechanisms through the establishment of legal frameworks and supportive infrastructure, and the attraction of liquidity providers.",""],[1,"108","8","Legal and Regulatory Framework Development","Continue to develop the relevant legal and regulatory framework",""],[1,"108","9","Securities Sector Supervisory and Enforcement Framework Strengthening","Continue to strengthen the supervisory and enforcement framework, particularly regulations addressing offenses and market misconduct in the securities sector",""],[1,"108","10","Market Infrastructure Upgrade","Continue to upgrade market infrastructure, including trading, clearing, and settlement systems",""],[1,"108","11","Bond Market Development and Foreign Investor Participation","Continue to deepen market participation and infrastructure by encouraging foreign bond investors and promoting the development of the corporate bond market and the government securities market.",""],[1,"108","13","Policy and Regulatory Development and Refinement","Continue to develop and refine relevant policies and regulations",""]],"135":[[1,"106","4","Real Estate Sector Legal and Data Management Reform","Continuing to strengthen the real estate development sector, especially the housing development business and real estate service business, pawn sector and transfers of title for security purpose, through the formulation and amendments of legal frameworks, the development of the real estate data management system in Cambodia, and the strengthening of the capacity of technical officers and market participants.",""],[1,"106","5","Trust Sector Development and Market Expansion","Continuing to develop the trust sector by promoting and strengthening law enforcement, promoting public awareness; developing new markets, trust operators and trust products; and exploring the possibility to set up mechanisms for trust management and operations by using technological innovations.",""],[1,"108","14","Strengthen Regulatory Supervision and Compliance of Real Estate Developers","Continue to strengthen institutional capacity, particularly regulatory functions such as ongoing supervision and enhanced compliance by real estate developers",""],[1,"108","15","Comprehensive Real Estate and Pawn Business Data Systems","Modernize and establish comprehensive data systems, notably by developing technology platforms for submitting reports and documentation from real estate developers, real estate service providers, and licensed pawn and collateral businesses",""],[1,"108","16","Real Estate and Pawn Business Training and Public Outreach","Enhance training and public outreach, especially on processes related to purchasing, selling, or leasing real estate and on licensed pawn and collateral businesses, and strengthen inter- agency cooperation.",""]],"136":[[1,"108","18","Accounting Curriculum Strengthening and Competency Integration Programme","Build capacity and promote outreach, with a focus on strengthening technical accounting curricula and cooperation to integrate accounting competency programs",""],[1,"108","19","Financial Reporting Management System","Implement a financial reporting management system",""],[1,"108","20","Adoption of Cambodian Financial Reporting Standards","Promote adoption of Cambodian International Financial Reporting Standards (CIFRS) and CIFRS for SMEs",""],[1,"108","21","Standardized Chart of Accounts and Financial Statement Templates","Develop a standardized chart of accounts and financial statement templates for small and medium enterprises and not-for-profit organizations.",""],[1,"108","23","Regulatory Authority Capacity-Building and Information System Development","Continue to build institutional capacity by issuing and implementing guidelines on procedures and standardized administrative document templates for the preparation and functioning of the Regulatory Authority, and by establishing an information system for personnel and records management",""],[1,"108","24","Sector Supervision, Risk Management, and Compliance Strengthening","Continue to strengthen institutional functions by promulgating regulations for supervision and risk management of the sector, developing systems for operational oversight of regulated activities and entities, and enhancing legal compliance and enforcement",""],[1,"108","25","Training, Public Education, and Outreach Strengthening","Promote training, public education, and outreach, and strengthen collaboration and coordination.",""],[1,"108","25","Collaboration and Coordination Strengthening","Promote training, public education, and outreach, and strengthen collaboration and coordination.",""]],"137":[[1,"110","14","Gender and Health Public Awareness and Women's Health Access Initiative","Promote public awareness on gender and health, and strengthen the agency of women and girls to access quality health services",""],[1,"110","15","Capacity Building for Gender and Health Outreach Officials","Build the capacity of officials at national and subnational levels responsible for broad- based education and outreach on gender and health",""]],"138":[[1,"111","7","Gender Mainstreaming in Climate Policy and Capacity Support","Continue mainstreaming gender in the formulation and implementation of climate change policies, programs, and strategic plans, and strengthen technical capacity and leadership support among relevant officials for implementing the Gender and Climate Change Strategy, building climate adaptation capacity, advancing green development, and reducing disaster risk",""],[1,"111","8","Women and Vulnerable Girls Inclusion in Climate and Social Protection Programs","Support and catalyze initiatives that enhance the role of women and address the needs of vulnerable women and girls within climate change programs, green development, disaster risk reduction, and the social protection framework",""],[1,"111","9","Gendered Climate Change Information Management and Dissemination System","Establish programs and systems to manage and disseminate information on the gendered impacts of climate change.",""]],"139":[[1,"114","6","State Land Protection and Land Resource Management","Strengthen state land protection through continued registration of state land and enhanced management of forest land, flooded forests, mangrove forests, fisheries management areas, and concession land; promote management and stewardship of agricultural land resources to prevent soil quality decline, erosion and sediment run-off, nutrient depletion, and water-quality degradation, and to restore degraded slopes and terrain, ecosystem services, soil productivity and health, and soil carbon stocks",""],[1,"114","7","Natural Resource Crime Investigation and Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen investigation and enforcement against natural resource crimes by enhancing rapid information-sharing networks on natural resource offenses, improving perpetrator identification, crime tracing, research and investigation, enabling early warning and timely action, and ensuring rigorous law enforcement",""]],"140":[[1,"114","8","Natural Resource Demand Management and Conservation Measures","Address demand for natural resource use through studies of resource demand and utilization, establishment of response mechanisms aligned with demand and market conditions, strengthened research, assessment and sustainable conservation of natural resources, promotion of management and development of agricultural natural resources, and reduced consumption through a shift to agroforestry systems",""]],"141":[[1,"115","8","Petroleum Resource Assessment and Geoscience Mapping","Study and assess petroleum resources and develop a petroleum geoscience map.",""]],"142":[[1,"116","11","Community-Based Tourism Development and Skills Programme","Promote community participation in tourism development, build entrepreneurship and tourism vocational skills for local residents so they can capture economic benefits from tourism, equip citizens and youth with clear competencies, and improve the quality of tour guide training",""],[1,"116","12","Cultural Heritage Tourism Management and Promotion","Conserve and promote culture linked to tourism by strengthening visitor flow management at cultural heritage sites and the management of cultural heritage assets, preparing tourism development plans for cultural heritage areas, strengthening enforcement of laws and normative legal documents, raising tourist awareness of cultural heritage, and stimulating domestic tourism connected to cultural tourism",""],[1,"116","13","Tourism Impact Management and Compliance Enforcement","Manage negative impacts from tourism by strengthening public education and awareness of laws and normative legal documents among tourism operators and visitors, and by reinforcing systems for responsible law enforcement and inspection of tourism activities",""],[1,"117","1","Green Tourism Development Programme","Promote development of green tourism products by advancing ecotourism and community-based tourism, energizing the \"Clean City, Clean Resort, Good Service, Good Hospitality\" movement, supporting tree-planting campaigns and the creation of tourism parks, implementing green standards in the tourism industry in line with Cambodian and ASEAN green standards, and developing green tourism destinations",""],[1,"117","2","Cambodia as a Clean and Green Destination Campaign","Advance the \"Cambodia as a Clean and Green Destination\" campaign by scaling up education and awareness on environmental sustainability, cleanliness, greenery, order, and good hygiene, expanding campaigns to reduce plastic waste and maintain clean public toilets, and mainstreaming green practices and green technologies across the tourism industry.",""]],"143":[[1,"117","7","Production Cost Reduction Support for Domestic Input Firms","Reducing production costs through raising awareness on usage of inputs and quality control, providing low-interest credits, and providing incentives to firms producing domestic inputs.",""],[1,"117","9","Agro-Industrial Modernization and Processing Investment Support","Promoting the processing of agricultural products through the improvements and modernization of agro-industry; encouraging the investment in processed agricultural products; undertaking a study and creating \"Agro-Industrial Parks in Cambodia\" for establishing the clusters of processing enterprises; fostering a stable supply of agricultural products; and continuing concessional financing for investment.",""],[1,"117","10","Domestic Market Connectivity and Export Promotion Measures","Continuing to enhance domestic market connectivity and export promotion by promoting support for domestic products through their direct use among public institutions and the public, strengthening contract farming mechanisms, establishing wholesale and distribution markets for domestic agricultural products, strengthening infrastructure, and maximizing benefits from free trade agreements.",""],[1,"118","12","Cambodian Product Market Promotion Strategy","Formulate a strategy to promote uptake of Cambodian products in domestic and international markets through organizing domestic and overseas trade fairs, business matchmaking and networking events, and negotiations of trade agreements to open new markets; upgrade product quality and supply for Cambodian goods in both markets; and scale up implementation of the One Village One Product movement by encouraging production aligned with geographic conditions and market demand, diversifying high-quality products, and leveraging innovation and modern technologies to achieve higher price realization",""],[1,"119","8","Agriculture and Agro-industry Investment Promotion and Investor Outreach Events","Organize promotion and investor outreach events to catalyze and attract investment in agriculture and agro-industry in Cambodia",""],[1,"119","9","Agro-Industrial Parks and Export-Oriented Agricultural Processing Zones","Collaborate with relevant ministries and institutions to establish agro-industrial parks in Cambodia, and encourage private sector development of export-oriented agricultural processing zones.","relevant ministries and institutions"],[1,"120","3","Technical Training and Producer Experience-Sharing Programme","Intensify relevant technical training for producers and promote experience-sharing among communities and producers to enhance market competitiveness and ensure the sustainability of production and supply chains",""]],"144":[[1,"119","14","Policy Dialogue, Research, and Knowledge Management Strengthening","Promote policy dialogue, research, and knowledge management, including the efficient utilization of digital systems and various technologies.",""]],"145":[[1,"120","8","Urban Infrastructure Master Planning and Service Upgrading","Developing infrastructure development master plans for cities and main urban areas to ensure resilience and beauty, promoting public urban transport services; enhancing waste management, handling and processing; creating pedestrian sidewalks and parking spaces; installing traffic signs, CCTV and traffic lights; expanding electricity networks, urban lighting, clean water networks, flood drainage systems, waste water filtration and treatment systems, and urban firefighting system; preserving buildings of historical value; proposing the building of natural and cultural public parks in capital city, provinces or region, which do not incur high operational costs or high costs of maintenance.",""],[1,"120","9","Private Sector Incentive Mechanism for Urban Management","considering the establishment of incentive mechanism for encouraging private sector's participations in urban management, especially the urban management related to the development of smart, green or livable cities.",""],[1,"122","1","Coastal Recreation and Beach Development Programme","competitive programs for beautiful sandy beaches and recreational canals; encourage the development of public and/or tourism roads along coastal strips; continue executing projects to convert mud beaches into public recreational sandy beaches; further develop detailed plans and enhancement strategies for additional public recreational sandy beaches; and monitor and inspect Cambodia's coastal areas to reinforce compliance with the directive on coastal development in the Kingdom of Cambodia, as well as prevailing laws and legal standards",""]],"146":[[1,"125","3","Officials' Digital Capacity Building and Digital Leadership Promotion","Continuing to strengthen officials' digital capacity through regular trainings and promotion of digital leadership for the management and officials, and assessment of the establishment of a digital transformation unit in ministries-institutions.",""],[1,"125","4","Education Curriculum Modernization and Digital Skills Training","Building human capital with digital skills through modernizing and finetuning education curricula and digital training programs, and mobilizing and attracting the digital talents from abroad.",""],[1,"125","4","Digital Talent Attraction from Abroad Initiative","Building human capital with digital skills through modernizing and finetuning education curricula and digital training programs, and mobilizing and attracting the digital talents from abroad.",""],[1,"125","5","Digital Literacy Promotion and Digital Skills Training","Continuing to promote digital literacy among citizens, including the inclusion of basic digital skills in education curricula and provision of training programs on digital skills in various sectors.",""],[1,"125","8","Digital Transformation Units and Capacity-Building Training","Establish digital transformation units and deliver training for leaders, civil servants, and technical officers across ministries, institutions, and subnational administrations to develop competent digital technology users",""],[1,"125","13","Digital Skills Training and Upskilling Programme","Train students in digital skills, promote study in digital disciplines, and upskill certified digital professionals working in public institutions, civil society organizations, and the private sector",""],[1,"125","14","Digital Literacy and Skills Development Initiative","Raise digital literacy among students and the general public through the \"Techo Talent\" scholarship program, digital skills development initiatives, and community digital technology centers",""],[1,"125","15","Digital Technology Training Roadmaps for Higher Education","Develop roadmaps for digital technology training and for digital management systems at higher education institutions",""],[1,"125","15","Digital Management Systems Roadmap for Higher Education Institutions","Develop roadmaps for digital technology training and for digital management systems at higher education institutions",""],[1,"125","16","Digital Professionals Association","Establish a Cambodia digital community platform to convene digital experts and collaborate with relevant ministries and institutions to promote digital technologies to communities and the public, and establish a Digital Professionals Association to pool human resources and build professional capacity in the digital sector.",""],[1,"126","1","Technology and Digital Skills Training for Students","Promote training of students in technology and digital technology disciplines",""],[1,"126","2","Digital Economy and Technology Colleges","Develop and establish colleges of digital economy and technology aligned with trends in the digital economy and digital society",""],[1,"126","3","Centers of Excellence and Research Strengthening in Public Higher Education","Promote research and innovation by enabling public higher education institutions to establish centers of excellence and by strengthening research based on their comparative advantages and specializations",""],[1,"126","4","Entrepreneurship and Business Centers","Establish entrepreneurship and business centers to train young entrepreneurs, encourage start-up creation and self-employment, and build the capacity of young researchers",""],[1,"126","5","University Artificial Intelligence Centers","Establish artificial intelligence centers at universities.",""],[1,"126","8","Digital Human Capital Development Programme","Build digital human capital by strengthening information technology capacity for management and training, developing training programs, conducting awareness campaigns and education on foundational digital literacy, and promoting the use of digital public services",""],[1,"126","9","Digital Infrastructure and Capacity Development Programme","Develop infrastructure and information technology and digital capacities, including delivering digital literacy and essential digital skills training for leaders, civil servants, and staff across ministries, institutions, and subnational administrations.",""],[1,"127","8","Digital Innovation Capacity Strengthening Programme","Strengthening digital innovation capacity through the development of human resources and talents in science, technology, and innovation, as well as the improvements of R&D, and innovation in education and training institutions.",""]],"147":[[1,"141","19","Compliance Strengthening for Quality Control, Product Safety, Consumer Protection, and Food Safety Laws","Strengthening compliance with the implementation of the law on quality control, product safety on goods and services; consumer protection law; and food safety law",""]],"148":[[1,"146","13","Work-Life Balance and Well-Being Policy Drafting","Laws and policies drafting that address and recognize work-life balance, and promote economy that considers well- being and health care",""]]}});